            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-69651",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: Binutils: Denial of Service via crafted ELF binary processing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a vulnerability that leads to an invalid pointer free when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed relocation or symbol data. If dump_relocations returns early due to parsing errors, the internal all_relocations array may remain partially uninitialized. Later, process_got_section_contents() may attempt to free an invalid r_symbol pointer, triggering memory corruption checks in glibc and causing the program to terminate with SIGABRT. No evidence of further memory corruption or code execution was observed; the impact is limited to denial of service. NOTE: this is disputed by third parties because the observed behavior occurred only in pre-release code and did not affect any tagged version."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69651",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-69651\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libsframe1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-69651](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69651)\nGNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a vulnerability that leads to an invalid pointer free when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed relocation or symbol data. If dump_relocations returns early due to parsing errors, the internal all_relocations array may remain partially uninitialized. Later, process_got_section_contents() may attempt to free an invalid r_symbol pointer, triggering memory corruption checks in glibc and causing the program to terminate with SIGABRT. No evidence of further memory corruption or code execution was observed; the impact is limited to denial of service. NOTE: this is disputed by third parties because the observed behavior occurred only in pre-release code and did not affect any tagged version.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-69651**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libsframe1||[CVE-2025-69651](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69651)|\n\nGNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a vulnerability that leads to an invalid pointer free when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed relocation or symbol data. If dump_relocations returns early due to parsing errors, the internal all_relocations array may remain partially uninitialized. Later, process_got_section_contents() may attempt to free an invalid r_symbol pointer, triggering memory corruption checks in glibc and causing the program to terminate with SIGABRT. No evidence of further memory corruption or code execution was observed; the impact is limited to denial of service. NOTE: this is disputed by third parties because the observed behavior occurred only in pre-release code and did not affect any tagged version."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-69652",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: abort in readelf via crafted ELF binary with malformed DWARF abbrev or debug information"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a vulnerability that leads to an abort (SIGABRT) when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed DWARF abbrev or debug information. Due to incomplete state cleanup in process_debug_info(), an invalid debug_info_p state may propagate into DWARF attribute parsing routines. When certain malformed attributes result in an unexpected data length of zero, byte_get_little_endian() triggers a fatal abort. No evidence of memory corruption or code execution was observed; the impact is limited to denial of service."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69652",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-69652\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libsframe1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-69652](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69652)\nGNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a vulnerability that leads to an abort (SIGABRT) when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed DWARF abbrev or debug information. Due to incomplete state cleanup in process_debug_info(), an invalid debug_info_p state may propagate into DWARF attribute parsing routines. When certain malformed attributes result in an unexpected data length of zero, byte_get_little_endian() triggers a fatal abort. No evidence of memory corruption or code execution was observed; the impact is limited to denial of service.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-69652**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libsframe1||[CVE-2025-69652](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-69652)|\n\nGNU Binutils thru 2.46 readelf contains a vulnerability that leads to an abort (SIGABRT) when processing a crafted ELF binary with malformed DWARF abbrev or debug information. Due to incomplete state cleanup in process_debug_info(), an invalid debug_info_p state may propagate into DWARF attribute parsing routines. When certain malformed attributes result in an unexpected data length of zero, byte_get_little_endian() triggers a fatal abort. No evidence of memory corruption or code execution was observed; the impact is limited to denial of service."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2017-13716",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: Memory leak with the C++ symbol demangler routine in libiberty"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The C++ symbol demangler routine in cplus-dem.c in libiberty, as distributed in GNU Binutils 2.29, allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (excessive memory allocation and application crash) via a crafted file, as demonstrated by a call from the Binary File Descriptor (BFD) library (aka libbfd)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2017-13716",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2017-13716\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libsframe1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2017-13716](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2017-13716)\nThe C++ symbol demangler routine in cplus-dem.c in libiberty, as distributed in GNU Binutils 2.29, allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (excessive memory allocation and application crash) via a crafted file, as demonstrated by a call from the Binary File Descriptor (BFD) library (aka libbfd).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2017-13716**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libsframe1||[CVE-2017-13716](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2017-13716)|\n\nThe C++ symbol demangler routine in cplus-dem.c in libiberty, as distributed in GNU Binutils 2.29, allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (excessive memory allocation and application crash) via a crafted file, as demonstrated by a call from the Binary File Descriptor (BFD) library (aka libbfd)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-1152",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: GNU Binutils ld xstrdup.c xstrdup memory leak"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability classified as problematic has been found in GNU Binutils 2.43. Affected is the function xstrdup of the file xstrdup.c of the component ld. The manipulation leads to memory leak. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The complexity of an attack is rather high. The exploitability is told to be difficult. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. It is recommended to apply a patch to fix this issue. The code maintainer explains: \"I'm not going to commit some of the leak fixes I've been working on to the 2.44 branch due to concern that would destabilise ld. All of the reported leaks in this bugzilla have been fixed on binutils master.\""
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-1152",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-1152\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libsframe1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-1152](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-1152)\nA vulnerability classified as problematic has been found in GNU Binutils 2.43. Affected is the function xstrdup of the file xstrdup.c of the component ld. The manipulation leads to memory leak. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The complexity of an attack is rather high. The exploitability is told to be difficult. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. It is recommended to apply a patch to fix this issue. The code maintainer explains: \"I'm not going to commit some of the leak fixes I've been working on to the 2.44 branch due to concern that would destabilise ld. All of the reported leaks in this bugzilla have been fixed on binutils master.\"",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-1152**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libsframe1||[CVE-2025-1152](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-1152)|\n\nA vulnerability classified as problematic has been found in GNU Binutils 2.43. Affected is the function xstrdup of the file xstrdup.c of the component ld. The manipulation leads to memory leak. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The complexity of an attack is rather high. The exploitability is told to be difficult. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. It is recommended to apply a patch to fix this issue. The code maintainer explains: \"I'm not going to commit some of the leak fixes I've been working on to the 2.44 branch due to concern that would destabilise ld. All of the reported leaks in this bugzilla have been fixed on binutils master.\""
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-5278",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "coreutils: Heap Buffer Under-Read in GNU Coreutils sort via Key Specification"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-5278",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-5278\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: coreutils\nFixed Version: 9.4-3ubuntu6.3\nLink: [CVE-2025-5278](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-5278)\nA flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-5278**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|coreutils|9.4-3ubuntu6.3|[CVE-2025-5278](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-5278)|\n\nA flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data."
