              "id": "CVE-2026-92389",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "curl: curl: TFTP direction confusion"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in curl. When handling Trivial File Transfer Protocol (TFTP) transfers, a malicious server can trigger information disclosure by responding to a download request in a way that forces the client into transmit mode. Consequently, the client may unintentionally send leftover sensitive data from prior operations on a reused connection handle to the attacker's server."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
