            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59731",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "FFmpeg: Heap-buffer-overflow write in FFmpeg EXR dwa_uncompress"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When decoding an OpenEXR file that uses DWAA or DWAB compression, the specified raw length of run-length-encoded data is not checked when using it to calculate the output data.\n\nWe read rle_raw_size from the input file at [0], we decompress and decode into the buffer td-\u003erle_raw_data of size rle_raw_size at [1], and then at [2] we will access entries in this buffer up to (td-\u003exsize - 1) * (td-\u003eysize - 1) + rle_raw_size / 2, which may exceed rle_raw_size.\n\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59731",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-59731\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libswscale7\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-59731](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59731)\nWhen decoding an OpenEXR file that uses DWAA or DWAB compression, the specified raw length of run-length-encoded data is not checked when using it to calculate the output data.\n\nWe read rle_raw_size from the input file at [0], we decompress and decode into the buffer td-\u003erle_raw_data of size rle_raw_size at [1], and then at [2] we will access entries in this buffer up to (td-\u003exsize - 1) * (td-\u003eysize - 1) + rle_raw_size / 2, which may exceed rle_raw_size.\n\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-59731**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libswscale7||[CVE-2025-59731](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59731)|\n\nWhen decoding an OpenEXR file that uses DWAA or DWAB compression, the specified raw length of run-length-encoded data is not checked when using it to calculate the output data.\n\nWe read rle_raw_size from the input file at [0], we decompress and decode into the buffer td-\u003erle_raw_data of size rle_raw_size at [1], and then at [2] we will access entries in this buffer up to (td-\u003exsize - 1) * (td-\u003eysize - 1) + rle_raw_size / 2, which may exceed rle_raw_size.\n\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59732",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "FFmpeg: FFmpeg: Heap memory corruption when decoding OpenEXR files with DWAA/DWAB compression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When decoding an OpenEXR file that uses DWAA or DWAB compression, there's an implicit assumption that the height and width are divisible by 8.\n\nIf the height or width of the image is not divisible by 8, the copy loops at [0] and [1] will continue to write until the next multiple of 8.\n\nThe buffer td-\u003euncompressed_data is allocated in decode_block based on the precise height and width of the image, so the \"rounded-up\" multiple of 8 in the copy loop can exceed the buffer bounds, and the write block starting at [2] can corrupt following heap memory.\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59732",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-59732\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libswscale7\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-59732](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59732)\nWhen decoding an OpenEXR file that uses DWAA or DWAB compression, there's an implicit assumption that the height and width are divisible by 8.\n\nIf the height or width of the image is not divisible by 8, the copy loops at [0] and [1] will continue to write until the next multiple of 8.\n\nThe buffer td-\u003euncompressed_data is allocated in decode_block based on the precise height and width of the image, so the \"rounded-up\" multiple of 8 in the copy loop can exceed the buffer bounds, and the write block starting at [2] can corrupt following heap memory.\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-59732**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libswscale7||[CVE-2025-59732](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59732)|\n\nWhen decoding an OpenEXR file that uses DWAA or DWAB compression, there's an implicit assumption that the height and width are divisible by 8.\n\nIf the height or width of the image is not divisible by 8, the copy loops at [0] and [1] will continue to write until the next multiple of 8.\n\nThe buffer td-\u003euncompressed_data is allocated in decode_block based on the precise height and width of the image, so the \"rounded-up\" multiple of 8 in the copy loop can exceed the buffer bounds, and the write block starting at [2] can corrupt following heap memory.\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59733",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "FFmpeg: FFmpeg: Buffer overflow in OpenEXR DWAA/DWAB decoding"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When decoding an OpenEXR file that uses DWAA or DWAB compression, there's an implicit assumption that all image channels have the same pixel type (and size), and that if there are four channels, the first four are \"B\", \"G\", \"R\" and \"A\". The channel parsing code can be found in decode_header. The buffer td-\u003euncompressed_data is allocated in decode_block based on the xsize, ysize and computed current_channel_offset.\n\nThe function dwa_uncompress then assumes at [5] that if there are 4 channels, these are \"B\", \"G\", \"R\" and \"A\", and in the calculations at [6] and [7] that all channels are of the same type, which matches the type of the main color channels.\n\nIf we set the main color channels to a 4-byte type and add duplicate or unknown channels of the 2-byte EXR_HALF type, then the addition at [7] will increment the pointer by 4-bytes * xsize * nb_channels, which will exceed the allocated buffer.\n\n\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59733",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-59733\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libswscale7\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-59733](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59733)\nWhen decoding an OpenEXR file that uses DWAA or DWAB compression, there's an implicit assumption that all image channels have the same pixel type (and size), and that if there are four channels, the first four are \"B\", \"G\", \"R\" and \"A\". The channel parsing code can be found in decode_header. The buffer td-\u003euncompressed_data is allocated in decode_block based on the xsize, ysize and computed current_channel_offset.\n\nThe function dwa_uncompress then assumes at [5] that if there are 4 channels, these are \"B\", \"G\", \"R\" and \"A\", and in the calculations at [6] and [7] that all channels are of the same type, which matches the type of the main color channels.\n\nIf we set the main color channels to a 4-byte type and add duplicate or unknown channels of the 2-byte EXR_HALF type, then the addition at [7] will increment the pointer by 4-bytes * xsize * nb_channels, which will exceed the allocated buffer.\n\n\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-59733**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libswscale7||[CVE-2025-59733](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59733)|\n\nWhen decoding an OpenEXR file that uses DWAA or DWAB compression, there's an implicit assumption that all image channels have the same pixel type (and size), and that if there are four channels, the first four are \"B\", \"G\", \"R\" and \"A\". The channel parsing code can be found in decode_header. The buffer td-\u003euncompressed_data is allocated in decode_block based on the xsize, ysize and computed current_channel_offset.\n\nThe function dwa_uncompress then assumes at [5] that if there are 4 channels, these are \"B\", \"G\", \"R\" and \"A\", and in the calculations at [6] and [7] that all channels are of the same type, which matches the type of the main color channels.\n\nIf we set the main color channels to a 4-byte type and add duplicate or unknown channels of the 2-byte EXR_HALF type, then the addition at [7] will increment the pointer by 4-bytes * xsize * nb_channels, which will exceed the allocated buffer.\n\n\n\n\n\nWe recommend upgrading to version 8.0 or beyond."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
