            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-3832",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "gnutls: gnutls: Security bypass allows acceptance of revoked server certificates via crafted OCSP response"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in gnutls. A remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability by presenting a specially crafted Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) response during a TLS handshake. Due to a logic error in how gnutls processes multi-record OCSP responses, a client with OCSP verification enabled may incorrectly accept a revoked server certificate, potentially leading to a compromise of trust."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3832",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-3832\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libgnutls30t64\nFixed Version: 3.8.3-1.1ubuntu3.6\nLink: [CVE-2026-3832](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3832)\nA flaw was found in gnutls. A remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability by presenting a specially crafted Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) response during a TLS handshake. Due to a logic error in how gnutls processes multi-record OCSP responses, a client with OCSP verification enabled may incorrectly accept a revoked server certificate, potentially leading to a compromise of trust.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-3832**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libgnutls30t64|3.8.3-1.1ubuntu3.6|[CVE-2026-3832](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3832)|\n\nA flaw was found in gnutls. A remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability by presenting a specially crafted Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) response during a TLS handshake. Due to a logic error in how gnutls processes multi-record OCSP responses, a client with OCSP verification enabled may incorrectly accept a revoked server certificate, potentially leading to a compromise of trust."
