            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-9820",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "gnutls: Stack-based Buffer Overflow in gnutls_pkcs11_token_init() Function"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in the GnuTLS library, specifically in the gnutls_pkcs11_token_init() function that handles PKCS#11 token initialization. When a token label longer than expected is processed, the function writes past the end of a fixed-size stack buffer. This programming error can cause the application using GnuTLS to crash or, in certain conditions, be exploited for code execution. As a result, systems or applications relying on GnuTLS may be vulnerable to a denial of service or local privilege escalation attacks."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-9820",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-9820\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libgnutls30t64\nFixed Version: 3.8.3-1.1ubuntu3.5\nLink: [CVE-2025-9820](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-9820)\nA flaw was found in the GnuTLS library, specifically in the gnutls_pkcs11_token_init() function that handles PKCS#11 token initialization. When a token label longer than expected is processed, the function writes past the end of a fixed-size stack buffer. This programming error can cause the application using GnuTLS to crash or, in certain conditions, be exploited for code execution. As a result, systems or applications relying on GnuTLS may be vulnerable to a denial of service or local privilege escalation attacks.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-9820**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libgnutls30t64|3.8.3-1.1ubuntu3.5|[CVE-2025-9820](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-9820)|\n\nA flaw was found in the GnuTLS library, specifically in the gnutls_pkcs11_token_init() function that handles PKCS#11 token initialization. When a token label longer than expected is processed, the function writes past the end of a fixed-size stack buffer. This programming error can cause the application using GnuTLS to crash or, in certain conditions, be exploited for code execution. As a result, systems or applications relying on GnuTLS may be vulnerable to a denial of service or local privilege escalation attacks."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-22693",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "harfbuzz: Null Pointer Dereference in harfbuzz"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HarfBuzz is a text shaping engine. Prior to version 12.3.0, a null pointer dereference vulnerability exists in the SubtableUnicodesCache::create function located in src/hb-ot-cmap-table.hh. The function fails to check if hb_malloc returns NULL before using placement new to construct an object at the returned pointer address. When hb_malloc fails to allocate memory (which can occur in low-memory conditions or when using custom allocators that simulate allocation failures), it returns NULL. The code then attempts to call the constructor on this null pointer using placement new syntax, resulting in undefined behavior and a Segmentation Fault. This issue has been patched in version 12.3.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-22693",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-22693\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: libharfbuzz0b\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-22693](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-22693)\nHarfBuzz is a text shaping engine. Prior to version 12.3.0, a null pointer dereference vulnerability exists in the SubtableUnicodesCache::create function located in src/hb-ot-cmap-table.hh. The function fails to check if hb_malloc returns NULL before using placement new to construct an object at the returned pointer address. When hb_malloc fails to allocate memory (which can occur in low-memory conditions or when using custom allocators that simulate allocation failures), it returns NULL. The code then attempts to call the constructor on this null pointer using placement new syntax, resulting in undefined behavior and a Segmentation Fault. This issue has been patched in version 12.3.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-22693**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|libharfbuzz0b||[CVE-2026-22693](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-22693)|\n\nHarfBuzz is a text shaping engine. Prior to version 12.3.0, a null pointer dereference vulnerability exists in the SubtableUnicodesCache::create function located in src/hb-ot-cmap-table.hh. The function fails to check if hb_malloc returns NULL before using placement new to construct an object at the returned pointer address. When hb_malloc fails to allocate memory (which can occur in low-memory conditions or when using custom allocators that simulate allocation failures), it returns NULL. The code then attempts to call the constructor on this null pointer using placement new syntax, resulting in undefined behavior and a Segmentation Fault. This issue has been patched in version 12.3.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
