            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11822",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "sqlite: SQLite: Arbitrary code execution via crafted FTS5 full-text search data"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite before 3.53.2 contains memory corruption vulnerabilities in the FTS5 full-text search extension that allow attackers to cause process crashes, memory exhaustion, or arbitrary code execution by supplying a crafted database with malformed FTS5 page data. Attackers can trigger an out-of-bounds read in fts5LeafSeek() via an attacker-controlled loop bound and a heap buffer overflow write in fts5ChunkIterate() through a crafted continuation page causing an integer underflow, exploitable when an FTS5 MATCH query is executed against the malicious database."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-11822",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11822\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libsqlite3-0\nFixed Version: 3.45.1-1ubuntu2.6\nLink: [CVE-2026-11822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-11822)\nSQLite before 3.53.2 contains memory corruption vulnerabilities in the FTS5 full-text search extension that allow attackers to cause process crashes, memory exhaustion, or arbitrary code execution by supplying a crafted database with malformed FTS5 page data. Attackers can trigger an out-of-bounds read in fts5LeafSeek() via an attacker-controlled loop bound and a heap buffer overflow write in fts5ChunkIterate() through a crafted continuation page causing an integer underflow, exploitable when an FTS5 MATCH query is executed against the malicious database.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11822**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libsqlite3-0|3.45.1-1ubuntu2.6|[CVE-2026-11822](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-11822)|\n\nSQLite before 3.53.2 contains memory corruption vulnerabilities in the FTS5 full-text search extension that allow attackers to cause process crashes, memory exhaustion, or arbitrary code execution by supplying a crafted database with malformed FTS5 page data. Attackers can trigger an out-of-bounds read in fts5LeafSeek() via an attacker-controlled loop bound and a heap buffer overflow write in fts5ChunkIterate() through a crafted continuation page causing an integer underflow, exploitable when an FTS5 MATCH query is executed against the malicious database."
              },
