            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11824",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "sqlite: SQLite: Arbitrary code execution and crash via heap-based buffer overflow in FTS5"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite before 3.53.2 contains a heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability in the FTS5 full-text search extension that allows attackers to cause a crash or execute arbitrary code by supplying a crafted database with malicious continuation page metadata specifying a szLeaf value smaller than 4. Attackers can trigger an integer underflow in fts5ChunkIterate() causing an inflated remaining byte count during FTS5 MATCH query processing, leading to a heap buffer overflow of attacker-controlled data in applications compiled with SQLITE_ENABLE_FTS5."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-11824",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11824\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libsqlite3-0\nFixed Version: 3.45.1-1ubuntu2.6\nLink: [CVE-2026-11824](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-11824)\nSQLite before 3.53.2 contains a heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability in the FTS5 full-text search extension that allows attackers to cause a crash or execute arbitrary code by supplying a crafted database with malicious continuation page metadata specifying a szLeaf value smaller than 4. Attackers can trigger an integer underflow in fts5ChunkIterate() causing an inflated remaining byte count during FTS5 MATCH query processing, leading to a heap buffer overflow of attacker-controlled data in applications compiled with SQLITE_ENABLE_FTS5.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11824**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libsqlite3-0|3.45.1-1ubuntu2.6|[CVE-2026-11824](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-11824)|\n\nSQLite before 3.53.2 contains a heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability in the FTS5 full-text search extension that allows attackers to cause a crash or execute arbitrary code by supplying a crafted database with malicious continuation page metadata specifying a szLeaf value smaller than 4. Attackers can trigger an integer underflow in fts5ChunkIterate() causing an inflated remaining byte count during FTS5 MATCH query processing, leading to a heap buffer overflow of attacker-controlled data in applications compiled with SQLITE_ENABLE_FTS5."
              },
              "properties": {
