            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-86144",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "libxml2: libxml2: Information disclosure, SSRF, or denial of service due to improper parseFlags propagation."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In xinclude in libxml2 before 2.15.4, xmlXIncludeProcess and xmlXIncludeProcessTree do not propagate parseFlags. This has security relevance for, for example, the XML_PARSE_NONET flag, if (without it) a custom resource loader accesses the internet and triggers XML external entity injection, SSRF, or a denial of service (e.g., for an attacker-controlled internet resource that is intentionally slow)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-86144",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-86144\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libxml2\nFixed Version: 2.9.14+dfsg-1.3ubuntu3.10\nLink: [CVE-2026-86144](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-86144)\nIn xinclude in libxml2 before 2.15.4, xmlXIncludeProcess and xmlXIncludeProcessTree do not propagate parseFlags. This has security relevance for, for example, the XML_PARSE_NONET flag, if (without it) a custom resource loader accesses the internet and triggers XML external entity injection, SSRF, or a denial of service (e.g., for an attacker-controlled internet resource that is intentionally slow).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-86144**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libxml2|2.9.14+dfsg-1.3ubuntu3.10|[CVE-2026-86144](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-86144)|\n\nIn xinclude in libxml2 before 2.15.4, xmlXIncludeProcess and xmlXIncludeProcessTree do not propagate parseFlags. This has security relevance for, for example, the XML_PARSE_NONET flag, if (without it) a custom resource loader accesses the internet and triggers XML external entity injection, SSRF, or a denial of service (e.g., for an attacker-controlled internet resource that is intentionally slow)."
