            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-40139",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: smc: Use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu() in in smc_clc_prfx_set()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmc: Use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu() in in smc_clc_prfx_set().\n\nsmc_clc_prfx_set() is called during connect() and not under RCU\nnor RTNL.\n\nUsing sk_dst_get(sk)-\u003edev could trigger UAF.\n\nLet's use __sk_dst_get() and dev_dst_rcu() under rcu_read_lock()\nafter kernel_getsockname().\n\nNote that the returned value of smc_clc_prfx_set() is not used\nin the caller.\n\nWhile at it, we change the 1st arg of smc_clc_prfx_set[46]_rcu()\nnot to touch dst there."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40139",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-40139\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-40139](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40139)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmc: Use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu() in in smc_clc_prfx_set().\n\nsmc_clc_prfx_set() is called during connect() and not under RCU\nnor RTNL.\n\nUsing sk_dst_get(sk)-\u003edev could trigger UAF.\n\nLet's use __sk_dst_get() and dev_dst_rcu() under rcu_read_lock()\nafter kernel_getsockname().\n\nNote that the returned value of smc_clc_prfx_set() is not used\nin the caller.\n\nWhile at it, we change the 1st arg of smc_clc_prfx_set[46]_rcu()\nnot to touch dst there.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-40139**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-40139](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40139)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmc: Use __sk_dst_get() and dst_dev_rcu() in in smc_clc_prfx_set().\n\nsmc_clc_prfx_set() is called during connect() and not under RCU\nnor RTNL.\n\nUsing sk_dst_get(sk)-\u003edev could trigger UAF.\n\nLet's use __sk_dst_get() and dev_dst_rcu() under rcu_read_lock()\nafter kernel_getsockname().\n\nNote that the returned value of smc_clc_prfx_set() is not used\nin the caller.\n\nWhile at it, we change the 1st arg of smc_clc_prfx_set[46]_rcu()\nnot to touch dst there."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-40158",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ipv6: use RCU in ip6_output()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: use RCU in ip6_output()\n\nUse RCU in ip6_output() in order to use dst_dev_rcu() to prevent\npossible UAF.\n\nWe can remove rcu_read_lock()/rcu_read_unlock() pairs\nfrom ip6_finish_output2()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40158",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-40158\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-40158](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40158)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: use RCU in ip6_output()\n\nUse RCU in ip6_output() in order to use dst_dev_rcu() to prevent\npossible UAF.\n\nWe can remove rcu_read_lock()/rcu_read_unlock() pairs\nfrom ip6_finish_output2().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-40158**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-40158](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40158)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: use RCU in ip6_output()\n\nUse RCU in ip6_output() in order to use dst_dev_rcu() to prevent\npossible UAF.\n\nWe can remove rcu_read_lock()/rcu_read_unlock() pairs\nfrom ip6_finish_output2()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
