            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-40344",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ASoC: Intel: avs: Disable periods-elapsed work when closing PCM"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: Intel: avs: Disable periods-elapsed work when closing PCM\n\navs_dai_fe_shutdown() handles the shutdown procedure for HOST HDAudio\nstream while period-elapsed work services its IRQs. As the former\nfrees the DAI's private context, these two operations shall be\nsynchronized to avoid slab-use-after-free or worse errors."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40344",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-40344\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-40344](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40344)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: Intel: avs: Disable periods-elapsed work when closing PCM\n\navs_dai_fe_shutdown() handles the shutdown procedure for HOST HDAudio\nstream while period-elapsed work services its IRQs. As the former\nfrees the DAI's private context, these two operations shall be\nsynchronized to avoid slab-use-after-free or worse errors.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-40344**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-40344](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40344)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: Intel: avs: Disable periods-elapsed work when closing PCM\n\navs_dai_fe_shutdown() handles the shutdown procedure for HOST HDAudio\nstream while period-elapsed work services its IRQs. As the former\nfrees the DAI's private context, these two operations shall be\nsynchronized to avoid slab-use-after-free or worse errors."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-68251",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Linux kernel (erofs): Denial of Service via corrupted subpage compact indexes"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nerofs: avoid infinite loops due to corrupted subpage compact indexes\n\nRobert reported an infinite loop observed by two crafted images.\n\nThe root cause is that `clusterofs` can be larger than `lclustersize`\nfor !NONHEAD `lclusters` in corrupted subpage compact indexes, e.g.:\n\n  blocksize = lclustersize = 512   lcn = 6   clusterofs = 515\n\nMove the corresponding check for full compress indexes to\n`z_erofs_load_lcluster_from_disk()` to also cover subpage compact\ncompress indexes.\n\nIt also fixes the position of `m-\u003etype \u003e= Z_EROFS_LCLUSTER_TYPE_MAX`\ncheck, since it should be placed right after\n`z_erofs_load_{compact,full}_lcluster()`."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68251",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-68251\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-68251](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68251)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nerofs: avoid infinite loops due to corrupted subpage compact indexes\n\nRobert reported an infinite loop observed by two crafted images.\n\nThe root cause is that `clusterofs` can be larger than `lclustersize`\nfor !NONHEAD `lclusters` in corrupted subpage compact indexes, e.g.:\n\n  blocksize = lclustersize = 512   lcn = 6   clusterofs = 515\n\nMove the corresponding check for full compress indexes to\n`z_erofs_load_lcluster_from_disk()` to also cover subpage compact\ncompress indexes.\n\nIt also fixes the position of `m-\u003etype \u003e= Z_EROFS_LCLUSTER_TYPE_MAX`\ncheck, since it should be placed right after\n`z_erofs_load_{compact,full}_lcluster()`.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-68251**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-68251](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68251)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nerofs: avoid infinite loops due to corrupted subpage compact indexes\n\nRobert reported an infinite loop observed by two crafted images.\n\nThe root cause is that `clusterofs` can be larger than `lclustersize`\nfor !NONHEAD `lclusters` in corrupted subpage compact indexes, e.g.:\n\n  blocksize = lclustersize = 512   lcn = 6   clusterofs = 515\n\nMove the corresponding check for full compress indexes to\n`z_erofs_load_lcluster_from_disk()` to also cover subpage compact\ncompress indexes.\n\nIt also fixes the position of `m-\u003etype \u003e= Z_EROFS_LCLUSTER_TYPE_MAX`\ncheck, since it should be placed right after\n`z_erofs_load_{compact,full}_lcluster()`."
              },
              "properties": {
