            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-31410",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: use volume UUID in FS_OBJECT_ID_INFORMATION"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: use volume UUID in FS_OBJECT_ID_INFORMATION\n\nUse sb-\u003es_uuid for a proper volume identifier as the primary choice.\nFor filesystems that do not provide a UUID, fall back to stfs.f_fsid\nobtained from vfs_statfs()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31410",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-31410\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-31410](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31410)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: use volume UUID in FS_OBJECT_ID_INFORMATION\n\nUse sb-\u003es_uuid for a proper volume identifier as the primary choice.\nFor filesystems that do not provide a UUID, fall back to stfs.f_fsid\nobtained from vfs_statfs().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-31410**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-31410](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31410)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: use volume UUID in FS_OBJECT_ID_INFORMATION\n\nUse sb-\u003es_uuid for a proper volume identifier as the primary choice.\nFor filesystems that do not provide a UUID, fall back to stfs.f_fsid\nobtained from vfs_statfs()."
              },
              "properties": {
