            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74724",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ipvs: avoid out-of-bounds write in ip_vs_nat_icmp"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipvs: avoid out-of-bounds write in ip_vs_nat_icmp\n\nSashiko warns that local attacker can modify the packet\nwhile it is processed by IPVS. Some places read the\nIP ihl field multiple times which can cause out-of-bounds\naccess. One such place is ip_vs_nat_icmp where we\ncan write after the validated area.\n\nFix it by providing ciph argument just like it is done for\nIPv6 and use ciph-\u003elen as offset to the embedded transport\nheader.\n\nModify some IPv4 header checks by reading the ihl field\nonly once."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74724",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74724\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-74724](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74724)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipvs: avoid out-of-bounds write in ip_vs_nat_icmp\n\nSashiko warns that local attacker can modify the packet\nwhile it is processed by IPVS. Some places read the\nIP ihl field multiple times which can cause out-of-bounds\naccess. One such place is ip_vs_nat_icmp where we\ncan write after the validated area.\n\nFix it by providing ciph argument just like it is done for\nIPv6 and use ciph-\u003elen as offset to the embedded transport\nheader.\n\nModify some IPv4 header checks by reading the ihl field\nonly once.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74724**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-74724](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74724)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipvs: avoid out-of-bounds write in ip_vs_nat_icmp\n\nSashiko warns that local attacker can modify the packet\nwhile it is processed by IPVS. Some places read the\nIP ihl field multiple times which can cause out-of-bounds\naccess. One such place is ip_vs_nat_icmp where we\ncan write after the validated area.\n\nFix it by providing ciph argument just like it is done for\nIPv6 and use ciph-\u003elen as offset to the embedded transport\nheader.\n\nModify some IPv4 header checks by reading the ihl field\nonly once."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
