            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89448",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: iommu/vt-d: Force requesting ACS when tboot is enabled"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/vt-d: Force requesting ACS when tboot is enabled\n\nCurrently the conditions of requesting ACS in detect_intel_iommu()\ndon't include tboot, leading to a possible misconfiguration with ACS\ndisabled (e.g. due to user opts) while iommu is later forced on by\ntboot_force_iommu().\n\nFix it by checking tboot in detect_intel_iommu()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89448",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89448\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89448](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89448)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/vt-d: Force requesting ACS when tboot is enabled\n\nCurrently the conditions of requesting ACS in detect_intel_iommu()\ndon't include tboot, leading to a possible misconfiguration with ACS\ndisabled (e.g. due to user opts) while iommu is later forced on by\ntboot_force_iommu().\n\nFix it by checking tboot in detect_intel_iommu().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89448**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89448](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89448)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/vt-d: Force requesting ACS when tboot is enabled\n\nCurrently the conditions of requesting ACS in detect_intel_iommu()\ndon't include tboot, leading to a possible misconfiguration with ACS\ndisabled (e.g. due to user opts) while iommu is later forced on by\ntboot_force_iommu().\n\nFix it by checking tboot in detect_intel_iommu()."
              },
