              "id": "CVE-2026-97497",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amdkfd: Check bounds for allocate_sdma_queue restore_sdma_id"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Check bounds for allocate_sdma_queue restore_sdma_id\n\nallocate_sdma_queue has an option where the sdma queue id can be\nspecified (used by CRIU). We weren't bounds-checking that\nvalue.\n\nConfirm it's less than the maximum number of queues."
              },
