            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97581",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: media: verisilicon: hantro: bound G2 HEVC tile loop to the buffer capacity"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: verisilicon: hantro: bound G2 HEVC tile loop to the buffer capacity\n\nprepare_tile_info_buffer() writes one entry per tile into the tile_sizes\nDMA buffer, sized for a grid equal to the PPS uAPI array capacity. Use the\nbounded v4l2_hevc_pps_num_tile_columns() / v4l2_hevc_pps_num_tile_rows()\nhelpers so the loops stay inside the buffer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97581",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97581\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97581](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97581)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: verisilicon: hantro: bound G2 HEVC tile loop to the buffer capacity\n\nprepare_tile_info_buffer() writes one entry per tile into the tile_sizes\nDMA buffer, sized for a grid equal to the PPS uAPI array capacity. Use the\nbounded v4l2_hevc_pps_num_tile_columns() / v4l2_hevc_pps_num_tile_rows()\nhelpers so the loops stay inside the buffer.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97581**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97581](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97581)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: verisilicon: hantro: bound G2 HEVC tile loop to the buffer capacity\n\nprepare_tile_info_buffer() writes one entry per tile into the tile_sizes\nDMA buffer, sized for a grid equal to the PPS uAPI array capacity. Use the\nbounded v4l2_hevc_pps_num_tile_columns() / v4l2_hevc_pps_num_tile_rows()\nhelpers so the loops stay inside the buffer."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
