              "id": "CVE-2015-7837",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: securelevel disabled after kexec"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Linux kernel, as used in Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7, kernel-rt, and Enterprise MRG 2 and when booted with UEFI Secure Boot enabled, allows local users to bypass intended securelevel/secureboot restrictions by leveraging improper handling of secure_boot flag across kexec reboot."
