            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-54187",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Linux kernel (F2FS): Data corruption and denial of service when moving a directory"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: fix potential corruption when moving a directory\n\nF2FS has the same issue in ext4_rename causing crash revealed by\nxfstests/generic/707.\n\nSee also commit 0813299c586b (\"ext4: Fix possible corruption when moving a directory\")"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-54187",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-54187\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2023-54187](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-54187)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: fix potential corruption when moving a directory\n\nF2FS has the same issue in ext4_rename causing crash revealed by\nxfstests/generic/707.\n\nSee also commit 0813299c586b (\"ext4: Fix possible corruption when moving a directory\")",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-54187**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2023-54187](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-54187)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: fix potential corruption when moving a directory\n\nF2FS has the same issue in ext4_rename causing crash revealed by\nxfstests/generic/707.\n\nSee also commit 0813299c586b (\"ext4: Fix possible corruption when moving a directory\")"
