              "id": "CVE-2024-27025",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: nbd: null check for nla_nest_start"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnbd: null check for nla_nest_start\n\nnla_nest_start() may fail and return NULL. Insert a check and set errno\nbased on other call sites within the same source code."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-27025",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-27025\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-27025](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-27025)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnbd: null check for nla_nest_start\n\nnla_nest_start() may fail and return NULL. Insert a check and set errno\nbased on other call sites within the same source code.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-27025**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2024-27025](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-27025)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnbd: null check for nla_nest_start\n\nnla_nest_start() may fail and return NULL. Insert a check and set errno\nbased on other call sites within the same source code."
