            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-43872",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: RDMA/hns: Fix soft lockup under heavy CEQE load"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/hns: Fix soft lockup under heavy CEQE load\n\nCEQEs are handled in interrupt handler currently. This may cause the\nCPU core staying in interrupt context too long and lead to soft lockup\nunder heavy load.\n\nHandle CEQEs in BH workqueue and set an upper limit for the number of\nCEQE handled by a single call of work handler."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-43872",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-43872\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-43872](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-43872)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/hns: Fix soft lockup under heavy CEQE load\n\nCEQEs are handled in interrupt handler currently. This may cause the\nCPU core staying in interrupt context too long and lead to soft lockup\nunder heavy load.\n\nHandle CEQEs in BH workqueue and set an upper limit for the number of\nCEQE handled by a single call of work handler.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-43872**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2024-43872](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-43872)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/hns: Fix soft lockup under heavy CEQE load\n\nCEQEs are handled in interrupt handler currently. This may cause the\nCPU core staying in interrupt context too long and lead to soft lockup\nunder heavy load.\n\nHandle CEQEs in BH workqueue and set an upper limit for the number of\nCEQE handled by a single call of work handler."
