            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50003",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amd/display: Fix system hang while resume with TBT monitor"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Fix system hang while resume with TBT monitor\n\n[Why]\nConnected with a Thunderbolt monitor and do the suspend and the system\nmay hang while resume.\n\nThe TBT monitor HPD will be triggered during the resume procedure\nand call the drm_client_modeset_probe() while\nstruct drm_connector connector-\u003edev-\u003emaster is NULL.\n\nIt will mess up the pipe topology after resume.\n\n[How]\nSkip the TBT monitor HPD during the resume procedure because we\ncurrently will probe the connectors after resume by default.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 453f86a26945207a16b8f66aaed5962dc2b95b85)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50003",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50003\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-50003](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50003)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Fix system hang while resume with TBT monitor\n\n[Why]\nConnected with a Thunderbolt monitor and do the suspend and the system\nmay hang while resume.\n\nThe TBT monitor HPD will be triggered during the resume procedure\nand call the drm_client_modeset_probe() while\nstruct drm_connector connector-\u003edev-\u003emaster is NULL.\n\nIt will mess up the pipe topology after resume.\n\n[How]\nSkip the TBT monitor HPD during the resume procedure because we\ncurrently will probe the connectors after resume by default.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 453f86a26945207a16b8f66aaed5962dc2b95b85)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50003**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2024-50003](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50003)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Fix system hang while resume with TBT monitor\n\n[Why]\nConnected with a Thunderbolt monitor and do the suspend and the system\nmay hang while resume.\n\nThe TBT monitor HPD will be triggered during the resume procedure\nand call the drm_client_modeset_probe() while\nstruct drm_connector connector-\u003edev-\u003emaster is NULL.\n\nIt will mess up the pipe topology after resume.\n\n[How]\nSkip the TBT monitor HPD during the resume procedure because we\ncurrently will probe the connectors after resume by default.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 453f86a26945207a16b8f66aaed5962dc2b95b85)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
