            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53098",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/xe/ufence: Prefetch ufence addr to catch bogus address"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe/ufence: Prefetch ufence addr to catch bogus address\n\naccess_ok() only checks for addr overflow so also try to read the addr\nto catch invalid addr sent from userspace.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9408c4508483ffc60811e910a93d6425b8e63928)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53098",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53098\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-53098](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53098)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe/ufence: Prefetch ufence addr to catch bogus address\n\naccess_ok() only checks for addr overflow so also try to read the addr\nto catch invalid addr sent from userspace.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9408c4508483ffc60811e910a93d6425b8e63928)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53098**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2024-53098](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53098)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/xe/ufence: Prefetch ufence addr to catch bogus address\n\naccess_ok() only checks for addr overflow so also try to read the addr\nto catch invalid addr sent from userspace.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9408c4508483ffc60811e910a93d6425b8e63928)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
