            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-40203",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: listmount: don't call path_put() under namespace semaphore"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlistmount: don't call path_put() under namespace semaphore\n\nMassage listmount() and make sure we don't call path_put() under the\nnamespace semaphore. If we put the last reference we're fscked."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40203",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-40203\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-40203](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40203)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlistmount: don't call path_put() under namespace semaphore\n\nMassage listmount() and make sure we don't call path_put() under the\nnamespace semaphore. If we put the last reference we're fscked.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-40203**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-40203](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40203)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlistmount: don't call path_put() under namespace semaphore\n\nMassage listmount() and make sure we don't call path_put() under the\nnamespace semaphore. If we put the last reference we're fscked."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
