            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46071",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: KVM: nSVM: Avoid clearing VMCB_LBR in vmcb12"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: nSVM: Avoid clearing VMCB_LBR in vmcb12\n\nsvm_copy_lbrs() always marks VMCB_LBR dirty in the destination VMCB.\nHowever, nested_svm_vmexit() uses it to copy LBRs to vmcb12, and\nclearing clean bits in vmcb12 is not architecturally defined.\n\nMove vmcb_mark_dirty() to callers and drop it for vmcb12.\n\nThis also facilitates incoming refactoring that does not pass the entire\nVMCB to svm_copy_lbrs()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46071",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-46071\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-46071](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46071)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: nSVM: Avoid clearing VMCB_LBR in vmcb12\n\nsvm_copy_lbrs() always marks VMCB_LBR dirty in the destination VMCB.\nHowever, nested_svm_vmexit() uses it to copy LBRs to vmcb12, and\nclearing clean bits in vmcb12 is not architecturally defined.\n\nMove vmcb_mark_dirty() to callers and drop it for vmcb12.\n\nThis also facilitates incoming refactoring that does not pass the entire\nVMCB to svm_copy_lbrs().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-46071**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-46071](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46071)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: nSVM: Avoid clearing VMCB_LBR in vmcb12\n\nsvm_copy_lbrs() always marks VMCB_LBR dirty in the destination VMCB.\nHowever, nested_svm_vmexit() uses it to copy LBRs to vmcb12, and\nclearing clean bits in vmcb12 is not architecturally defined.\n\nMove vmcb_mark_dirty() to callers and drop it for vmcb12.\n\nThis also facilitates incoming refactoring that does not pass the entire\nVMCB to svm_copy_lbrs()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
