            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64160",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: netfs: Fix potential for tearing in -\u003eremote_i_size and -\u003ezero_point"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix potential for tearing in -\u003eremote_i_size and -\u003ezero_point\n\nFix potential tearing in using -\u003eremote_i_size and -\u003ezero_point by copying\ni_size_read() and i_size_write() and using the same seqcount as for i_size.\n\nWe need to make sure that netfslib and the filesystems that use it always\nhold i_lock whilst updating any of the sizes to prevent i_size_seqcount\nfrom getting corrupted."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64160",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64160\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64160](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64160)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix potential for tearing in -\u003eremote_i_size and -\u003ezero_point\n\nFix potential tearing in using -\u003eremote_i_size and -\u003ezero_point by copying\ni_size_read() and i_size_write() and using the same seqcount as for i_size.\n\nWe need to make sure that netfslib and the filesystems that use it always\nhold i_lock whilst updating any of the sizes to prevent i_size_seqcount\nfrom getting corrupted.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64160**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64160](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64160)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix potential for tearing in -\u003eremote_i_size and -\u003ezero_point\n\nFix potential tearing in using -\u003eremote_i_size and -\u003ezero_point by copying\ni_size_read() and i_size_write() and using the same seqcount as for i_size.\n\nWe need to make sure that netfslib and the filesystems that use it always\nhold i_lock whilst updating any of the sizes to prevent i_size_seqcount\nfrom getting corrupted."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
