                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68242",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/i915/gt: Fix NULL deref on sched_engine alloc failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/gt: Fix NULL deref on sched_engine alloc failure\n\nAvoid using intel_context_put() before intel_context_init() in\nexeclists_create_virtual() as the kref_put() inside would lead\nto NULL deref on the IOCTL path when sched_engine allocation fails.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by\nIntel Product Security.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4f2a12f2d50e9f48227656e4dcbd6423506be31d)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68242",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68242\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-68242](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68242)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/gt: Fix NULL deref on sched_engine alloc failure\n\nAvoid using intel_context_put() before intel_context_init() in\nexeclists_create_virtual() as the kref_put() inside would lead\nto NULL deref on the IOCTL path when sched_engine allocation fails.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by\nIntel Product Security.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4f2a12f2d50e9f48227656e4dcbd6423506be31d)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68242**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-68242](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68242)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/gt: Fix NULL deref on sched_engine alloc failure\n\nAvoid using intel_context_put() before intel_context_init() in\nexeclists_create_virtual() as the kref_put() inside would lead\nto NULL deref on the IOCTL path when sched_engine allocation fails.\n\nDiscovered using AI-assisted static analysis confirmed by\nIntel Product Security.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4f2a12f2d50e9f48227656e4dcbd6423506be31d)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-68252",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amdgpu/sdma7.0: replace BUG_ON() with WARN_ON()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/sdma7.0: replace BUG_ON() with WARN_ON()\n\nThere's no need to crash the kernel for these cases.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9723a8bed3aa251a26bee4583bac9d8fb064dd44)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68252",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-68252\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-68252](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68252)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/sdma7.0: replace BUG_ON() with WARN_ON()\n\nThere's no need to crash the kernel for these cases.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9723a8bed3aa251a26bee4583bac9d8fb064dd44)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-68252**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-68252](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-68252)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu/sdma7.0: replace BUG_ON() with WARN_ON()\n\nThere's no need to crash the kernel for these cases.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9723a8bed3aa251a26bee4583bac9d8fb064dd44)"
