            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74258",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: bpf: Guard __get_user acesss with access_ok for uprobe_multi data"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Guard __get_user acesss with access_ok for uprobe_multi data\n\nAs reported by sashiko [1] we need to use access_ok to check the user\nspace data bounds before we use __get-user to get it.\n\n[1] https://lore.kernel.org/bpf/20260610145235.CB1441F00893@smtp.kernel.org/"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74258",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74258\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-74258](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74258)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Guard __get_user acesss with access_ok for uprobe_multi data\n\nAs reported by sashiko [1] we need to use access_ok to check the user\nspace data bounds before we use __get-user to get it.\n\n[1] https://lore.kernel.org/bpf/20260610145235.CB1441F00893@smtp.kernel.org/",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74258**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-74258](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74258)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Guard __get_user acesss with access_ok for uprobe_multi data\n\nAs reported by sashiko [1] we need to use access_ok to check the user\nspace data bounds before we use __get-user to get it.\n\n[1] https://lore.kernel.org/bpf/20260610145235.CB1441F00893@smtp.kernel.org/"
              },
