            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74458",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: can: kvaser_usb_leaf: kvaser_usb_leaf_wait_cmd(): validate received command extents"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: kvaser_usb_leaf: kvaser_usb_leaf_wait_cmd(): validate received command extents\n\nThe wait and bulk receive paths walk variable-length commands from a\nUSB buffer. A nonzero command shorter than CMD_HEADER_LEN can still be\ndispatched, and the wait path copies a matching command into a fixed\ncaller-owned struct kvaser_cmd using the device-provided length.\n\nReject nonzero commands that do not contain the fixed header or that\nextend beyond the current USB buffer item. In the wait path, also reject\na matching command that exceeds the destination before copying it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74458",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74458\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-74458](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74458)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: kvaser_usb_leaf: kvaser_usb_leaf_wait_cmd(): validate received command extents\n\nThe wait and bulk receive paths walk variable-length commands from a\nUSB buffer. A nonzero command shorter than CMD_HEADER_LEN can still be\ndispatched, and the wait path copies a matching command into a fixed\ncaller-owned struct kvaser_cmd using the device-provided length.\n\nReject nonzero commands that do not contain the fixed header or that\nextend beyond the current USB buffer item. In the wait path, also reject\na matching command that exceeds the destination before copying it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74458**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-74458](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74458)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: kvaser_usb_leaf: kvaser_usb_leaf_wait_cmd(): validate received command extents\n\nThe wait and bulk receive paths walk variable-length commands from a\nUSB buffer. A nonzero command shorter than CMD_HEADER_LEN can still be\ndispatched, and the wait path copies a matching command into a fixed\ncaller-owned struct kvaser_cmd using the device-provided length.\n\nReject nonzero commands that do not contain the fixed header or that\nextend beyond the current USB buffer item. In the wait path, also reject\na matching command that exceeds the destination before copying it."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
