            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74459",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: can: etas_es58x: es58x_read_bulk_callback(): fix RX buffer leak on URB resubmit failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: etas_es58x: es58x_read_bulk_callback(): fix RX buffer leak on URB resubmit failure\n\nes58x_read_bulk_callback() resubmits the RX URB after processing a received\npacket. If the resubmit succeeds, the URB remains anchored and will be\nhandled by the normal RX path or by teardown.\n\nHowever, if usb_submit_urb() fails, the callback unanchors the URB and then\nreturns directly. This skips the existing free_urb path, so the coherent\ntransfer buffer allocated with usb_alloc_coherent() is not released.\n\nReuse the existing free_urb path after a resubmit failure so that the RX\ncoherent buffer is freed before leaving the callback."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74459",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74459\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-74459](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74459)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: etas_es58x: es58x_read_bulk_callback(): fix RX buffer leak on URB resubmit failure\n\nes58x_read_bulk_callback() resubmits the RX URB after processing a received\npacket. If the resubmit succeeds, the URB remains anchored and will be\nhandled by the normal RX path or by teardown.\n\nHowever, if usb_submit_urb() fails, the callback unanchors the URB and then\nreturns directly. This skips the existing free_urb path, so the coherent\ntransfer buffer allocated with usb_alloc_coherent() is not released.\n\nReuse the existing free_urb path after a resubmit failure so that the RX\ncoherent buffer is freed before leaving the callback.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74459**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-74459](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74459)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: etas_es58x: es58x_read_bulk_callback(): fix RX buffer leak on URB resubmit failure\n\nes58x_read_bulk_callback() resubmits the RX URB after processing a received\npacket. If the resubmit succeeds, the URB remains anchored and will be\nhandled by the normal RX path or by teardown.\n\nHowever, if usb_submit_urb() fails, the callback unanchors the URB and then\nreturns directly. This skips the existing free_urb path, so the coherent\ntransfer buffer allocated with usb_alloc_coherent() is not released.\n\nReuse the existing free_urb path after a resubmit failure so that the RX\ncoherent buffer is freed before leaving the callback."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74460",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: can: ems_usb: validate CPC message lengths"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: ems_usb: validate CPC message lengths\n\nems_usb_read_bulk_callback() walks CPC messages packed in one USB\nreceive buffer.\n\nCheck that each declared message fits in the URB payload. Also require the\ntype-specific payload to cover the fields used by the CAN, state, error and\noverrun handlers."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74460",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74460\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-74460](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74460)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: ems_usb: validate CPC message lengths\n\nems_usb_read_bulk_callback() walks CPC messages packed in one USB\nreceive buffer.\n\nCheck that each declared message fits in the URB payload. Also require the\ntype-specific payload to cover the fields used by the CAN, state, error and\noverrun handlers.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74460**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-74460](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74460)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: ems_usb: validate CPC message lengths\n\nems_usb_read_bulk_callback() walks CPC messages packed in one USB\nreceive buffer.\n\nCheck that each declared message fits in the URB payload. Also require the\ntype-specific payload to cover the fields used by the CAN, state, error and\noverrun handlers."
              },
              "properties": {
