            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74705",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: udp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nudp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation\n\n__skb_udp_tunnel_segment() gets the UDP header before ensuring the\ntunnel header is in the skb head. If the pull reallocates skb-\u003ehead,\nthe saved UDP header pointer is no longer valid.\n\nGet the UDP header after the pull to avoid a potential use-after-free."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74705",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-74705\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-74705](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74705)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nudp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation\n\n__skb_udp_tunnel_segment() gets the UDP header before ensuring the\ntunnel header is in the skb head. If the pull reallocates skb-\u003ehead,\nthe saved UDP header pointer is no longer valid.\n\nGet the UDP header after the pull to avoid a potential use-after-free.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-74705**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-74705](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-74705)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nudp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation\n\n__skb_udp_tunnel_segment() gets the UDP header before ensuring the\ntunnel header is in the skb head. If the pull reallocates skb-\u003ehead,\nthe saved UDP header pointer is no longer valid.\n\nGet the UDP header after the pull to avoid a potential use-after-free."
              },
