            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80568",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Input: synaptics-rmi4 - block s_input when F54 queue is busy"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nInput: synaptics-rmi4 - block s_input when F54 queue is busy\n\nChanging the input (diagnostic report type) mid-stream changes the\nreport size. Since V4L2 buffers are allocated based on the size at\nstream start, changing the input while streaming could lead to a\nheap buffer overflow if the new size is larger than the allocated\nbuffers.\n\nPrevent this by blocking VIDIOC_S_INPUT with -EBUSY if the V4L2 queue\nis busy (streaming)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80568",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80568\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80568](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80568)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nInput: synaptics-rmi4 - block s_input when F54 queue is busy\n\nChanging the input (diagnostic report type) mid-stream changes the\nreport size. Since V4L2 buffers are allocated based on the size at\nstream start, changing the input while streaming could lead to a\nheap buffer overflow if the new size is larger than the allocated\nbuffers.\n\nPrevent this by blocking VIDIOC_S_INPUT with -EBUSY if the V4L2 queue\nis busy (streaming).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80568**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80568](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80568)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nInput: synaptics-rmi4 - block s_input when F54 queue is busy\n\nChanging the input (diagnostic report type) mid-stream changes the\nreport size. Since V4L2 buffers are allocated based on the size at\nstream start, changing the input while streaming could lead to a\nheap buffer overflow if the new size is larger than the allocated\nbuffers.\n\nPrevent this by blocking VIDIOC_S_INPUT with -EBUSY if the V4L2 queue\nis busy (streaming)."
              },
