            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80684",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: KVM: s390: pci: Fix NULL dereference on AIBV allocation failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: pci: Fix NULL dereference on AIBV allocation failure\n\nThe airq_iv_create() can return NULL on failure, but the return value was\nnever checked. If it fails, zdev-\u003eaibv will be NULL and fail when\ndereferenced in kvm_zpci_set_airq(). Add a NULL check and free the\npreviously allocated AISB bit and zdev-\u003eaisb on failure."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80684",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80684\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80684](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80684)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: pci: Fix NULL dereference on AIBV allocation failure\n\nThe airq_iv_create() can return NULL on failure, but the return value was\nnever checked. If it fails, zdev-\u003eaibv will be NULL and fail when\ndereferenced in kvm_zpci_set_airq(). Add a NULL check and free the\npreviously allocated AISB bit and zdev-\u003eaisb on failure.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80684**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80684](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80684)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: pci: Fix NULL dereference on AIBV allocation failure\n\nThe airq_iv_create() can return NULL on failure, but the return value was\nnever checked. If it fails, zdev-\u003eaibv will be NULL and fail when\ndereferenced in kvm_zpci_set_airq(). Add a NULL check and free the\npreviously allocated AISB bit and zdev-\u003eaisb on failure."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80686",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: mm: migrate_device: fix pte_pfn/pte_dirty called on non-present PTE"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm: migrate_device: fix pte_pfn/pte_dirty called on non-present PTE\n\npte_pfn() and pte_dirty() have undefined behaviour when called on a\nnon-present PTE. In migrate_vma_collect_pmd(), these functions may be\ninvoked on non-present entries (e.g., device-private entries), leading\nto potential crashes from pte_pfn() or incorrect dirty folio accounting\nfrom pte_dirty(). Fix both by guarding with pte_present() checks."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80686",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80686\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80686](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80686)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm: migrate_device: fix pte_pfn/pte_dirty called on non-present PTE\n\npte_pfn() and pte_dirty() have undefined behaviour when called on a\nnon-present PTE. In migrate_vma_collect_pmd(), these functions may be\ninvoked on non-present entries (e.g., device-private entries), leading\nto potential crashes from pte_pfn() or incorrect dirty folio accounting\nfrom pte_dirty(). Fix both by guarding with pte_present() checks.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80686**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80686](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80686)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm: migrate_device: fix pte_pfn/pte_dirty called on non-present PTE\n\npte_pfn() and pte_dirty() have undefined behaviour when called on a\nnon-present PTE. In migrate_vma_collect_pmd(), these functions may be\ninvoked on non-present entries (e.g., device-private entries), leading\nto potential crashes from pte_pfn() or incorrect dirty folio accounting\nfrom pte_dirty(). Fix both by guarding with pte_present() checks."
              },
