            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80737",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  s ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nserial: amba-pl011: synchronize DMA teardown\n\ndmaengine_terminate_all() does not wait for a running callback, so the TX\ncallback can still touch the TX buffer after it is freed. The RX poll\ntimer reads the RX buffers without the port lock.\n\nSwitch to dmaengine_terminate_sync() and delete the RX timer before\nfreeing the buffers."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80737",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80737\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80737](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80737)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nserial: amba-pl011: synchronize DMA teardown\n\ndmaengine_terminate_all() does not wait for a running callback, so the TX\ncallback can still touch the TX buffer after it is freed. The RX poll\ntimer reads the RX buffers without the port lock.\n\nSwitch to dmaengine_terminate_sync() and delete the RX timer before\nfreeing the buffers.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80737**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80737](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80737)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nserial: amba-pl011: synchronize DMA teardown\n\ndmaengine_terminate_all() does not wait for a running callback, so the TX\ncallback can still touch the TX buffer after it is freed. The RX poll\ntimer reads the RX buffers without the port lock.\n\nSwitch to dmaengine_terminate_sync() and delete the RX timer before\nfreeing the buffers."
              },
              "properties": {
