            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80770",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  H ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: nintendo: stop device IO before hid_hw_stop on probe failure\n\nnintendo_hid_probe() calls hid_device_io_start() before joycon_init()\nand joycon_leds_create().  If either fails, the error path jumps to\nerr_close which calls hid_hw_close()/hid_hw_stop() without first calling\nhid_device_io_stop().\n\nhid_hw_stop() does not stop device IO, so hid_input_report() may still\nrun and access driver data that is being torn down, resulting in a\nuse-after-free.\n\nAdd an err_io_stop label that calls hid_device_io_stop() before\nhid_hw_close(), and point the two post-io_start error paths at it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80770",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80770\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80770](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80770)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: nintendo: stop device IO before hid_hw_stop on probe failure\n\nnintendo_hid_probe() calls hid_device_io_start() before joycon_init()\nand joycon_leds_create().  If either fails, the error path jumps to\nerr_close which calls hid_hw_close()/hid_hw_stop() without first calling\nhid_device_io_stop().\n\nhid_hw_stop() does not stop device IO, so hid_input_report() may still\nrun and access driver data that is being torn down, resulting in a\nuse-after-free.\n\nAdd an err_io_stop label that calls hid_device_io_stop() before\nhid_hw_close(), and point the two post-io_start error paths at it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80770**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80770](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80770)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: nintendo: stop device IO before hid_hw_stop on probe failure\n\nnintendo_hid_probe() calls hid_device_io_start() before joycon_init()\nand joycon_leds_create().  If either fails, the error path jumps to\nerr_close which calls hid_hw_close()/hid_hw_stop() without first calling\nhid_device_io_stop().\n\nhid_hw_stop() does not stop device IO, so hid_input_report() may still\nrun and access driver data that is being torn down, resulting in a\nuse-after-free.\n\nAdd an err_io_stop label that calls hid_device_io_stop() before\nhid_hw_close(), and point the two post-io_start error paths at it."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
