            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80774",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  H ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: asus: fix missing hid_is_usb() check\n\nto_usb_interface() can only be used on a hid_device whose parent is really\nUSB; uhid can create devices that identify as being on BUS_USB, but don't\nactually have a USB parent.\nFix the use of to_usb_interface() without a hid_is_usb() check.\n\nI have verified that it is currently possible to trigger a kernel splat due\nto this bug in an ASAN build, and that this commit fixes the issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80774",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80774\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80774](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80774)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: asus: fix missing hid_is_usb() check\n\nto_usb_interface() can only be used on a hid_device whose parent is really\nUSB; uhid can create devices that identify as being on BUS_USB, but don't\nactually have a USB parent.\nFix the use of to_usb_interface() without a hid_is_usb() check.\n\nI have verified that it is currently possible to trigger a kernel splat due\nto this bug in an ASAN build, and that this commit fixes the issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80774**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80774](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80774)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: asus: fix missing hid_is_usb() check\n\nto_usb_interface() can only be used on a hid_device whose parent is really\nUSB; uhid can create devices that identify as being on BUS_USB, but don't\nactually have a USB parent.\nFix the use of to_usb_interface() without a hid_is_usb() check.\n\nI have verified that it is currently possible to trigger a kernel splat due\nto this bug in an ASAN build, and that this commit fixes the issue."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
