            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80801",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  n ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfc: microread: validate target discovery payload lengths\n\nmicroread_target_discovered() parses target discovery payloads from\nskb-\u003edata according to the HCI gate. The fixed field offsets and UID\ncopies were checked only against the destination nfc_target buffers, not\nagainst the actual skb length.\n\nValidate that each gate-specific payload contains the fixed fields and\nUID bytes before reading or copying them."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80801",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80801\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80801](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80801)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfc: microread: validate target discovery payload lengths\n\nmicroread_target_discovered() parses target discovery payloads from\nskb-\u003edata according to the HCI gate. The fixed field offsets and UID\ncopies were checked only against the destination nfc_target buffers, not\nagainst the actual skb length.\n\nValidate that each gate-specific payload contains the fixed fields and\nUID bytes before reading or copying them.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80801**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80801](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80801)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfc: microread: validate target discovery payload lengths\n\nmicroread_target_discovered() parses target discovery payloads from\nskb-\u003edata according to the HCI gate. The fixed field offsets and UID\ncopies were checked only against the destination nfc_target buffers, not\nagainst the actual skb length.\n\nValidate that each gate-specific payload contains the fixed fields and\nUID bytes before reading or copying them."
              },
