            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80814",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  r ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrndis_host: add overflow check in rndis_rx_fixup()\n\nAdd an overflow check to ensure that data_offset + data_len + 8 does not\nwrap, which would enable an OOB read of the USB data buffer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80814",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80814\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80814](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80814)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrndis_host: add overflow check in rndis_rx_fixup()\n\nAdd an overflow check to ensure that data_offset + data_len + 8 does not\nwrap, which would enable an OOB read of the USB data buffer.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80814**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80814](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80814)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrndis_host: add overflow check in rndis_rx_fixup()\n\nAdd an overflow check to ensure that data_offset + data_len + 8 does not\nwrap, which would enable an OOB read of the USB data buffer."
