            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80843",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: xfrm: fix xfrm_state_construct() auth-trunc leak"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfrm: fix xfrm_state_construct() auth-trunc leak\n\nattach_auth_trunc() can allocate x-\u003eaalg while leaving\nx-\u003eprops.aalgo at zero when the selected auth algorithm has no\nsadb_alg_id. One real case is cmac(aes).\n\nxfrm_state_construct() then treats !x-\u003eprops.aalgo as \"no auth\nalgorithm attached yet\" and calls attach_auth(). That overwrites\nx-\u003eaalg and loses the first allocation. Any later failure or teardown\nonly frees the replacement pointer.\n\nCheck whether x-\u003eaalg is already attached instead of inferring that\nstate from x-\u003eprops.aalgo."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80843",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80843\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80843](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80843)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfrm: fix xfrm_state_construct() auth-trunc leak\n\nattach_auth_trunc() can allocate x-\u003eaalg while leaving\nx-\u003eprops.aalgo at zero when the selected auth algorithm has no\nsadb_alg_id. One real case is cmac(aes).\n\nxfrm_state_construct() then treats !x-\u003eprops.aalgo as \"no auth\nalgorithm attached yet\" and calls attach_auth(). That overwrites\nx-\u003eaalg and loses the first allocation. Any later failure or teardown\nonly frees the replacement pointer.\n\nCheck whether x-\u003eaalg is already attached instead of inferring that\nstate from x-\u003eprops.aalgo.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80843**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80843](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80843)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfrm: fix xfrm_state_construct() auth-trunc leak\n\nattach_auth_trunc() can allocate x-\u003eaalg while leaving\nx-\u003eprops.aalgo at zero when the selected auth algorithm has no\nsadb_alg_id. One real case is cmac(aes).\n\nxfrm_state_construct() then treats !x-\u003eprops.aalgo as \"no auth\nalgorithm attached yet\" and calls attach_auth(). That overwrites\nx-\u003eaalg and loses the first allocation. Any later failure or teardown\nonly frees the replacement pointer.\n\nCheck whether x-\u003eaalg is already attached instead of inferring that\nstate from x-\u003eprops.aalgo."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
