            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80963",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: dm-stats: fix a crash if allocation of per-cpu data fails"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-stats: fix a crash if allocation of per-cpu data fails\n\nIf \"dm_kvzalloc(percpu_alloc_size, cpu_to_node(cpu))\" fails, the code\njumps to the \"out\" label and calls dm_stat_free. dm_stat_free does\n\"for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) { dm_kvfree(s-\u003estat_percpu[cpu][0].histogram,\ns-\u003ehistogram_alloc_size);\", which crashes with NULL pointer dereference\nif s-\u003estat_percpu[cpu] is NULL.\n\nThis commit fixes the bug by testing s-\u003estat_percpu[cpu] for NULL before\nusing it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80963",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80963\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80963](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80963)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-stats: fix a crash if allocation of per-cpu data fails\n\nIf \"dm_kvzalloc(percpu_alloc_size, cpu_to_node(cpu))\" fails, the code\njumps to the \"out\" label and calls dm_stat_free. dm_stat_free does\n\"for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) { dm_kvfree(s-\u003estat_percpu[cpu][0].histogram,\ns-\u003ehistogram_alloc_size);\", which crashes with NULL pointer dereference\nif s-\u003estat_percpu[cpu] is NULL.\n\nThis commit fixes the bug by testing s-\u003estat_percpu[cpu] for NULL before\nusing it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80963**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80963](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80963)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-stats: fix a crash if allocation of per-cpu data fails\n\nIf \"dm_kvzalloc(percpu_alloc_size, cpu_to_node(cpu))\" fails, the code\njumps to the \"out\" label and calls dm_stat_free. dm_stat_free does\n\"for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) { dm_kvfree(s-\u003estat_percpu[cpu][0].histogram,\ns-\u003ehistogram_alloc_size);\", which crashes with NULL pointer dereference\nif s-\u003estat_percpu[cpu] is NULL.\n\nThis commit fixes the bug by testing s-\u003estat_percpu[cpu] for NULL before\nusing it."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
