            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80966",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ALSA: portman2x4: Check card index validity at probe"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: portman2x4: Check card index validity at probe\n\nAlthough portman2x4 driver has a check of the given devptr-\u003eid value,\nit doesn't check for a negative id, which is often given as \"none\" or\nsuch value when bound via sysfs.  This may lead to OOB access for\nindex[] and other parameters.\n\nAdd a sanity check for the card index and warn/correct it if it's a\nvalue out of the range."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80966",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80966\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80966](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80966)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: portman2x4: Check card index validity at probe\n\nAlthough portman2x4 driver has a check of the given devptr-\u003eid value,\nit doesn't check for a negative id, which is often given as \"none\" or\nsuch value when bound via sysfs.  This may lead to OOB access for\nindex[] and other parameters.\n\nAdd a sanity check for the card index and warn/correct it if it's a\nvalue out of the range.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80966**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80966](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80966)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: portman2x4: Check card index validity at probe\n\nAlthough portman2x4 driver has a check of the given devptr-\u003eid value,\nit doesn't check for a negative id, which is often given as \"none\" or\nsuch value when bound via sysfs.  This may lead to OOB access for\nindex[] and other parameters.\n\nAdd a sanity check for the card index and warn/correct it if it's a\nvalue out of the range."
