            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89502",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ring-buffer: Free cpu_buffer::free_page with subbuf_order"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nring-buffer: Free cpu_buffer::free_page with subbuf_order\n\nWhen sub-buffers use an order greater than 0, cpu_buffer-\u003efree_page is\nallocated with subbuf_order. Use the correct order for\ncpu_buffer-\u003efree_page."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89502",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89502\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89502](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89502)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nring-buffer: Free cpu_buffer::free_page with subbuf_order\n\nWhen sub-buffers use an order greater than 0, cpu_buffer-\u003efree_page is\nallocated with subbuf_order. Use the correct order for\ncpu_buffer-\u003efree_page.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89502**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89502](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89502)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nring-buffer: Free cpu_buffer::free_page with subbuf_order\n\nWhen sub-buffers use an order greater than 0, cpu_buffer-\u003efree_page is\nallocated with subbuf_order. Use the correct order for\ncpu_buffer-\u003efree_page."
              },
              "properties": {
