            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89510",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: RDMA/cxgb4: Cancel reg_work before freeing device on remove"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/cxgb4: Cancel reg_work before freeing device on remove\n\nc4iw_uld_state_change() queues reg_work to register the RDMA device.\nc4iw_remove() can free ctx-\u003edev while this work is pending or running,\nleaving c4iw_register_device() accessing the freed device.\n\nCancel reg_work before removing the device.  The registration work can\ntear down ctx-\u003edev when registration fails, so do not unregister or\ndeallocate it again in that case.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89510",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89510\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89510](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89510)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/cxgb4: Cancel reg_work before freeing device on remove\n\nc4iw_uld_state_change() queues reg_work to register the RDMA device.\nc4iw_remove() can free ctx-\u003edev while this work is pending or running,\nleaving c4iw_register_device() accessing the freed device.\n\nCancel reg_work before removing the device.  The registration work can\ntear down ctx-\u003edev when registration fails, so do not unregister or\ndeallocate it again in that case.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89510**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89510](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89510)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/cxgb4: Cancel reg_work before freeing device on remove\n\nc4iw_uld_state_change() queues reg_work to register the RDMA device.\nc4iw_remove() can free ctx-\u003edev while this work is pending or running,\nleaving c4iw_register_device() accessing the freed device.\n\nCancel reg_work before removing the device.  The registration work can\ntear down ctx-\u003edev when registration fails, so do not unregister or\ndeallocate it again in that case.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
