            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89512",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: remoteproc: scp: Fix device reference leak on failed lookup"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nremoteproc: scp: Fix device reference leak on failed lookup\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken to the SCP device when attempting\nto look up its driver data before the driver has been bound.\n\nNote that holding a reference to a device does not prevent its driver\ndata from going away."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89512",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89512\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89512](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89512)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nremoteproc: scp: Fix device reference leak on failed lookup\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken to the SCP device when attempting\nto look up its driver data before the driver has been bound.\n\nNote that holding a reference to a device does not prevent its driver\ndata from going away.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89512**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89512](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89512)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nremoteproc: scp: Fix device reference leak on failed lookup\n\nMake sure to drop the reference taken to the SCP device when attempting\nto look up its driver data before the driver has been bound.\n\nNote that holding a reference to a device does not prevent its driver\ndata from going away."
              },
