            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89553",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: nouveau/gem: reserve the bo in the info ioctl around the vma lookup"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnouveau/gem: reserve the bo in the info ioctl around the vma lookup\n\nIn the non-uvmm path, there could be a race between the info lookup\nfinding the vma, and the gem close path closing the vma leading\nto a use-after-free.\n\nSpotted with the help of Opus 4.6."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89553",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89553\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89553](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89553)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnouveau/gem: reserve the bo in the info ioctl around the vma lookup\n\nIn the non-uvmm path, there could be a race between the info lookup\nfinding the vma, and the gem close path closing the vma leading\nto a use-after-free.\n\nSpotted with the help of Opus 4.6.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89553**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89553](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89553)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnouveau/gem: reserve the bo in the info ioctl around the vma lookup\n\nIn the non-uvmm path, there could be a race between the info lookup\nfinding the vma, and the gem close path closing the vma leading\nto a use-after-free.\n\nSpotted with the help of Opus 4.6."
              },
