            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89575",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: dm raid1: reserve space for NUL-terminator in build_constructor_string()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm raid1: reserve space for NUL-terminator in build_constructor_string()\n\nReserve space for the termination NUL after the maximum 20 decimal\ndigits of a long long value to avoid buffer overflow in sprintf()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89575",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89575\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89575](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89575)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm raid1: reserve space for NUL-terminator in build_constructor_string()\n\nReserve space for the termination NUL after the maximum 20 decimal\ndigits of a long long value to avoid buffer overflow in sprintf().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89575**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89575](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89575)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm raid1: reserve space for NUL-terminator in build_constructor_string()\n\nReserve space for the termination NUL after the maximum 20 decimal\ndigits of a long long value to avoid buffer overflow in sprintf()."
              },
              "properties": {
