            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89609",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ecryptfs: hold msg ctx list lock when cleaning daemon queue"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\necryptfs: hold msg ctx list lock when cleaning daemon queue\n\necryptfs_exorcise_daemon() drops queued messages from a dying daemon\nwithout holding ecryptfs_msg_ctx_lists_mux, but\necryptfs_msg_ctx_alloc_to_free() requires that lock.\n\nTake the list lock while moving the queued contexts back to the free\nlist to avoid racing with other global msg ctx list users."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89609",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89609\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89609](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89609)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\necryptfs: hold msg ctx list lock when cleaning daemon queue\n\necryptfs_exorcise_daemon() drops queued messages from a dying daemon\nwithout holding ecryptfs_msg_ctx_lists_mux, but\necryptfs_msg_ctx_alloc_to_free() requires that lock.\n\nTake the list lock while moving the queued contexts back to the free\nlist to avoid racing with other global msg ctx list users.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89609**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89609](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89609)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\necryptfs: hold msg ctx list lock when cleaning daemon queue\n\necryptfs_exorcise_daemon() drops queued messages from a dying daemon\nwithout holding ecryptfs_msg_ctx_lists_mux, but\necryptfs_msg_ctx_alloc_to_free() requires that lock.\n\nTake the list lock while moving the queued contexts back to the free\nlist to avoid racing with other global msg ctx list users."
              },
              "properties": {
