            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89693",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: nfsd: check nfsd4_acl_to_attr() return value in nfsd4_create()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: check nfsd4_acl_to_attr() return value in nfsd4_create()\n\nnfsd4_create() stores the return value of nfsd4_acl_to_attr() in\nstatus, but the switch(create-\u003ecr_type) block unconditionally\noverwrites it in every branch. ACL translation errors are silently\ndiscarded, and the CREATE proceeds without the requested ACL.\n\nAdd an early exit check after nfsd4_acl_to_attr(), matching the\npattern already used in nfsd4_setattr().\n\n[ cel: prefer NFS4ERR_BADTYPE over NFS4ERR_ATTRNOTSUPP ]"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89693",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89693\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89693](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89693)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: check nfsd4_acl_to_attr() return value in nfsd4_create()\n\nnfsd4_create() stores the return value of nfsd4_acl_to_attr() in\nstatus, but the switch(create-\u003ecr_type) block unconditionally\noverwrites it in every branch. ACL translation errors are silently\ndiscarded, and the CREATE proceeds without the requested ACL.\n\nAdd an early exit check after nfsd4_acl_to_attr(), matching the\npattern already used in nfsd4_setattr().\n\n[ cel: prefer NFS4ERR_BADTYPE over NFS4ERR_ATTRNOTSUPP ]",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89693**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89693](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89693)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: check nfsd4_acl_to_attr() return value in nfsd4_create()\n\nnfsd4_create() stores the return value of nfsd4_acl_to_attr() in\nstatus, but the switch(create-\u003ecr_type) block unconditionally\noverwrites it in every branch. ACL translation errors are silently\ndiscarded, and the CREATE proceeds without the requested ACL.\n\nAdd an early exit check after nfsd4_acl_to_attr(), matching the\npattern already used in nfsd4_setattr().\n\n[ cel: prefer NFS4ERR_BADTYPE over NFS4ERR_ATTRNOTSUPP ]"
              },
