            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89694",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: nfsd: check client ownership when cancelling a copy-notify stateid"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: check client ownership when cancelling a copy-notify stateid\n\nOn the OFFLOAD_CANCEL path (clp != NULL), manage_cpntf_state() freed the\ntarget cpntf state without checking ownership. The lookup key\nst-\u003esi_opaque.so_id is allocated cyclically (guessable) and the embedded\nclientid is the fixed per-net nn-\u003es2s_cp_cl_id, so any authenticated\nNFSv4.2 client could cancel and free another client's copy-notify\nstateid.\n\nCompare the creating clientid recorded in state-\u003ecp_p_clid against the\nrequesting client's cl_clientid and return nfserr_bad_stateid on a\nmismatch instead of freeing the entry."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89694",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89694\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89694](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89694)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: check client ownership when cancelling a copy-notify stateid\n\nOn the OFFLOAD_CANCEL path (clp != NULL), manage_cpntf_state() freed the\ntarget cpntf state without checking ownership. The lookup key\nst-\u003esi_opaque.so_id is allocated cyclically (guessable) and the embedded\nclientid is the fixed per-net nn-\u003es2s_cp_cl_id, so any authenticated\nNFSv4.2 client could cancel and free another client's copy-notify\nstateid.\n\nCompare the creating clientid recorded in state-\u003ecp_p_clid against the\nrequesting client's cl_clientid and return nfserr_bad_stateid on a\nmismatch instead of freeing the entry.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89694**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89694](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89694)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: check client ownership when cancelling a copy-notify stateid\n\nOn the OFFLOAD_CANCEL path (clp != NULL), manage_cpntf_state() freed the\ntarget cpntf state without checking ownership. The lookup key\nst-\u003esi_opaque.so_id is allocated cyclically (guessable) and the embedded\nclientid is the fixed per-net nn-\u003es2s_cp_cl_id, so any authenticated\nNFSv4.2 client could cancel and free another client's copy-notify\nstateid.\n\nCompare the creating clientid recorded in state-\u003ecp_p_clid against the\nrequesting client's cl_clientid and return nfserr_bad_stateid on a\nmismatch instead of freeing the entry."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
