            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89730",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: fpga: altera-cvp: Avoid out-of-bounds read in trailing byte write"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfpga: altera-cvp: Avoid out-of-bounds read in trailing byte write\n\nThe trailing byte path in altera_cvp_send_block() dereferences a u32\npointer even when only 1-3 bytes remain in the input buffer. If the buffer\nends at a page or scatterlist boundary, this can read past the valid image\ndata and fault.\n\nCopy the remaining bytes into a zero-initialized u32 before writing the\nfinal word so only valid bytes are read from the input buffer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89730",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89730\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89730](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89730)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfpga: altera-cvp: Avoid out-of-bounds read in trailing byte write\n\nThe trailing byte path in altera_cvp_send_block() dereferences a u32\npointer even when only 1-3 bytes remain in the input buffer. If the buffer\nends at a page or scatterlist boundary, this can read past the valid image\ndata and fault.\n\nCopy the remaining bytes into a zero-initialized u32 before writing the\nfinal word so only valid bytes are read from the input buffer.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89730**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89730](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89730)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfpga: altera-cvp: Avoid out-of-bounds read in trailing byte write\n\nThe trailing byte path in altera_cvp_send_block() dereferences a u32\npointer even when only 1-3 bytes remain in the input buffer. If the buffer\nends at a page or scatterlist boundary, this can read past the valid image\ndata and fault.\n\nCopy the remaining bytes into a zero-initialized u32 before writing the\nfinal word so only valid bytes are read from the input buffer."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
