            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89751",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: x86/tdx: Fix off-by-one in port I/O handling"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nx86/tdx: Fix off-by-one in port I/O handling\n\nhandle_in() and handle_out() in arch/x86/coco/tdx/tdx.c use:\n\n    u64 mask = GENMASK(BITS_PER_BYTE * size, 0);\n\nGENMASK(h, l) includes bit h. For size=1 (INB), this produces\nGENMASK(8, 0) = 0x1FF (9 bits) instead of GENMASK(7, 0) = 0xFF (8\nbits). The mask is one bit too wide for all I/O sizes.\n\nFix the mask calculation."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89751",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89751\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89751](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89751)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nx86/tdx: Fix off-by-one in port I/O handling\n\nhandle_in() and handle_out() in arch/x86/coco/tdx/tdx.c use:\n\n    u64 mask = GENMASK(BITS_PER_BYTE * size, 0);\n\nGENMASK(h, l) includes bit h. For size=1 (INB), this produces\nGENMASK(8, 0) = 0x1FF (9 bits) instead of GENMASK(7, 0) = 0xFF (8\nbits). The mask is one bit too wide for all I/O sizes.\n\nFix the mask calculation.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89751**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89751](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89751)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nx86/tdx: Fix off-by-one in port I/O handling\n\nhandle_in() and handle_out() in arch/x86/coco/tdx/tdx.c use:\n\n    u64 mask = GENMASK(BITS_PER_BYTE * size, 0);\n\nGENMASK(h, l) includes bit h. For size=1 (INB), this produces\nGENMASK(8, 0) = 0x1FF (9 bits) instead of GENMASK(7, 0) = 0xFF (8\nbits). The mask is one bit too wide for all I/O sizes.\n\nFix the mask calculation."
              },
