            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89792",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  k ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: prevent out-of-bounds reads in share config responses\n\nValidate IPC share configuration payload sizes before consuming\nvariable-length fields. Bound veto list parsing and account for\nthe separator byte when deriving the path length."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89792",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89792\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89792](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89792)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: prevent out-of-bounds reads in share config responses\n\nValidate IPC share configuration payload sizes before consuming\nvariable-length fields. Bound veto list parsing and account for\nthe separator byte when deriving the path length.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89792**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89792](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89792)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: prevent out-of-bounds reads in share config responses\n\nValidate IPC share configuration payload sizes before consuming\nvariable-length fields. Bound veto list parsing and account for\nthe separator byte when deriving the path length."
