            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89817",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  d ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/gud: NUL-terminate TV mode names read from the device\n\ngud_connector_add_tv_mode() reads a buffer of fixed-size mode names from\nthe USB device and passes pointers into it to\ndrm_mode_create_tv_properties_legacy(), which calls strlen() on each one.\nNothing guarantees the device NUL-terminates a name, so strlen() can run\npast the end of a slot and, for the last mode, past the end of the\nallocation.\n\nTerminate each name at the end of its slot before use."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89817",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89817\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89817](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89817)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/gud: NUL-terminate TV mode names read from the device\n\ngud_connector_add_tv_mode() reads a buffer of fixed-size mode names from\nthe USB device and passes pointers into it to\ndrm_mode_create_tv_properties_legacy(), which calls strlen() on each one.\nNothing guarantees the device NUL-terminates a name, so strlen() can run\npast the end of a slot and, for the last mode, past the end of the\nallocation.\n\nTerminate each name at the end of its slot before use.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89817**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89817](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89817)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/gud: NUL-terminate TV mode names read from the device\n\ngud_connector_add_tv_mode() reads a buffer of fixed-size mode names from\nthe USB device and passes pointers into it to\ndrm_mode_create_tv_properties_legacy(), which calls strlen() on each one.\nNothing guarantees the device NUL-terminates a name, so strlen() can run\npast the end of a slot and, for the last mode, past the end of the\nallocation.\n\nTerminate each name at the end of its slot before use."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
