            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89821",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  d ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: avoid divide-by-zero in __is_lut_linear()\n\n__is_lut_linear() computes the expected value of each entry with\n\n\texpected = i * MAX_DRM_LUT_VALUE / (size - 1);\n\nIf it is ever called with a single-entry LUT, size - 1 is zero and the\nkernel takes a divide error (#DE). A LUT with fewer than two entries\ncannot describe a linear mapping anyway, so return false early instead\nof dividing by zero."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89821",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89821\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89821](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89821)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: avoid divide-by-zero in __is_lut_linear()\n\n__is_lut_linear() computes the expected value of each entry with\n\n\texpected = i * MAX_DRM_LUT_VALUE / (size - 1);\n\nIf it is ever called with a single-entry LUT, size - 1 is zero and the\nkernel takes a divide error (#DE). A LUT with fewer than two entries\ncannot describe a linear mapping anyway, so return false early instead\nof dividing by zero.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89821**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89821](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89821)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: avoid divide-by-zero in __is_lut_linear()\n\n__is_lut_linear() computes the expected value of each entry with\n\n\texpected = i * MAX_DRM_LUT_VALUE / (size - 1);\n\nIf it is ever called with a single-entry LUT, size - 1 is zero and the\nkernel takes a divide error (#DE). A LUT with fewer than two entries\ncannot describe a linear mapping anyway, so return false early instead\nof dividing by zero."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
