            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89897",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  m ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: cec: Serialize exclusive follower delivery\n\ncec_receive_notify() reads the exclusive follower pointer without the\nadapter lock. Serialize the no-follower check and message delivery\nagainst mode changes and release."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89897",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89897\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89897](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89897)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: cec: Serialize exclusive follower delivery\n\ncec_receive_notify() reads the exclusive follower pointer without the\nadapter lock. Serialize the no-follower check and message delivery\nagainst mode changes and release.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89897**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89897](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89897)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: cec: Serialize exclusive follower delivery\n\ncec_receive_notify() reads the exclusive follower pointer without the\nadapter lock. Serialize the no-follower check and message delivery\nagainst mode changes and release."
              },
