            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89904",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  L ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: Fix acpi_package_ids[] array overflow\n\nWith LoongArch virt machine, a typical setting is one core per socket,\nthere will max 256 sockets (packages) on one VM. With PPTT acpi table,\narray acpi_package_ids[] will be overflowed.\n\nHere change the array size of acpi_package_ids[] with the max value of\nMAX_PACKAGES and KVM_MAX_VCPUS."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89904",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89904\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89904](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89904)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: Fix acpi_package_ids[] array overflow\n\nWith LoongArch virt machine, a typical setting is one core per socket,\nthere will max 256 sockets (packages) on one VM. With PPTT acpi table,\narray acpi_package_ids[] will be overflowed.\n\nHere change the array size of acpi_package_ids[] with the max value of\nMAX_PACKAGES and KVM_MAX_VCPUS.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89904**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89904](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89904)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: Fix acpi_package_ids[] array overflow\n\nWith LoongArch virt machine, a typical setting is one core per socket,\nthere will max 256 sockets (packages) on one VM. With PPTT acpi table,\narray acpi_package_ids[] will be overflowed.\n\nHere change the array size of acpi_package_ids[] with the max value of\nMAX_PACKAGES and KVM_MAX_VCPUS."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89906",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  L ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: BPF: Refactor jump offset calculation in tail call\n\nThe old macro-based jmp_offset calculation derives the jump distance\nfrom a stale prior-pass code stride, which can lead to wrong branch\noffsets and soft lockups under extra JIT passes.\n\nFix this by calculating the offset directly on the absolute target:\n\"ctx-\u003eoffset[insn + 1] - ctx-\u003eidx\".\n\nTo avoid a false 16-bit range check abort during size estimation, add\na \"ctx-\u003eimage == NULL\" guard to inject a safe dummy offset."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89906",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89906\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89906](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89906)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: BPF: Refactor jump offset calculation in tail call\n\nThe old macro-based jmp_offset calculation derives the jump distance\nfrom a stale prior-pass code stride, which can lead to wrong branch\noffsets and soft lockups under extra JIT passes.\n\nFix this by calculating the offset directly on the absolute target:\n\"ctx-\u003eoffset[insn + 1] - ctx-\u003eidx\".\n\nTo avoid a false 16-bit range check abort during size estimation, add\na \"ctx-\u003eimage == NULL\" guard to inject a safe dummy offset.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89906**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89906](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89906)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nLoongArch: BPF: Refactor jump offset calculation in tail call\n\nThe old macro-based jmp_offset calculation derives the jump distance\nfrom a stale prior-pass code stride, which can lead to wrong branch\noffsets and soft lockups under extra JIT passes.\n\nFix this by calculating the offset directly on the absolute target:\n\"ctx-\u003eoffset[insn + 1] - ctx-\u003eidx\".\n\nTo avoid a false 16-bit range check abort during size estimation, add\na \"ctx-\u003eimage == NULL\" guard to inject a safe dummy offset."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
