            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89937",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  i ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: chemical: sgp30: Handle IAQ thread creation failure\n\nkthread_run() can fail and return an error pointer, but sgp_probe() stores\nit and returns success, so the device is registered without its IAQ thread\nand sgp_remove() later passes the error pointer to kthread_stop(). Return\nthe error from probe instead."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89937",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89937\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89937](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89937)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: chemical: sgp30: Handle IAQ thread creation failure\n\nkthread_run() can fail and return an error pointer, but sgp_probe() stores\nit and returns success, so the device is registered without its IAQ thread\nand sgp_remove() later passes the error pointer to kthread_stop(). Return\nthe error from probe instead.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89937**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89937](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89937)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: chemical: sgp30: Handle IAQ thread creation failure\n\nkthread_run() can fail and return an error pointer, but sgp_probe() stores\nit and returns success, so the device is registered without its IAQ thread\nand sgp_remove() later passes the error pointer to kthread_stop(). Return\nthe error from probe instead."
              },
              "properties": {
