            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89949",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  b ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: dat: avoid unaligned fault in IP extraction\n\nIndependent of the alignment of the ARP packet in the SKB, either the\nbatadv_arp_ip_src or the batadv_arp_ip_dst will have an unaligned access\n(on HW without native unaligned read support).\n\nUse get_unaligned() to handle this properly on all architectures."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89949",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89949\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89949](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89949)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: dat: avoid unaligned fault in IP extraction\n\nIndependent of the alignment of the ARP packet in the SKB, either the\nbatadv_arp_ip_src or the batadv_arp_ip_dst will have an unaligned access\n(on HW without native unaligned read support).\n\nUse get_unaligned() to handle this properly on all architectures.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89949**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89949](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89949)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: dat: avoid unaligned fault in IP extraction\n\nIndependent of the alignment of the ARP packet in the SKB, either the\nbatadv_arp_ip_src or the batadv_arp_ip_dst will have an unaligned access\n(on HW without native unaligned read support).\n\nUse get_unaligned() to handle this properly on all architectures."
              },
              "properties": {
