            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90019",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  u ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: fix null pointer dereference in usb_put_function_instance()\n\nusb_put_function_instance() attempts to dereference fd inside fi struct\nto get mod in uvc_alloc_inst() error path. However, fd is not allocated\nuntil later in try_get_usb_function_instance() after allocating fi in\nuvc_alloc_inst() and thus guranteed to be null in error path. Fix this\nby adding a null check for fi-\u003efd that returns if fd is null."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90019",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90019\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90019](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90019)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: fix null pointer dereference in usb_put_function_instance()\n\nusb_put_function_instance() attempts to dereference fd inside fi struct\nto get mod in uvc_alloc_inst() error path. However, fd is not allocated\nuntil later in try_get_usb_function_instance() after allocating fi in\nuvc_alloc_inst() and thus guranteed to be null in error path. Fix this\nby adding a null check for fi-\u003efd that returns if fd is null.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90019**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90019](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90019)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: fix null pointer dereference in usb_put_function_instance()\n\nusb_put_function_instance() attempts to dereference fd inside fi struct\nto get mod in uvc_alloc_inst() error path. However, fd is not allocated\nuntil later in try_get_usb_function_instance() after allocating fi in\nuvc_alloc_inst() and thus guranteed to be null in error path. Fix this\nby adding a null check for fi-\u003efd that returns if fd is null."
              },
