            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90026",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  u ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic: cancel reset_work on stop\n\npdphy_stop() disables IRQs but leaves reset_work pending.  If the IRQ\nhandler schedules it just before disable_irq(), the work runs after\nremove() frees the struct via devm.\n\nCall cancel_work_sync() after disabling IRQs to close the window.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90026",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90026\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90026](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90026)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic: cancel reset_work on stop\n\npdphy_stop() disables IRQs but leaves reset_work pending.  If the IRQ\nhandler schedules it just before disable_irq(), the work runs after\nremove() frees the struct via devm.\n\nCall cancel_work_sync() after disabling IRQs to close the window.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90026**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90026](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90026)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic: cancel reset_work on stop\n\npdphy_stop() disables IRQs but leaves reset_work pending.  If the IRQ\nhandler schedules it just before disable_irq(), the work runs after\nremove() frees the struct via devm.\n\nCall cancel_work_sync() after disabling IRQs to close the window.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool."
              },
              "properties": {
