            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90066",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: samples/ftrace: Fix kthread_stop() on ERR_PTR in ftrace-direct-multi-modify"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsamples/ftrace: Fix kthread_stop() on ERR_PTR in ftrace-direct-multi-modify\n\nftrace_direct_multi_init() assigns kthread_run()'s return value to\nsimple_tsk without an IS_ERR() check. When kthread_run() fails it\nreturns ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM), but init still returns 0, so the module loads\nwith simple_tsk holding an error pointer. On unload,\nftrace_direct_multi_exit() then passes that ERR_PTR to kthread_stop(),\nleading to a null-pointer-dereference.\n\nCheck the return value of kthread_run() with IS_ERR(); on failure,\nunregister the ftrace direct call and propagate the error code."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90066",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90066\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90066](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90066)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsamples/ftrace: Fix kthread_stop() on ERR_PTR in ftrace-direct-multi-modify\n\nftrace_direct_multi_init() assigns kthread_run()'s return value to\nsimple_tsk without an IS_ERR() check. When kthread_run() fails it\nreturns ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM), but init still returns 0, so the module loads\nwith simple_tsk holding an error pointer. On unload,\nftrace_direct_multi_exit() then passes that ERR_PTR to kthread_stop(),\nleading to a null-pointer-dereference.\n\nCheck the return value of kthread_run() with IS_ERR(); on failure,\nunregister the ftrace direct call and propagate the error code.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90066**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90066](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90066)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsamples/ftrace: Fix kthread_stop() on ERR_PTR in ftrace-direct-multi-modify\n\nftrace_direct_multi_init() assigns kthread_run()'s return value to\nsimple_tsk without an IS_ERR() check. When kthread_run() fails it\nreturns ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM), but init still returns 0, so the module loads\nwith simple_tsk holding an error pointer. On unload,\nftrace_direct_multi_exit() then passes that ERR_PTR to kthread_stop(),\nleading to a null-pointer-dereference.\n\nCheck the return value of kthread_run() with IS_ERR(); on failure,\nunregister the ftrace direct call and propagate the error code."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
