            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90074",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net/sched: fq_pie: clamp default quantum to avoid signed overflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sched: fq_pie: clamp default quantum to avoid signed overflow\n\nfq_pie_init() sets q-\u003equantum = psched_mtu(qdisc_dev(sch)) without\nclamping. A device with a huge MTU (e.g. dummy with max_mtu == 0\naccepting MTU 2147483634) makes psched_mtu() return 0x80000000, which\noverflows the signed flow-\u003edeficit to INT_MIN in fq_pie_qdisc_dequeue(),\ncausing an infinite loop and soft lockup. Emulate fq_pie_policy which\nis already bounded to [1, 1 \u003c\u003c 20]; clamp the default to [256, 1 \u003c\u003c 20].\n256 matches fq_codel's floor and is a sane minimum for a DRR quantum.\n\nConditions to recreate the bug: a device whose MTU (plus\nhard_header_len) wraps psched_mtu() into the sign bit (e.g. a dummy\ndevice with max_mtu == 0 accepting MTU 2147483634). Requires\nCAP_NET_ADMIN in a user namespace."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90074",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90074\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90074](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90074)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sched: fq_pie: clamp default quantum to avoid signed overflow\n\nfq_pie_init() sets q-\u003equantum = psched_mtu(qdisc_dev(sch)) without\nclamping. A device with a huge MTU (e.g. dummy with max_mtu == 0\naccepting MTU 2147483634) makes psched_mtu() return 0x80000000, which\noverflows the signed flow-\u003edeficit to INT_MIN in fq_pie_qdisc_dequeue(),\ncausing an infinite loop and soft lockup. Emulate fq_pie_policy which\nis already bounded to [1, 1 \u003c\u003c 20]; clamp the default to [256, 1 \u003c\u003c 20].\n256 matches fq_codel's floor and is a sane minimum for a DRR quantum.\n\nConditions to recreate the bug: a device whose MTU (plus\nhard_header_len) wraps psched_mtu() into the sign bit (e.g. a dummy\ndevice with max_mtu == 0 accepting MTU 2147483634). Requires\nCAP_NET_ADMIN in a user namespace.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90074**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90074](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90074)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sched: fq_pie: clamp default quantum to avoid signed overflow\n\nfq_pie_init() sets q-\u003equantum = psched_mtu(qdisc_dev(sch)) without\nclamping. A device with a huge MTU (e.g. dummy with max_mtu == 0\naccepting MTU 2147483634) makes psched_mtu() return 0x80000000, which\noverflows the signed flow-\u003edeficit to INT_MIN in fq_pie_qdisc_dequeue(),\ncausing an infinite loop and soft lockup. Emulate fq_pie_policy which\nis already bounded to [1, 1 \u003c\u003c 20]; clamp the default to [256, 1 \u003c\u003c 20].\n256 matches fq_codel's floor and is a sane minimum for a DRR quantum.\n\nConditions to recreate the bug: a device whose MTU (plus\nhard_header_len) wraps psched_mtu() into the sign bit (e.g. a dummy\ndevice with max_mtu == 0 accepting MTU 2147483634). Requires\nCAP_NET_ADMIN in a user namespace."
              },
