            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90101",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: bnxt_en: Fix call to hardware monitoring event handler"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbnxt_en: Fix call to hardware monitoring event handler\n\nThe first parameter of hwmon_notify_event() is supposed to be the hardware\nmonitoring device. The bnxt driver calls it with the platform device as\nfirst parameter instead. This API break results in undefined behavior and\nmay result in a crash.\n\nPass the hardware monitoring device as parameter instead to fix the\nproblem."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90101",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90101\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90101](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90101)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbnxt_en: Fix call to hardware monitoring event handler\n\nThe first parameter of hwmon_notify_event() is supposed to be the hardware\nmonitoring device. The bnxt driver calls it with the platform device as\nfirst parameter instead. This API break results in undefined behavior and\nmay result in a crash.\n\nPass the hardware monitoring device as parameter instead to fix the\nproblem.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90101**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90101](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90101)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbnxt_en: Fix call to hardware monitoring event handler\n\nThe first parameter of hwmon_notify_event() is supposed to be the hardware\nmonitoring device. The bnxt driver calls it with the platform device as\nfirst parameter instead. This API break results in undefined behavior and\nmay result in a crash.\n\nPass the hardware monitoring device as parameter instead to fix the\nproblem."
              },
