            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90128",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: vdpa/mlx5: fix wrong list iterated in add_direct_chain error path"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvdpa/mlx5: fix wrong list iterated in add_direct_chain error path\n\nIn add_direct_chain(), newly allocated direct MR entries are added to\nthe local list 'tmp', which is spliced into mr-\u003ehead only on success.\nOn the error path, the cleanup loop was incorrectly iterating over\nmr-\u003ehead instead of tmp.\n\nFix by iterating over 'tmp' in the err_alloc cleanup path."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90128",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90128\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90128](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90128)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvdpa/mlx5: fix wrong list iterated in add_direct_chain error path\n\nIn add_direct_chain(), newly allocated direct MR entries are added to\nthe local list 'tmp', which is spliced into mr-\u003ehead only on success.\nOn the error path, the cleanup loop was incorrectly iterating over\nmr-\u003ehead instead of tmp.\n\nFix by iterating over 'tmp' in the err_alloc cleanup path.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90128**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90128](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90128)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvdpa/mlx5: fix wrong list iterated in add_direct_chain error path\n\nIn add_direct_chain(), newly allocated direct MR entries are added to\nthe local list 'tmp', which is spliced into mr-\u003ehead only on success.\nOn the error path, the cleanup loop was incorrectly iterating over\nmr-\u003ehead instead of tmp.\n\nFix by iterating over 'tmp' in the err_alloc cleanup path."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
