            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90273",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: coresight: etm4x: missing cscfg_csdev_disable_active_config() in perf enable"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncoresight: etm4x: missing cscfg_csdev_disable_active_config() in perf enable\n\nIn the perf enable path, there are missing cases where\ncscfg_csdev_disable_active_config() is not called:\n\n  - Branch broadcast is selected but not supported by the hardware\n  - etm4_enable_hw() fails\n\nThis can lead to a leak of config_desc-\u003eactive_cnt.\nFix this by properly calling cscfg_csdev_disable_active_config()\nin these error paths."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90273",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90273\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90273](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90273)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncoresight: etm4x: missing cscfg_csdev_disable_active_config() in perf enable\n\nIn the perf enable path, there are missing cases where\ncscfg_csdev_disable_active_config() is not called:\n\n  - Branch broadcast is selected but not supported by the hardware\n  - etm4_enable_hw() fails\n\nThis can lead to a leak of config_desc-\u003eactive_cnt.\nFix this by properly calling cscfg_csdev_disable_active_config()\nin these error paths.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90273**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90273](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90273)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncoresight: etm4x: missing cscfg_csdev_disable_active_config() in perf enable\n\nIn the perf enable path, there are missing cases where\ncscfg_csdev_disable_active_config() is not called:\n\n  - Branch broadcast is selected but not supported by the hardware\n  - etm4_enable_hw() fails\n\nThis can lead to a leak of config_desc-\u003eactive_cnt.\nFix this by properly calling cscfg_csdev_disable_active_config()\nin these error paths."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
