            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90287",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: phy: sunplus: fix error handling in sp_uphy_init()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nphy: sunplus: fix error handling in sp_uphy_init()\n\nFix the error paths of sp_uphy_init() to undo exactly what each stage\ndid: return directly if clk_prepare_enable() fails, release only the clock\nif reset_control_deassert() fails, and jump to err_reset if\nupdate_disc_vol() fails so the clock and reset are not leaked."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90287",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90287\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90287](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90287)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nphy: sunplus: fix error handling in sp_uphy_init()\n\nFix the error paths of sp_uphy_init() to undo exactly what each stage\ndid: return directly if clk_prepare_enable() fails, release only the clock\nif reset_control_deassert() fails, and jump to err_reset if\nupdate_disc_vol() fails so the clock and reset are not leaked.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90287**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90287](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90287)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nphy: sunplus: fix error handling in sp_uphy_init()\n\nFix the error paths of sp_uphy_init() to undo exactly what each stage\ndid: return directly if clk_prepare_enable() fails, release only the clock\nif reset_control_deassert() fails, and jump to err_reset if\nupdate_disc_vol() fails so the clock and reset are not leaked."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90289",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amd/display: Resize MST HDCP per-connector arrays to 32"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Resize MST HDCP per-connector arrays to 32\n\nAMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_INDEX is 31. It suggest a maximum number of\n32 connectors. But the way it's used is like MAX_DISPLAY_COUNT.\nHence we're off by one with DRM core, which supports a max of 32\nconnectors.\n\nRename AMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_INDEX to AMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_COUNT\nto match its actual use, and increase the size to 32 to match the\noriginally intended size."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90289",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90289\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90289](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90289)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Resize MST HDCP per-connector arrays to 32\n\nAMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_INDEX is 31. It suggest a maximum number of\n32 connectors. But the way it's used is like MAX_DISPLAY_COUNT.\nHence we're off by one with DRM core, which supports a max of 32\nconnectors.\n\nRename AMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_INDEX to AMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_COUNT\nto match its actual use, and increase the size to 32 to match the\noriginally intended size.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90289**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90289](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90289)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Resize MST HDCP per-connector arrays to 32\n\nAMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_INDEX is 31. It suggest a maximum number of\n32 connectors. But the way it's used is like MAX_DISPLAY_COUNT.\nHence we're off by one with DRM core, which supports a max of 32\nconnectors.\n\nRename AMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_INDEX to AMDGPU_DM_MAX_DISPLAY_COUNT\nto match its actual use, and increase the size to 32 to match the\noriginally intended size."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90290",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: arm64: hibernate: Restore DAIF state on error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: hibernate: Restore DAIF state on error\n\nSashiko AI has reported that if swsusp_mte_save_tags() for some reason\nfails we return from swsusp_arch_suspend() with DAIF being masked -\nthat is not what we'd expect. Restore the saved DAIF state before\nreturning from the error path."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90290",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90290\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90290](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90290)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: hibernate: Restore DAIF state on error\n\nSashiko AI has reported that if swsusp_mte_save_tags() for some reason\nfails we return from swsusp_arch_suspend() with DAIF being masked -\nthat is not what we'd expect. Restore the saved DAIF state before\nreturning from the error path.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90290**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90290](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90290)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: hibernate: Restore DAIF state on error\n\nSashiko AI has reported that if swsusp_mte_save_tags() for some reason\nfails we return from swsusp_arch_suspend() with DAIF being masked -\nthat is not what we'd expect. Restore the saved DAIF state before\nreturning from the error path."
              },
