            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90318",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: fat: release buffer head after rebuilding parent"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfat: release buffer head after rebuilding parent\n\nfat_scan_logstart() leaves the matching directory entry's buffer head in\nsinfo.bh for the caller to release, just like fat_scan().\n\nfat_rebuild_parent() uses the directory entry to rebuild the parent inode\nfor the nostale_ro NFS export path, but does not release sinfo.bh after a\nsuccessful scan.  Release it once fat_build_inode() has consumed the\ndirectory entry data."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90318",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90318\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90318](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90318)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfat: release buffer head after rebuilding parent\n\nfat_scan_logstart() leaves the matching directory entry's buffer head in\nsinfo.bh for the caller to release, just like fat_scan().\n\nfat_rebuild_parent() uses the directory entry to rebuild the parent inode\nfor the nostale_ro NFS export path, but does not release sinfo.bh after a\nsuccessful scan.  Release it once fat_build_inode() has consumed the\ndirectory entry data.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90318**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90318](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90318)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfat: release buffer head after rebuilding parent\n\nfat_scan_logstart() leaves the matching directory entry's buffer head in\nsinfo.bh for the caller to release, just like fat_scan().\n\nfat_rebuild_parent() uses the directory entry to rebuild the parent inode\nfor the nostale_ro NFS export path, but does not release sinfo.bh after a\nsuccessful scan.  Release it once fat_build_inode() has consumed the\ndirectory entry data."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
