            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90330",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: HID: logitech-hidpp: Fix FF device cleanup on init failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: logitech-hidpp: Fix FF device cleanup on init failure\n\nhidpp_ff_init() creates the input force-feedback device with\ninput_ff_create(), then allocates the HID++ FF private data,\neffect ID array, and workqueue.\n\nIf any of those allocations fail after input_ff_create() succeeds,\nthe function returns an error without destroying the FF device.\nAdd an unwind path that frees the private allocations made by\nhidpp_ff_init() and calls input_ff_destroy() for failures after\ninput_ff_create() succeeds."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90330",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90330\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90330](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90330)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: logitech-hidpp: Fix FF device cleanup on init failure\n\nhidpp_ff_init() creates the input force-feedback device with\ninput_ff_create(), then allocates the HID++ FF private data,\neffect ID array, and workqueue.\n\nIf any of those allocations fail after input_ff_create() succeeds,\nthe function returns an error without destroying the FF device.\nAdd an unwind path that frees the private allocations made by\nhidpp_ff_init() and calls input_ff_destroy() for failures after\ninput_ff_create() succeeds.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90330**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90330](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90330)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: logitech-hidpp: Fix FF device cleanup on init failure\n\nhidpp_ff_init() creates the input force-feedback device with\ninput_ff_create(), then allocates the HID++ FF private data,\neffect ID array, and workqueue.\n\nIf any of those allocations fail after input_ff_create() succeeds,\nthe function returns an error without destroying the FF device.\nAdd an unwind path that frees the private allocations made by\nhidpp_ff_init() and calls input_ff_destroy() for failures after\ninput_ff_create() succeeds."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90333",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: dm-integrity: replace forgeable discard filler with a keyed sector marker"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-integrity: replace forgeable discard filler with a keyed sector marker\n\nThe discard-block check in dm_integrity_rw_tag() treats a stored tag\nof all 0xf6 bytes (DISCARD_FILLER) as proof a block was discarded and\nskips HMAC verification. allow_discards is only accepted in\ndm-integrity's standalone mode. An attacker with raw write access to\nthe backing device, but without the integrity key, can stamp any block\nwith an all-0xf6 tag and have it served as authentic.\n\nAdd a new \"allow_discards_keyed\" target argument that marks discarded\nblocks with a keyed checksum of (salt || sector) instead, computed by\nintegrity_discard_checksum()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90333",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90333\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90333](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90333)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-integrity: replace forgeable discard filler with a keyed sector marker\n\nThe discard-block check in dm_integrity_rw_tag() treats a stored tag\nof all 0xf6 bytes (DISCARD_FILLER) as proof a block was discarded and\nskips HMAC verification. allow_discards is only accepted in\ndm-integrity's standalone mode. An attacker with raw write access to\nthe backing device, but without the integrity key, can stamp any block\nwith an all-0xf6 tag and have it served as authentic.\n\nAdd a new \"allow_discards_keyed\" target argument that marks discarded\nblocks with a keyed checksum of (salt || sector) instead, computed by\nintegrity_discard_checksum().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90333**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90333](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90333)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-integrity: replace forgeable discard filler with a keyed sector marker\n\nThe discard-block check in dm_integrity_rw_tag() treats a stored tag\nof all 0xf6 bytes (DISCARD_FILLER) as proof a block was discarded and\nskips HMAC verification. allow_discards is only accepted in\ndm-integrity's standalone mode. An attacker with raw write access to\nthe backing device, but without the integrity key, can stamp any block\nwith an all-0xf6 tag and have it served as authentic.\n\nAdd a new \"allow_discards_keyed\" target argument that marks discarded\nblocks with a keyed checksum of (salt || sector) instead, computed by\nintegrity_discard_checksum()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
