            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90352",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: mt76: mt7915: release hif2 reference on probe IRQ failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: release hif2 reference on probe IRQ failure\n\nThe hif2 reference obtained by mt7915_pci_init_hif2() is only released on\nerror paths that key off dev-\u003ehif2, which is not assigned until after the\nIRQ setup. If pci_alloc_irq_vectors() or the primary devm_request_irq()\nfails, the reference leaks. Drop it explicitly on those paths via\nmt7915_put_hif2()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90352",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90352\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90352](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90352)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: release hif2 reference on probe IRQ failure\n\nThe hif2 reference obtained by mt7915_pci_init_hif2() is only released on\nerror paths that key off dev-\u003ehif2, which is not assigned until after the\nIRQ setup. If pci_alloc_irq_vectors() or the primary devm_request_irq()\nfails, the reference leaks. Drop it explicitly on those paths via\nmt7915_put_hif2().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90352**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90352](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90352)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: release hif2 reference on probe IRQ failure\n\nThe hif2 reference obtained by mt7915_pci_init_hif2() is only released on\nerror paths that key off dev-\u003ehif2, which is not assigned until after the\nIRQ setup. If pci_alloc_irq_vectors() or the primary devm_request_irq()\nfails, the reference leaks. Drop it explicitly on those paths via\nmt7915_put_hif2()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90353",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: fix ext PHY use-after-free on register error path\n\nAfter mt7915_register_ext_phy() succeeded, a failure of the main PHY\nmt7915_init_debugfs() or mt7915_coredump_register() unwound through\nfree_phy2, which called ieee80211_free_hw() on the ext PHY hw while it\nwas still registered with mac80211, since mt76_unregister_device() only\nunregisters the main hw. Unregister the ext PHY (thermal + phy + hw)\nfirst and skip the redundant free."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90353",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90353\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90353](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90353)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: fix ext PHY use-after-free on register error path\n\nAfter mt7915_register_ext_phy() succeeded, a failure of the main PHY\nmt7915_init_debugfs() or mt7915_coredump_register() unwound through\nfree_phy2, which called ieee80211_free_hw() on the ext PHY hw while it\nwas still registered with mac80211, since mt76_unregister_device() only\nunregisters the main hw. Unregister the ext PHY (thermal + phy + hw)\nfirst and skip the redundant free.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90353**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90353](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90353)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: fix ext PHY use-after-free on register error path\n\nAfter mt7915_register_ext_phy() succeeded, a failure of the main PHY\nmt7915_init_debugfs() or mt7915_coredump_register() unwound through\nfree_phy2, which called ieee80211_free_hw() on the ext PHY hw while it\nwas still registered with mac80211, since mt76_unregister_device() only\nunregisters the main hw. Unregister the ext PHY (thermal + phy + hw)\nfirst and skip the redundant free."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
