            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90364",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ACPI: processor: Unregister cpufreq notifier on init failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: processor: Unregister cpufreq notifier on init failure\n\nacpi_processor_driver_init() registers the cpufreq policy notifier before\nregistering the ACPI processor driver and setting up CPU hotplug state.\n\nIf driver_register() or cpuhp_setup_state() fails, the error path only\nunregisters the ACPI processor driver and the idle driver. The cpufreq\nnotifier remains registered even though initialization failed.\n\nMirror the module exit path on the init failure path and unregister the\ncpufreq notifier when it has been registered."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90364",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90364\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90364](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90364)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: processor: Unregister cpufreq notifier on init failure\n\nacpi_processor_driver_init() registers the cpufreq policy notifier before\nregistering the ACPI processor driver and setting up CPU hotplug state.\n\nIf driver_register() or cpuhp_setup_state() fails, the error path only\nunregisters the ACPI processor driver and the idle driver. The cpufreq\nnotifier remains registered even though initialization failed.\n\nMirror the module exit path on the init failure path and unregister the\ncpufreq notifier when it has been registered.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90364**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90364](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90364)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: processor: Unregister cpufreq notifier on init failure\n\nacpi_processor_driver_init() registers the cpufreq policy notifier before\nregistering the ACPI processor driver and setting up CPU hotplug state.\n\nIf driver_register() or cpuhp_setup_state() fails, the error path only\nunregisters the ACPI processor driver and the idle driver. The cpufreq\nnotifier remains registered even though initialization failed.\n\nMirror the module exit path on the init failure path and unregister the\ncpufreq notifier when it has been registered."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90366",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: reserve space for the CSA-abort countdown TLV\n\nWhen a CSA countdown is active, mt7996_mcu_beacon_cntdwn() emits two\nbss_bcn_cntdwn_tlv entries (the CSA countdown and the CCA-abort BCC), but\nMT7996_BEACON_UPDATE_SIZE only reserved one. With MBSSID enabled and a\nnear-maximum beacon template the extra 8 bytes could push the offload\ncommand past MT7996_MAX_BSS_OFFLOAD_SIZE and trigger skb_over_panic().\nReserve room for both countdown TLVs."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90366",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90366\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90366](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90366)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: reserve space for the CSA-abort countdown TLV\n\nWhen a CSA countdown is active, mt7996_mcu_beacon_cntdwn() emits two\nbss_bcn_cntdwn_tlv entries (the CSA countdown and the CCA-abort BCC), but\nMT7996_BEACON_UPDATE_SIZE only reserved one. With MBSSID enabled and a\nnear-maximum beacon template the extra 8 bytes could push the offload\ncommand past MT7996_MAX_BSS_OFFLOAD_SIZE and trigger skb_over_panic().\nReserve room for both countdown TLVs.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90366**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90366](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90366)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: reserve space for the CSA-abort countdown TLV\n\nWhen a CSA countdown is active, mt7996_mcu_beacon_cntdwn() emits two\nbss_bcn_cntdwn_tlv entries (the CSA countdown and the CCA-abort BCC), but\nMT7996_BEACON_UPDATE_SIZE only reserved one. With MBSSID enabled and a\nnear-maximum beacon template the extra 8 bytes could push the offload\ncommand past MT7996_MAX_BSS_OFFLOAD_SIZE and trigger skb_over_panic().\nReserve room for both countdown TLVs."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
