            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90368",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: unwind state on add_interface failure\n\nWhen mt76_wcid_alloc() fails, mt7915_add_interface() returned without\nclearing the vif_mask/omac_mask bits it had already set, without removing\nthe firmware dev info added earlier, and without clearing a monitor_vif\npointer to the vif mac80211 is about to free. mac80211 does not call\nremove_interface() for a failed add, so the indices and firmware dev\nentry leaked permanently and testmode could dereference the stale\nmonitor_vif. Add a proper error unwind."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90368",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90368\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90368](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90368)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: unwind state on add_interface failure\n\nWhen mt76_wcid_alloc() fails, mt7915_add_interface() returned without\nclearing the vif_mask/omac_mask bits it had already set, without removing\nthe firmware dev info added earlier, and without clearing a monitor_vif\npointer to the vif mac80211 is about to free. mac80211 does not call\nremove_interface() for a failed add, so the indices and firmware dev\nentry leaked permanently and testmode could dereference the stale\nmonitor_vif. Add a proper error unwind.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90368**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90368](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90368)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: unwind state on add_interface failure\n\nWhen mt76_wcid_alloc() fails, mt7915_add_interface() returned without\nclearing the vif_mask/omac_mask bits it had already set, without removing\nthe firmware dev info added earlier, and without clearing a monitor_vif\npointer to the vif mac80211 is about to free. mac80211 does not call\nremove_interface() for a failed add, so the indices and firmware dev\nentry leaked permanently and testmode could dereference the stale\nmonitor_vif. Add a proper error unwind."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
