            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90372",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: avoid nss underflow in mt7915_mcu_get_sta_nss\n\nIf a peer's VHT/HE MCS map has no supported spatial stream (all fields\n0x3), the loop exits with nss == 0 and the function returned (u8)-1 (255),\nwhich was then written into the firmware sta_rec_bf beamforming fields.\nClamp the result to 0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90372",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90372\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90372](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90372)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: avoid nss underflow in mt7915_mcu_get_sta_nss\n\nIf a peer's VHT/HE MCS map has no supported spatial stream (all fields\n0x3), the loop exits with nss == 0 and the function returned (u8)-1 (255),\nwhich was then written into the firmware sta_rec_bf beamforming fields.\nClamp the result to 0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90372**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90372](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90372)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: avoid nss underflow in mt7915_mcu_get_sta_nss\n\nIf a peer's VHT/HE MCS map has no supported spatial stream (all fields\n0x3), the loop exits with nss == 0 and the function returned (u8)-1 (255),\nwhich was then written into the firmware sta_rec_bf beamforming fields.\nClamp the result to 0."
              },
