            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90374",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: validate RX band_idx before dereferencing phys[]\n\nband_idx comes from a 2-bit descriptor field (0-3) and was used directly\nto index dev-\u003emt76.phys[] (size __MT_MAX_BAND == 3) and dereference the\nresult. A corrupt or reserved descriptor value could index out of bounds\nor hit a NULL phy on parts with fewer bands. Reject invalid band indices,\nmirroring mt7996_rx_get_wcid()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90374",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90374\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90374](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90374)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: validate RX band_idx before dereferencing phys[]\n\nband_idx comes from a 2-bit descriptor field (0-3) and was used directly\nto index dev-\u003emt76.phys[] (size __MT_MAX_BAND == 3) and dereference the\nresult. A corrupt or reserved descriptor value could index out of bounds\nor hit a NULL phy on parts with fewer bands. Reject invalid band indices,\nmirroring mt7996_rx_get_wcid().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90374**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90374](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90374)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: validate RX band_idx before dereferencing phys[]\n\nband_idx comes from a 2-bit descriptor field (0-3) and was used directly\nto index dev-\u003emt76.phys[] (size __MT_MAX_BAND == 3) and dereference the\nresult. A corrupt or reserved descriptor value could index out of bounds\nor hit a NULL phy on parts with fewer bands. Reject invalid band indices,\nmirroring mt7996_rx_get_wcid()."
              },
