            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90394",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  p ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: supply: sc2731_charger: cancel work on remove\n\nThe USB notifier and initial charger detection can schedule info-\u003ework.\nThe remove path unregisters the notifier, but does not cancel queued or\nrunning work before the devm-allocated driver data is released.\n\nSet the platform drvdata used by remove, then cancel the work after\nunregistering the notifier.\n\nThis issue was found by a static analysis tool."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90394",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90394\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90394](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90394)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: supply: sc2731_charger: cancel work on remove\n\nThe USB notifier and initial charger detection can schedule info-\u003ework.\nThe remove path unregisters the notifier, but does not cancel queued or\nrunning work before the devm-allocated driver data is released.\n\nSet the platform drvdata used by remove, then cancel the work after\nunregistering the notifier.\n\nThis issue was found by a static analysis tool.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90394**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90394](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90394)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: supply: sc2731_charger: cancel work on remove\n\nThe USB notifier and initial charger detection can schedule info-\u003ework.\nThe remove path unregisters the notifier, but does not cancel queued or\nrunning work before the devm-allocated driver data is released.\n\nSet the platform drvdata used by remove, then cancel the work after\nunregistering the notifier.\n\nThis issue was found by a static analysis tool."
              },
