            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90403",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtlwifi: pci: fix error path in rtl_pci_probe()\n\nIn the last error path in rtl_pci_probe(), the cleanup functions are\nskipped due to a wrong goto label. Moreover, the successful call to\nrtl_init_rfkill(), ieee80211_register_hw(), rtl_debug_add_one() have to\nbe reverted. Fix this issue by updating the labels and adding the\nrelevant cleanup functions to the last error path."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90403",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90403\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90403](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90403)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtlwifi: pci: fix error path in rtl_pci_probe()\n\nIn the last error path in rtl_pci_probe(), the cleanup functions are\nskipped due to a wrong goto label. Moreover, the successful call to\nrtl_init_rfkill(), ieee80211_register_hw(), rtl_debug_add_one() have to\nbe reverted. Fix this issue by updating the labels and adding the\nrelevant cleanup functions to the last error path.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90403**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90403](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90403)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtlwifi: pci: fix error path in rtl_pci_probe()\n\nIn the last error path in rtl_pci_probe(), the cleanup functions are\nskipped due to a wrong goto label. Moreover, the successful call to\nrtl_init_rfkill(), ieee80211_register_hw(), rtl_debug_add_one() have to\nbe reverted. Fix this issue by updating the labels and adding the\nrelevant cleanup functions to the last error path."
              },
