            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90404",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: platform/chrome: cros_ec_debugfs: Unregister panic notifier"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/chrome: cros_ec_debugfs: Unregister panic notifier\n\ncros_ec_debugfs_probe() registers notifier_panic with the EC panic\nnotifier chain. The remove path tears down debugfs and the console log,\nbut leaves the notifier registered. A later panic notification can call\nback into the removed instance and queue work that accesses released\ndata.\n\nUnregister the panic notifier before tearing down the debugfs and\nconsole log state.\n\nThis issue was found by a static analysis tool."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90404",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90404\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90404](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90404)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/chrome: cros_ec_debugfs: Unregister panic notifier\n\ncros_ec_debugfs_probe() registers notifier_panic with the EC panic\nnotifier chain. The remove path tears down debugfs and the console log,\nbut leaves the notifier registered. A later panic notification can call\nback into the removed instance and queue work that accesses released\ndata.\n\nUnregister the panic notifier before tearing down the debugfs and\nconsole log state.\n\nThis issue was found by a static analysis tool.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90404**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90404](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90404)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/chrome: cros_ec_debugfs: Unregister panic notifier\n\ncros_ec_debugfs_probe() registers notifier_panic with the EC panic\nnotifier chain. The remove path tears down debugfs and the console log,\nbut leaves the notifier registered. A later panic notification can call\nback into the removed instance and queue work that accesses released\ndata.\n\nUnregister the panic notifier before tearing down the debugfs and\nconsole log state.\n\nThis issue was found by a static analysis tool."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
