            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90434",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: isofs: release zisofs block pointer buffer head"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nisofs: release zisofs block pointer buffer head\n\nzisofs_fill_pages() reads the compressed block pointer table.  The error\npaths release the current buffer_head, the loop also releases the old\nbuffer_head when it advances. However, the success path leaves the last\nbuffer_head referenced. Release it before returning success."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90434",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90434\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90434](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90434)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nisofs: release zisofs block pointer buffer head\n\nzisofs_fill_pages() reads the compressed block pointer table.  The error\npaths release the current buffer_head, the loop also releases the old\nbuffer_head when it advances. However, the success path leaves the last\nbuffer_head referenced. Release it before returning success.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90434**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90434](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90434)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nisofs: release zisofs block pointer buffer head\n\nzisofs_fill_pages() reads the compressed block pointer table.  The error\npaths release the current buffer_head, the loop also releases the old\nbuffer_head when it advances. However, the success path leaves the last\nbuffer_head referenced. Release it before returning success."
              },
