            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-92497",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath12k: Avoid buffer overread in ath12k_wmi_op_rx()\n\nCurrently, in ath12k_wmi_op_rx(), the firmware buffer is read without\nfirst verifying that the buffer has enough data to hold a header. This\ncould result in a buffer overread.\n\nUpdate the logic to verify the buffer contains at least enough data to\nhold a wmi_cmd_hdr before reading from the buffer.\n\nTested-on: WCN7850 hw2.0 PCI WLAN.HMT.1.1.c7-00108-QCAHMTSWPL_V1.0_V2.0_SILICONZ_UPSTREAM-3"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-92497",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-92497\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-92497](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-92497)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath12k: Avoid buffer overread in ath12k_wmi_op_rx()\n\nCurrently, in ath12k_wmi_op_rx(), the firmware buffer is read without\nfirst verifying that the buffer has enough data to hold a header. This\ncould result in a buffer overread.\n\nUpdate the logic to verify the buffer contains at least enough data to\nhold a wmi_cmd_hdr before reading from the buffer.\n\nTested-on: WCN7850 hw2.0 PCI WLAN.HMT.1.1.c7-00108-QCAHMTSWPL_V1.0_V2.0_SILICONZ_UPSTREAM-3",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-92497**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-92497](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-92497)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath12k: Avoid buffer overread in ath12k_wmi_op_rx()\n\nCurrently, in ath12k_wmi_op_rx(), the firmware buffer is read without\nfirst verifying that the buffer has enough data to hold a header. This\ncould result in a buffer overread.\n\nUpdate the logic to verify the buffer contains at least enough data to\nhold a wmi_cmd_hdr before reading from the buffer.\n\nTested-on: WCN7850 hw2.0 PCI WLAN.HMT.1.1.c7-00108-QCAHMTSWPL_V1.0_V2.0_SILICONZ_UPSTREAM-3"
              },
