            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-92524",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: irqchip/gic-v3-its: Prevent leak in its_vpe_irq_domain_alloc()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nirqchip/gic-v3-its: Prevent leak in its_vpe_irq_domain_alloc()\n\nWhen its_irq_gic_domain_alloc() fails, the following\nits_vpe_irq_domain_free() fails to invoke its_vep_teardown() for the\ncorresponding interrupt, which leaks the resource.\n\nInvoke its_vpe_teardown() in the error handling path to avoid the leak.\n\n[ tglx: Massaged change log ]"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-92524",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-92524\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-92524](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-92524)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nirqchip/gic-v3-its: Prevent leak in its_vpe_irq_domain_alloc()\n\nWhen its_irq_gic_domain_alloc() fails, the following\nits_vpe_irq_domain_free() fails to invoke its_vep_teardown() for the\ncorresponding interrupt, which leaks the resource.\n\nInvoke its_vpe_teardown() in the error handling path to avoid the leak.\n\n[ tglx: Massaged change log ]",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-92524**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-92524](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-92524)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nirqchip/gic-v3-its: Prevent leak in its_vpe_irq_domain_alloc()\n\nWhen its_irq_gic_domain_alloc() fails, the following\nits_vpe_irq_domain_free() fails to invoke its_vep_teardown() for the\ncorresponding interrupt, which leaks the resource.\n\nInvoke its_vpe_teardown() in the error handling path to avoid the leak.\n\n[ tglx: Massaged change log ]"
              },
