            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93055",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  U ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nUDF symlink pathComponent header OOB read\n\nudf_symlink_filler() can enter udf_pc_to_char() with a partial pathComponent header.\n\nValidate that enough input remains for a complete pathComponent header\nbefore accessing it. Reject malformed symlink data that would otherwise\nmake udf_pc_to_char() perform an out-of-bounds read."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93055",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93055\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93055](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93055)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nUDF symlink pathComponent header OOB read\n\nudf_symlink_filler() can enter udf_pc_to_char() with a partial pathComponent header.\n\nValidate that enough input remains for a complete pathComponent header\nbefore accessing it. Reject malformed symlink data that would otherwise\nmake udf_pc_to_char() perform an out-of-bounds read.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93055**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-93055](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93055)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nUDF symlink pathComponent header OOB read\n\nudf_symlink_filler() can enter udf_pc_to_char() with a partial pathComponent header.\n\nValidate that enough input remains for a complete pathComponent header\nbefore accessing it. Reject malformed symlink data that would otherwise\nmake udf_pc_to_char() perform an out-of-bounds read."
              },
