            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93065",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: fix counter type in iwl_fwrt_dump_error_logs\n\nThe loop counter 'count' was declared as u8 while num_pc is u32.\nIf firmware advertises more than 255 PC entries the counter wraps\nback to zero and the loop never terminates potentially causing an\ninfinite loop or reading past the allocated pc_data array.\n\nChange the declaration to u32 to match num_pc."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93065",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93065\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93065](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93065)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: fix counter type in iwl_fwrt_dump_error_logs\n\nThe loop counter 'count' was declared as u8 while num_pc is u32.\nIf firmware advertises more than 255 PC entries the counter wraps\nback to zero and the loop never terminates potentially causing an\ninfinite loop or reading past the allocated pc_data array.\n\nChange the declaration to u32 to match num_pc.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93065**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-93065](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93065)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: fix counter type in iwl_fwrt_dump_error_logs\n\nThe loop counter 'count' was declared as u8 while num_pc is u32.\nIf firmware advertises more than 255 PC entries the counter wraps\nback to zero and the loop never terminates potentially causing an\ninfinite loop or reading past the allocated pc_data array.\n\nChange the declaration to u32 to match num_pc."
              },
