            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93108",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  R ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/ipoib: Drain RCU callbacks during module teardown\n\nIPoIB reclamation completions can be signaled from inside an RCU callback.\nTeardown can wake before the callback returns and unload ib_ipoib while its\ncode is still executing.\n\nClient registration failure can also remove already-added devices and queue\ncallbacks. Wait after client and workqueue teardown."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93108",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93108\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93108](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93108)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/ipoib: Drain RCU callbacks during module teardown\n\nIPoIB reclamation completions can be signaled from inside an RCU callback.\nTeardown can wake before the callback returns and unload ib_ipoib while its\ncode is still executing.\n\nClient registration failure can also remove already-added devices and queue\ncallbacks. Wait after client and workqueue teardown.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93108**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-93108](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93108)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/ipoib: Drain RCU callbacks during module teardown\n\nIPoIB reclamation completions can be signaled from inside an RCU callback.\nTeardown can wake before the callback returns and unload ib_ipoib while its\ncode is still executing.\n\nClient registration failure can also remove already-added devices and queue\ncallbacks. Wait after client and workqueue teardown."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
