            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93213",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  o ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nof: fix out-of-bounds read in of_alias_scan() stem parser\n\nThe stem parser tests isdigit(*(end - 1)) before checking end \u003e start\nand so reads one byte before the property name when the name is empty\nor all digits. Check the bound first."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93213",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93213\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93213](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93213)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nof: fix out-of-bounds read in of_alias_scan() stem parser\n\nThe stem parser tests isdigit(*(end - 1)) before checking end \u003e start\nand so reads one byte before the property name when the name is empty\nor all digits. Check the bound first.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93213**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-93213](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93213)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nof: fix out-of-bounds read in of_alias_scan() stem parser\n\nThe stem parser tests isdigit(*(end - 1)) before checking end \u003e start\nand so reads one byte before the property name when the name is empty\nor all digits. Check the bound first."
              },
