            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93215",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  c ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncdx: Fix double free when sysfs file creation fails\n\nIn cdx_create_res_attr(), if sysfs_create_bin_file() fails, the code\nfrees res_attr but doesn't set cdx_dev-\u003eres_attr[num] to NULL. This\nleaves a dangling pointer in the array. Then cdx_destroy_res_attr()\nfrees the already-freed memory. Fix the double free by initializing\ncdx_dev-\u003eres_attr[num] after sysfs_create_bin_file() completes."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93215",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93215\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93215](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93215)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncdx: Fix double free when sysfs file creation fails\n\nIn cdx_create_res_attr(), if sysfs_create_bin_file() fails, the code\nfrees res_attr but doesn't set cdx_dev-\u003eres_attr[num] to NULL. This\nleaves a dangling pointer in the array. Then cdx_destroy_res_attr()\nfrees the already-freed memory. Fix the double free by initializing\ncdx_dev-\u003eres_attr[num] after sysfs_create_bin_file() completes.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93215**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-93215](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93215)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncdx: Fix double free when sysfs file creation fails\n\nIn cdx_create_res_attr(), if sysfs_create_bin_file() fails, the code\nfrees res_attr but doesn't set cdx_dev-\u003eres_attr[num] to NULL. This\nleaves a dangling pointer in the array. Then cdx_destroy_res_attr()\nfrees the already-freed memory. Fix the double free by initializing\ncdx_dev-\u003eres_attr[num] after sysfs_create_bin_file() completes."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
