            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93789",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: iwlwifi: bound aligned TLV advance in FW parser"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: bound aligned TLV advance in FW parser\n\nValidate ALIGN(tlv_len, 4) against remaining parser length before\nconsuming bytes from the firmware image.\n\nThis avoids length underflow on malformed TLVs."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93789",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93789\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93789](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93789)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: bound aligned TLV advance in FW parser\n\nValidate ALIGN(tlv_len, 4) against remaining parser length before\nconsuming bytes from the firmware image.\n\nThis avoids length underflow on malformed TLVs.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93789**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-93789](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93789)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: bound aligned TLV advance in FW parser\n\nValidate ALIGN(tlv_len, 4) against remaining parser length before\nconsuming bytes from the firmware image.\n\nThis avoids length underflow on malformed TLVs."
              },
