            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93801",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: smb/client: zero-initialize stack-allocated cifs_open_info_data"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb/client: zero-initialize stack-allocated cifs_open_info_data\n\nStack-allocated cifs_open_info_data may contain random data.\nThis can make some fields have wrong value if they are not set later."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93801",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93801\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93801](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93801)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb/client: zero-initialize stack-allocated cifs_open_info_data\n\nStack-allocated cifs_open_info_data may contain random data.\nThis can make some fields have wrong value if they are not set later.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93801**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-93801](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93801)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb/client: zero-initialize stack-allocated cifs_open_info_data\n\nStack-allocated cifs_open_info_data may contain random data.\nThis can make some fields have wrong value if they are not set later."
              },
              "properties": {
