            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93826",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: HID: hidpp: fix potential UAF in hidpp_connect_event()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: hidpp: fix potential UAF in hidpp_connect_event()\n\nIf input_register_device() fails, we call input_free_device(), but keep\nstale pointer to the old device in hidpp-\u003einput, which could potentially\nlead to UAF. Fix that by resetting it to NULL before returning from\nhidpp_connect_event()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93826",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93826\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93826](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93826)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: hidpp: fix potential UAF in hidpp_connect_event()\n\nIf input_register_device() fails, we call input_free_device(), but keep\nstale pointer to the old device in hidpp-\u003einput, which could potentially\nlead to UAF. Fix that by resetting it to NULL before returning from\nhidpp_connect_event().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93826**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-93826](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93826)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: hidpp: fix potential UAF in hidpp_connect_event()\n\nIf input_register_device() fails, we call input_free_device(), but keep\nstale pointer to the old device in hidpp-\u003einput, which could potentially\nlead to UAF. Fix that by resetting it to NULL before returning from\nhidpp_connect_event()."
              },
