            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97418",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ALSA: es18xx: check control allocation before private data setup"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: es18xx: check control allocation before private data setup\n\nsnd_es18xx_mixer() creates controls with snd_ctl_new1() and then stores\nbookkeeping pointers or sets private_free before calling snd_ctl_add().\nsnd_ctl_new1() can return NULL on allocation failure, so those writes\ncan dereference a NULL control pointer.\n\nCheck the returned control pointers before using them and return -ENOMEM\non allocation failure."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97418",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97418\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97418](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97418)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: es18xx: check control allocation before private data setup\n\nsnd_es18xx_mixer() creates controls with snd_ctl_new1() and then stores\nbookkeeping pointers or sets private_free before calling snd_ctl_add().\nsnd_ctl_new1() can return NULL on allocation failure, so those writes\ncan dereference a NULL control pointer.\n\nCheck the returned control pointers before using them and return -ENOMEM\non allocation failure.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97418**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97418](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97418)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: es18xx: check control allocation before private data setup\n\nsnd_es18xx_mixer() creates controls with snd_ctl_new1() and then stores\nbookkeeping pointers or sets private_free before calling snd_ctl_add().\nsnd_ctl_new1() can return NULL on allocation failure, so those writes\ncan dereference a NULL control pointer.\n\nCheck the returned control pointers before using them and return -ENOMEM\non allocation failure."
              },
