            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97440",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net: qrtr: fix node refcount leak on ctrl packet alloc failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: qrtr: fix node refcount leak on ctrl packet alloc failure\n\nqrtr_send_resume_tx() calls qrtr_node_lookup() which takes a\nreference on the returned node. If the subsequent call to\nqrtr_alloc_ctrl_packet() fails due to memory allocation failure, the\nfunction returns -ENOMEM without calling qrtr_node_release() to\nrelease the node reference.\n\nAdd qrtr_node_release(node) before returning on the allocation failure\npath to properly release the reference."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97440",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97440\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97440](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97440)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: qrtr: fix node refcount leak on ctrl packet alloc failure\n\nqrtr_send_resume_tx() calls qrtr_node_lookup() which takes a\nreference on the returned node. If the subsequent call to\nqrtr_alloc_ctrl_packet() fails due to memory allocation failure, the\nfunction returns -ENOMEM without calling qrtr_node_release() to\nrelease the node reference.\n\nAdd qrtr_node_release(node) before returning on the allocation failure\npath to properly release the reference.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97440**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97440](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97440)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: qrtr: fix node refcount leak on ctrl packet alloc failure\n\nqrtr_send_resume_tx() calls qrtr_node_lookup() which takes a\nreference on the returned node. If the subsequent call to\nqrtr_alloc_ctrl_packet() fails due to memory allocation failure, the\nfunction returns -ENOMEM without calling qrtr_node_release() to\nrelease the node reference.\n\nAdd qrtr_node_release(node) before returning on the allocation failure\npath to properly release the reference."
              },
