            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97483",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: usb: core: hcd: fix possible deadlock in rh control transfers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: core: hcd: fix possible deadlock in rh control transfers\n\n\u003eFrom within the SCSI error handler memory allocations must not\ntrigger IO. Handling errors in UAS and the storage driver may\ninvolve resetting a device. The thread doing the reset itself\nrelies on VM magic. However, that is insufficient, as resetting\na device involves resuming it. Resumption as well as resetting\ninvolves conrol transfers to the parent of the device to be reset.\nThat may be a root hub. Hence usbcore must heed the flags passed\nto usb_submit_urb() processing control transfers to root hubs.\n\nThe problem exist since the storage driver has been merged."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97483",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97483\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97483](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97483)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: core: hcd: fix possible deadlock in rh control transfers\n\n\u003eFrom within the SCSI error handler memory allocations must not\ntrigger IO. Handling errors in UAS and the storage driver may\ninvolve resetting a device. The thread doing the reset itself\nrelies on VM magic. However, that is insufficient, as resetting\na device involves resuming it. Resumption as well as resetting\ninvolves conrol transfers to the parent of the device to be reset.\nThat may be a root hub. Hence usbcore must heed the flags passed\nto usb_submit_urb() processing control transfers to root hubs.\n\nThe problem exist since the storage driver has been merged.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97483**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97483](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97483)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: core: hcd: fix possible deadlock in rh control transfers\n\n\u003eFrom within the SCSI error handler memory allocations must not\ntrigger IO. Handling errors in UAS and the storage driver may\ninvolve resetting a device. The thread doing the reset itself\nrelies on VM magic. However, that is insufficient, as resetting\na device involves resuming it. Resumption as well as resetting\ninvolves conrol transfers to the parent of the device to be reset.\nThat may be a root hub. Hence usbcore must heed the flags passed\nto usb_submit_urb() processing control transfers to root hubs.\n\nThe problem exist since the storage driver has been merged."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97484",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: usbip: vhci_hcd: fix NULL deref in status_show_vhci"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusbip: vhci_hcd: fix NULL deref in status_show_vhci\n\nplatform_get_drvdata() can return NULL if a VHCI host controller's\nprobe failed (e.g. due to USB bus number exhaustion). status_show_vhci()\nchecked for a NULL pdev but not for a NULL hcd returned by\nplatform_get_drvdata(). Passing NULL to hcd_to_vhci_hcd() does not\nreturn NULL - it returns a pointer offset of 0x260, causing a NULL\npointer dereference when that value is subsequently dereferenced.\n\nAdd a NULL check on hcd before calling hcd_to_vhci_hcd(). Move\nstatus_show_not_ready() above status_show_vhci() to make it callable\nfrom the new error path without a forward declaration."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97484",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97484\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97484](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97484)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusbip: vhci_hcd: fix NULL deref in status_show_vhci\n\nplatform_get_drvdata() can return NULL if a VHCI host controller's\nprobe failed (e.g. due to USB bus number exhaustion). status_show_vhci()\nchecked for a NULL pdev but not for a NULL hcd returned by\nplatform_get_drvdata(). Passing NULL to hcd_to_vhci_hcd() does not\nreturn NULL - it returns a pointer offset of 0x260, causing a NULL\npointer dereference when that value is subsequently dereferenced.\n\nAdd a NULL check on hcd before calling hcd_to_vhci_hcd(). Move\nstatus_show_not_ready() above status_show_vhci() to make it callable\nfrom the new error path without a forward declaration.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97484**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97484](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97484)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusbip: vhci_hcd: fix NULL deref in status_show_vhci\n\nplatform_get_drvdata() can return NULL if a VHCI host controller's\nprobe failed (e.g. due to USB bus number exhaustion). status_show_vhci()\nchecked for a NULL pdev but not for a NULL hcd returned by\nplatform_get_drvdata(). Passing NULL to hcd_to_vhci_hcd() does not\nreturn NULL - it returns a pointer offset of 0x260, causing a NULL\npointer dereference when that value is subsequently dereferenced.\n\nAdd a NULL check on hcd before calling hcd_to_vhci_hcd(). Move\nstatus_show_not_ready() above status_show_vhci() to make it callable\nfrom the new error path without a forward declaration."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97485",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: omfs: handle set_blocksize failures"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nomfs: handle set_blocksize failures\n\nomfs uses buffer_heads, which don't handle block size \u003e PAGE_SIZE well.\nWithout this, mounting we will hit the\n\n        BUG_ON(offset \u003e= folio_size(folio));\n\nin folio_set_bh on the first __bread_gfp call."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97485",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97485\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97485](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97485)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nomfs: handle set_blocksize failures\n\nomfs uses buffer_heads, which don't handle block size \u003e PAGE_SIZE well.\nWithout this, mounting we will hit the\n\n        BUG_ON(offset \u003e= folio_size(folio));\n\nin folio_set_bh on the first __bread_gfp call.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97485**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97485](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97485)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nomfs: handle set_blocksize failures\n\nomfs uses buffer_heads, which don't handle block size \u003e PAGE_SIZE well.\nWithout this, mounting we will hit the\n\n        BUG_ON(offset \u003e= folio_size(folio));\n\nin folio_set_bh on the first __bread_gfp call."
              },
