            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97510",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: thunderbolt: Release request if tb_cfg_request() fails in __tb_xdomain_response()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nthunderbolt: Release request if tb_cfg_request() fails in __tb_xdomain_response()\n\nIf tb_cfg_request() fails setting up the request (for example the\ncontrol channel is shut down already) it returns an error without\ncalling the callback. To avoid leaking that memory, call\ntb_cfg_request_put() if tb_cfg_request() fails."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97510",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97510\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97510](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97510)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nthunderbolt: Release request if tb_cfg_request() fails in __tb_xdomain_response()\n\nIf tb_cfg_request() fails setting up the request (for example the\ncontrol channel is shut down already) it returns an error without\ncalling the callback. To avoid leaking that memory, call\ntb_cfg_request_put() if tb_cfg_request() fails.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97510**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97510](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97510)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nthunderbolt: Release request if tb_cfg_request() fails in __tb_xdomain_response()\n\nIf tb_cfg_request() fails setting up the request (for example the\ncontrol channel is shut down already) it returns an error without\ncalling the callback. To avoid leaking that memory, call\ntb_cfg_request_put() if tb_cfg_request() fails."
              },
