            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97542",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: xfs: bail out on bitmap errors in xrep_agfl_fill"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: bail out on bitmap errors in xrep_agfl_fill\n\nLOLLM also points out that the xagb_bitmap_set call in xrep_agfl_fill\ncan fail, but we don't check the result of xagb_bitmap_walk, so we\nsilently drop the error and proceed with inconsistent incore data.\nThat shouldn't be allowed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97542",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97542\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97542](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97542)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: bail out on bitmap errors in xrep_agfl_fill\n\nLOLLM also points out that the xagb_bitmap_set call in xrep_agfl_fill\ncan fail, but we don't check the result of xagb_bitmap_walk, so we\nsilently drop the error and proceed with inconsistent incore data.\nThat shouldn't be allowed.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97542**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97542](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97542)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: bail out on bitmap errors in xrep_agfl_fill\n\nLOLLM also points out that the xagb_bitmap_set call in xrep_agfl_fill\ncan fail, but we don't check the result of xagb_bitmap_walk, so we\nsilently drop the error and proceed with inconsistent incore data.\nThat shouldn't be allowed."
              },
