            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97568",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  m ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: syncookies: remember the request backup flag\n\nInstead of using an uninitialised bit when copying the info in\nsubflow_ulp_clone().\n\nTo fix this, no need to extend the join_entry structure: backup is\ncoming from struct mptcp_subflow_request_sock, only one bit. Do the same\nhere by using one bit for both."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97568",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97568\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97568](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97568)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: syncookies: remember the request backup flag\n\nInstead of using an uninitialised bit when copying the info in\nsubflow_ulp_clone().\n\nTo fix this, no need to extend the join_entry structure: backup is\ncoming from struct mptcp_subflow_request_sock, only one bit. Do the same\nhere by using one bit for both.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97568**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97568](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97568)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: syncookies: remember the request backup flag\n\nInstead of using an uninitialised bit when copying the info in\nsubflow_ulp_clone().\n\nTo fix this, no need to extend the join_entry structure: backup is\ncoming from struct mptcp_subflow_request_sock, only one bit. Do the same\nhere by using one bit for both."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
