            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97579",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: media: mediatek: vcodec: bound AV1 tile-start copy to the array capacity"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: mediatek: vcodec: bound AV1 tile-start copy to the array capacity\n\nvdec_av1_slice_setup_tile() copies tile_cols + 1 / tile_rows + 1 entries\ninto mi_col_starts[] / mi_row_starts[] from the bitstream tile_info. Bound\nthe copy to the array capacity."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97579",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97579\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97579](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97579)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: mediatek: vcodec: bound AV1 tile-start copy to the array capacity\n\nvdec_av1_slice_setup_tile() copies tile_cols + 1 / tile_rows + 1 entries\ninto mi_col_starts[] / mi_row_starts[] from the bitstream tile_info. Bound\nthe copy to the array capacity.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97579**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97579](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97579)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: mediatek: vcodec: bound AV1 tile-start copy to the array capacity\n\nvdec_av1_slice_setup_tile() copies tile_cols + 1 / tile_rows + 1 entries\ninto mi_col_starts[] / mi_row_starts[] from the bitstream tile_info. Bound\nthe copy to the array capacity."
              },
