            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97916",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: accel/ivpu: Validate firmware log buffer metadata"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/ivpu: Validate firmware log buffer metadata\n\nThe tracing log headers parsed by fw_log_print_buffer() reside in\nDMA-shared BOs that the NPU firmware can write to.\n\nfw_log_from_bo() validated log-\u003eheader_size and log-\u003esize, but\nfw_log_print_buffer() re-read those same fields from shared memory\nafterwards, allowing a TOCTOU where firmware changes them between the\ncheck and the use, and making the host dereference out-of-bounds\naddresses while printing logs.\n\nSnapshot the validated values once with READ_ONCE() and pass them down\nexplicitly in a new struct ivpu_fw_log_desc instead of re-reading them\nfrom the shared struct."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97916",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97916\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97916](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97916)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/ivpu: Validate firmware log buffer metadata\n\nThe tracing log headers parsed by fw_log_print_buffer() reside in\nDMA-shared BOs that the NPU firmware can write to.\n\nfw_log_from_bo() validated log-\u003eheader_size and log-\u003esize, but\nfw_log_print_buffer() re-read those same fields from shared memory\nafterwards, allowing a TOCTOU where firmware changes them between the\ncheck and the use, and making the host dereference out-of-bounds\naddresses while printing logs.\n\nSnapshot the validated values once with READ_ONCE() and pass them down\nexplicitly in a new struct ivpu_fw_log_desc instead of re-reading them\nfrom the shared struct.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97916**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97916](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97916)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/ivpu: Validate firmware log buffer metadata\n\nThe tracing log headers parsed by fw_log_print_buffer() reside in\nDMA-shared BOs that the NPU firmware can write to.\n\nfw_log_from_bo() validated log-\u003eheader_size and log-\u003esize, but\nfw_log_print_buffer() re-read those same fields from shared memory\nafterwards, allowing a TOCTOU where firmware changes them between the\ncheck and the use, and making the host dereference out-of-bounds\naddresses while printing logs.\n\nSnapshot the validated values once with READ_ONCE() and pass them down\nexplicitly in a new struct ivpu_fw_log_desc instead of re-reading them\nfrom the shared struct."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97917",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: accel/ivpu: Validate full buffer range in ivpu_to_cpu_addr"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/ivpu: Validate full buffer range in ivpu_to_cpu_addr\n\nAdd a size parameter to ivpu_to_cpu_addr() and validate that the\nwhole [vpu_addr, vpu_addr + size) range stays within the BO."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97917",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97917\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97917](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97917)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/ivpu: Validate full buffer range in ivpu_to_cpu_addr\n\nAdd a size parameter to ivpu_to_cpu_addr() and validate that the\nwhole [vpu_addr, vpu_addr + size) range stays within the BO.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97917**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97917](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97917)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/ivpu: Validate full buffer range in ivpu_to_cpu_addr\n\nAdd a size parameter to ivpu_to_cpu_addr() and validate that the\nwhole [vpu_addr, vpu_addr + size) range stays within the BO."
              },
              "properties": {
