            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98024",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: s390/ism: folio_put() after error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/ism: folio_put() after error\n\ndmb-\u003ecpu_addr was allocated via folio_alloc(). Use folio_put() instead of\nkfree() in the error exit of ism_alloc_dmb() to avoid slab allocator\ncorruption.\n\nWhile at it, reset dmb-\u003ecpu_addr after folio_put to avoid unintentional UAF\nby future callers."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98024",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98024\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98024](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98024)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/ism: folio_put() after error\n\ndmb-\u003ecpu_addr was allocated via folio_alloc(). Use folio_put() instead of\nkfree() in the error exit of ism_alloc_dmb() to avoid slab allocator\ncorruption.\n\nWhile at it, reset dmb-\u003ecpu_addr after folio_put to avoid unintentional UAF\nby future callers.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98024**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98024](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98024)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/ism: folio_put() after error\n\ndmb-\u003ecpu_addr was allocated via folio_alloc(). Use folio_put() instead of\nkfree() in the error exit of ism_alloc_dmb() to avoid slab allocator\ncorruption.\n\nWhile at it, reset dmb-\u003ecpu_addr after folio_put to avoid unintentional UAF\nby future callers."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
