            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98031",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: nexthop: Initialize extack in remove_nh_grp_entry()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnexthop: Initialize extack in remove_nh_grp_entry()\n\nremove_nh_grp_entry() prints the extack message when a listener fails\nto replace the reduced nexthop group. However, extack is not\ninitialized and listeners are not required to set a message when\nreturning an error. Neither netdevsim nor mlxsw do so when an\nallocation fails, resulting in the dereference of an uninitialized\nstack pointer.\n\nFix by zero-initializing extack, as was done in commit 6347c5314cee\n(\"nexthop: initialize extack in nh_res_bucket_migrate()\")."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98031",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98031\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98031](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98031)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnexthop: Initialize extack in remove_nh_grp_entry()\n\nremove_nh_grp_entry() prints the extack message when a listener fails\nto replace the reduced nexthop group. However, extack is not\ninitialized and listeners are not required to set a message when\nreturning an error. Neither netdevsim nor mlxsw do so when an\nallocation fails, resulting in the dereference of an uninitialized\nstack pointer.\n\nFix by zero-initializing extack, as was done in commit 6347c5314cee\n(\"nexthop: initialize extack in nh_res_bucket_migrate()\").",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98031**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98031](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98031)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnexthop: Initialize extack in remove_nh_grp_entry()\n\nremove_nh_grp_entry() prints the extack message when a listener fails\nto replace the reduced nexthop group. However, extack is not\ninitialized and listeners are not required to set a message when\nreturning an error. Neither netdevsim nor mlxsw do so when an\nallocation fails, resulting in the dereference of an uninitialized\nstack pointer.\n\nFix by zero-initializing extack, as was done in commit 6347c5314cee\n(\"nexthop: initialize extack in nh_res_bucket_migrate()\")."
              },
