            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98051",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net: bcmasp: fix tx_spb_ring_full() checking same slot cnt times"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bcmasp: fix tx_spb_ring_full() checking same slot cnt times\n\nThe loop initialised next_index from intf-\u003etx_spb_index on every\niteration, so incr_ring() always produced the same result and only\none slot was ever tested.  Move the initialisation before the loop\nso each iteration advances next_index and the function correctly\nchecks that cnt consecutive descriptor slots are available before\nallowing a new transmission."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98051",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98051\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98051](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98051)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bcmasp: fix tx_spb_ring_full() checking same slot cnt times\n\nThe loop initialised next_index from intf-\u003etx_spb_index on every\niteration, so incr_ring() always produced the same result and only\none slot was ever tested.  Move the initialisation before the loop\nso each iteration advances next_index and the function correctly\nchecks that cnt consecutive descriptor slots are available before\nallowing a new transmission.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98051**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98051](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98051)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: bcmasp: fix tx_spb_ring_full() checking same slot cnt times\n\nThe loop initialised next_index from intf-\u003etx_spb_index on every\niteration, so incr_ring() always produced the same result and only\none slot was ever tested.  Move the initialisation before the loop\nso each iteration advances next_index and the function correctly\nchecks that cnt consecutive descriptor slots are available before\nallowing a new transmission."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
