                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98092\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98092](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98092)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: amd: yc: fix memory leak in acp6x_pdm_dma_close()\n\nacp6x_pdm_dma_close() does not free the runtime-\u003eprivate_data buffer\nallocated in acp6x_pdm_dma_open(). Add the missing kfree.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98092**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98092](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98092)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: amd: yc: fix memory leak in acp6x_pdm_dma_close()\n\nacp6x_pdm_dma_close() does not free the runtime-\u003eprivate_data buffer\nallocated in acp6x_pdm_dma_open(). Add the missing kfree."
