            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98114",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: propagate DACL parsing errors"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: propagate DACL parsing errors\n\nparse_dacl() silently accepts truncated ACEs and allocation failures,\nallowing set_info_sec() to continue with an incomplete ACL conversion.\n\nReturn parsing and allocation errors to parse_sec_desc() so malformed\nsecurity descriptors are rejected before inode attributes or ACL xattrs\nare updated."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98114",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98114\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98114](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98114)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: propagate DACL parsing errors\n\nparse_dacl() silently accepts truncated ACEs and allocation failures,\nallowing set_info_sec() to continue with an incomplete ACL conversion.\n\nReturn parsing and allocation errors to parse_sec_desc() so malformed\nsecurity descriptors are rejected before inode attributes or ACL xattrs\nare updated.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98114**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98114](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98114)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: propagate DACL parsing errors\n\nparse_dacl() silently accepts truncated ACEs and allocation failures,\nallowing set_info_sec() to continue with an incomplete ACL conversion.\n\nReturn parsing and allocation errors to parse_sec_desc() so malformed\nsecurity descriptors are rejected before inode attributes or ACL xattrs\nare updated."
