            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98177",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amdkfd: Avoid integer underflow in EOP ring size calculation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Avoid integer underflow in EOP ring size calculation.\n\nThe low 6 bits of cp_hqd_eop_control store the base-2 logarithm\nof the EOP ring size. This was calculated as\n\norder_base_2(q-\u003eeop_ring_buffer_size / 4) - 1\n\nBut order_base_2 can in theory return 0, so this could underflow\n(although in practice the ring buffer size cannot be less than 4096).\n\nChange this to\n\norder_base_2(q-\u003eeop_ring_buffer_size / 8)\n\nusing properties of logarithms.\n\nAlso add to the above comment to make the mathematics more clear.\n\n(cherry picked from commit f0f43fcf8b2b3a924cad9444340921c96ed5f634)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98177",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98177\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98177](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98177)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Avoid integer underflow in EOP ring size calculation.\n\nThe low 6 bits of cp_hqd_eop_control store the base-2 logarithm\nof the EOP ring size. This was calculated as\n\norder_base_2(q-\u003eeop_ring_buffer_size / 4) - 1\n\nBut order_base_2 can in theory return 0, so this could underflow\n(although in practice the ring buffer size cannot be less than 4096).\n\nChange this to\n\norder_base_2(q-\u003eeop_ring_buffer_size / 8)\n\nusing properties of logarithms.\n\nAlso add to the above comment to make the mathematics more clear.\n\n(cherry picked from commit f0f43fcf8b2b3a924cad9444340921c96ed5f634)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98177**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98177](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98177)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Avoid integer underflow in EOP ring size calculation.\n\nThe low 6 bits of cp_hqd_eop_control store the base-2 logarithm\nof the EOP ring size. This was calculated as\n\norder_base_2(q-\u003eeop_ring_buffer_size / 4) - 1\n\nBut order_base_2 can in theory return 0, so this could underflow\n(although in practice the ring buffer size cannot be less than 4096).\n\nChange this to\n\norder_base_2(q-\u003eeop_ring_buffer_size / 8)\n\nusing properties of logarithms.\n\nAlso add to the above comment to make the mathematics more clear.\n\n(cherry picked from commit f0f43fcf8b2b3a924cad9444340921c96ed5f634)"
              },
