            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98191",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: wlcore: release runtime PM ref on regdomain config failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: wlcore: release runtime PM ref on regdomain config failure\n\nwlcore_regdomain_config() gets a runtime PM reference before sending\nthe regulatory-domain command. When\nwlcore_cmd_regdomain_config_locked() fails, the function queues recovery\nand returns without dropping that reference.\n\nRelease the reference after handling the command result so both success\nand failure paths balance the preceding\npm_runtime_resume_and_get(). The recovery worker takes a separate\nruntime PM reference and cannot release the reference held here."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98191",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98191\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98191](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98191)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: wlcore: release runtime PM ref on regdomain config failure\n\nwlcore_regdomain_config() gets a runtime PM reference before sending\nthe regulatory-domain command. When\nwlcore_cmd_regdomain_config_locked() fails, the function queues recovery\nand returns without dropping that reference.\n\nRelease the reference after handling the command result so both success\nand failure paths balance the preceding\npm_runtime_resume_and_get(). The recovery worker takes a separate\nruntime PM reference and cannot release the reference held here.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98191**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98191](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98191)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: wlcore: release runtime PM ref on regdomain config failure\n\nwlcore_regdomain_config() gets a runtime PM reference before sending\nthe regulatory-domain command. When\nwlcore_cmd_regdomain_config_locked() fails, the function queues recovery\nand returns without dropping that reference.\n\nRelease the reference after handling the command result so both success\nand failure paths balance the preceding\npm_runtime_resume_and_get(). The recovery worker takes a separate\nruntime PM reference and cannot release the reference held here."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98193",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: libipw: reject TKIP frames without a full MIC"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libipw: reject TKIP frames without a full MIC\n\nlibipw_michael_mic_verify() assumes that an skb contains an eight-byte\nMichael MIC. A short TKIP frame makes the unsigned payload length wrap,\ncausing michael_mic() to read past the skb.\n\nCheck that the MIC is present before verifying it, and use the existing\nMICHAEL_MIC_LEN constant for all MIC lengths in the verifier."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98193",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98193\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98193](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98193)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libipw: reject TKIP frames without a full MIC\n\nlibipw_michael_mic_verify() assumes that an skb contains an eight-byte\nMichael MIC. A short TKIP frame makes the unsigned payload length wrap,\ncausing michael_mic() to read past the skb.\n\nCheck that the MIC is present before verifying it, and use the existing\nMICHAEL_MIC_LEN constant for all MIC lengths in the verifier.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98193**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98193](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98193)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libipw: reject TKIP frames without a full MIC\n\nlibipw_michael_mic_verify() assumes that an skb contains an eight-byte\nMichael MIC. A short TKIP frame makes the unsigned payload length wrap,\ncausing michael_mic() to read past the skb.\n\nCheck that the MIC is present before verifying it, and use the existing\nMICHAEL_MIC_LEN constant for all MIC lengths in the verifier."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98194",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: libertas_tf: fix UAF in lbtf_free_adapter()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libertas_tf: fix UAF in lbtf_free_adapter()\n\nlbtf_free_adapter() calls lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() to free the command\nbuffers before calling timer_delete_sync() to wait for the command\ntimer callback.  If the timer callback (command_timer_fn) is already\nrunning when lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() frees the command array, the\ncallback dereferences priv-\u003ecur_cmd-\u003ecmdbuf which points to freed\nmemory.\n\nSwap the order so that timer_delete_sync() runs first, ensuring any\nin-flight callback has completed before the command buffers are freed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98194",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98194\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98194](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98194)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libertas_tf: fix UAF in lbtf_free_adapter()\n\nlbtf_free_adapter() calls lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() to free the command\nbuffers before calling timer_delete_sync() to wait for the command\ntimer callback.  If the timer callback (command_timer_fn) is already\nrunning when lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() frees the command array, the\ncallback dereferences priv-\u003ecur_cmd-\u003ecmdbuf which points to freed\nmemory.\n\nSwap the order so that timer_delete_sync() runs first, ensuring any\nin-flight callback has completed before the command buffers are freed.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98194**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98194](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98194)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libertas_tf: fix UAF in lbtf_free_adapter()\n\nlbtf_free_adapter() calls lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() to free the command\nbuffers before calling timer_delete_sync() to wait for the command\ntimer callback.  If the timer callback (command_timer_fn) is already\nrunning when lbtf_free_cmd_buffer() frees the command array, the\ncallback dereferences priv-\u003ecur_cmd-\u003ecmdbuf which points to freed\nmemory.\n\nSwap the order so that timer_delete_sync() runs first, ensuring any\nin-flight callback has completed before the command buffers are freed."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
