              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nInput: cyttsp5 - clamp the HID report size before memcpy\n\nThe size field comes from the device and is used as the memcpy()\nlength into response_buf, which is CY_MAX_INPUT bytes."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
