            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98293",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Bluetooth: ISO: Fix parent socket leak in iso_conn_ready()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: Fix parent socket leak in iso_conn_ready()\n\niso_get_sock() returns the parent socket with a reference held, which is\ndropped by sock_put() once the child socket has been set up. The error\npath taken when iso_sock_alloc() fails only calls release_sock() and\nreturns, leaking the reference and thus the parent socket itself.\n\nDrop the reference on that path as well."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98293",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98293\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98293](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98293)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: Fix parent socket leak in iso_conn_ready()\n\niso_get_sock() returns the parent socket with a reference held, which is\ndropped by sock_put() once the child socket has been set up. The error\npath taken when iso_sock_alloc() fails only calls release_sock() and\nreturns, leaking the reference and thus the parent socket itself.\n\nDrop the reference on that path as well.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98293**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98293](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98293)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: Fix parent socket leak in iso_conn_ready()\n\niso_get_sock() returns the parent socket with a reference held, which is\ndropped by sock_put() once the child socket has been set up. The error\npath taken when iso_sock_alloc() fails only calls release_sock() and\nreturns, leaking the reference and thus the parent socket itself.\n\nDrop the reference on that path as well."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
