            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98410",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: watchdog: da9063: fix suspend/resume handling of HW_RUNNING watchdog"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwatchdog: da9063: fix suspend/resume handling of HW_RUNNING watchdog\n\nda9063_wdt_suspend() and da9063_wdt_resume() only check watchdog_active(),\nwhen the watchdog is left running by the driver sets\nWDOG_HW_RUNNING in da9063_wdt_probe() but userspace never opens the\ndevice, so WDOG_ACTIVE remains cleared, the wdt_disable() will not be\nexecuted in da9063_wdt_suspend. In this case, the suspend callback is\na no-op and the watchdog keeps counting during system suspend,\nleading to an unexpected system reset.\nCheck WDOG_HW_RUNNING and wdd，can fix this issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98410",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98410\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98410](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98410)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwatchdog: da9063: fix suspend/resume handling of HW_RUNNING watchdog\n\nda9063_wdt_suspend() and da9063_wdt_resume() only check watchdog_active(),\nwhen the watchdog is left running by the driver sets\nWDOG_HW_RUNNING in da9063_wdt_probe() but userspace never opens the\ndevice, so WDOG_ACTIVE remains cleared, the wdt_disable() will not be\nexecuted in da9063_wdt_suspend. In this case, the suspend callback is\na no-op and the watchdog keeps counting during system suspend,\nleading to an unexpected system reset.\nCheck WDOG_HW_RUNNING and wdd，can fix this issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98410**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98410](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98410)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwatchdog: da9063: fix suspend/resume handling of HW_RUNNING watchdog\n\nda9063_wdt_suspend() and da9063_wdt_resume() only check watchdog_active(),\nwhen the watchdog is left running by the driver sets\nWDOG_HW_RUNNING in da9063_wdt_probe() but userspace never opens the\ndevice, so WDOG_ACTIVE remains cleared, the wdt_disable() will not be\nexecuted in da9063_wdt_suspend. In this case, the suspend callback is\na no-op and the watchdog keeps counting during system suspend,\nleading to an unexpected system reset.\nCheck WDOG_HW_RUNNING and wdd，can fix this issue."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
