            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98413",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: selinux: always fill AVC decision in avc_has_perm_noaudit()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nselinux: always fill AVC decision in avc_has_perm_noaudit()\n\navc_has_perm_noaudit() is documented to return a copy of the access\ndecision in @avd, but its early return for an empty requested permission\nset leaves the buffer untouched.  All callers pass an uninitialized\nstack variable and afterwards feed it to avc_audit(), and the inode hook\neven stores it in the per-task decision cache.\n\nFill in a deny-all, audit-all decision, similar to avd_init(), so every\ncaller receives a defined value at no cost on the hot path."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98413",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98413\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98413](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98413)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nselinux: always fill AVC decision in avc_has_perm_noaudit()\n\navc_has_perm_noaudit() is documented to return a copy of the access\ndecision in @avd, but its early return for an empty requested permission\nset leaves the buffer untouched.  All callers pass an uninitialized\nstack variable and afterwards feed it to avc_audit(), and the inode hook\neven stores it in the per-task decision cache.\n\nFill in a deny-all, audit-all decision, similar to avd_init(), so every\ncaller receives a defined value at no cost on the hot path.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98413**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98413](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98413)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nselinux: always fill AVC decision in avc_has_perm_noaudit()\n\navc_has_perm_noaudit() is documented to return a copy of the access\ndecision in @avd, but its early return for an empty requested permission\nset leaves the buffer untouched.  All callers pass an uninitialized\nstack variable and afterwards feed it to avc_audit(), and the inode hook\neven stores it in the per-task decision cache.\n\nFill in a deny-all, audit-all decision, similar to avd_init(), so every\ncaller receives a defined value at no cost on the hot path."
              },
