            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98421",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: mac80211: require a peer station for TDLS setup confirm"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: require a peer station for TDLS setup confirm\n\nIt's nonsense for the setup confirm to go to station that\ndoesn't even exist, and it hits a warning when building\nthe frame:\n\n  WARN_ON_ONCE(!sta || !ap_sta)\n\nOnly accept WLAN_TDLS_SETUP_CONFIRM when the station is\nalready there as a TDLS station. Need to copy the call\nto ieee80211_tdls_prep_mgmt_packet() since the existing\nWLAN_TDLS_DISCOVERY_REQUEST already falls through to it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98421",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98421\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98421](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98421)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: require a peer station for TDLS setup confirm\n\nIt's nonsense for the setup confirm to go to station that\ndoesn't even exist, and it hits a warning when building\nthe frame:\n\n  WARN_ON_ONCE(!sta || !ap_sta)\n\nOnly accept WLAN_TDLS_SETUP_CONFIRM when the station is\nalready there as a TDLS station. Need to copy the call\nto ieee80211_tdls_prep_mgmt_packet() since the existing\nWLAN_TDLS_DISCOVERY_REQUEST already falls through to it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98421**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98421](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98421)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: require a peer station for TDLS setup confirm\n\nIt's nonsense for the setup confirm to go to station that\ndoesn't even exist, and it hits a warning when building\nthe frame:\n\n  WARN_ON_ONCE(!sta || !ap_sta)\n\nOnly accept WLAN_TDLS_SETUP_CONFIRM when the station is\nalready there as a TDLS station. Need to copy the call\nto ieee80211_tdls_prep_mgmt_packet() since the existing\nWLAN_TDLS_DISCOVERY_REQUEST already falls through to it."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
