            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98422",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: mac80211: reset the AP_VLAN tailroom counter on ifdown"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: reset the AP_VLAN tailroom counter on ifdown\n\nOn ifup, AP_VLAN interfaces get crypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt from\nthe AP interface, but it's never decremented again unless the AP is\nalso brought down. Thus, bringing the same AP_VLAN up again will\nincrement the counter again and eventually hit the sanity check:\n\n  WARN_ON_ONCE(sdata-\u003ecrypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt !=\n               master-\u003ecrypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt);\n\nReset it on ifdown to avoid that."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98422",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98422\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98422](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98422)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: reset the AP_VLAN tailroom counter on ifdown\n\nOn ifup, AP_VLAN interfaces get crypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt from\nthe AP interface, but it's never decremented again unless the AP is\nalso brought down. Thus, bringing the same AP_VLAN up again will\nincrement the counter again and eventually hit the sanity check:\n\n  WARN_ON_ONCE(sdata-\u003ecrypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt !=\n               master-\u003ecrypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt);\n\nReset it on ifdown to avoid that.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98422**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98422](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98422)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: reset the AP_VLAN tailroom counter on ifdown\n\nOn ifup, AP_VLAN interfaces get crypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt from\nthe AP interface, but it's never decremented again unless the AP is\nalso brought down. Thus, bringing the same AP_VLAN up again will\nincrement the counter again and eventually hit the sanity check:\n\n  WARN_ON_ONCE(sdata-\u003ecrypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt !=\n               master-\u003ecrypto_tx_tailroom_needed_cnt);\n\nReset it on ifdown to avoid that."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
