            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-6238",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: nvme: memory corruption via unprivileged user passthrough"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A buffer overflow vulnerability was found in the NVM Express (NVMe) driver in the Linux kernel. Only privileged user could specify a small meta buffer and let the device perform larger Direct Memory Access (DMA) into the same buffer, overwriting unrelated kernel memory, causing random kernel crashes and memory corruption."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-6238",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-6238\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2023-6238](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-6238)\nA buffer overflow vulnerability was found in the NVM Express (NVMe) driver in the Linux kernel. Only privileged user could specify a small meta buffer and let the device perform larger Direct Memory Access (DMA) into the same buffer, overwriting unrelated kernel memory, causing random kernel crashes and memory corruption.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-6238**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2023-6238](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-6238)|\n\nA buffer overflow vulnerability was found in the NVM Express (NVMe) driver in the Linux kernel. Only privileged user could specify a small meta buffer and let the device perform larger Direct Memory Access (DMA) into the same buffer, overwriting unrelated kernel memory, causing random kernel crashes and memory corruption."
              },
