            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-58012",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ASoC: SOF: Intel: hda-dai: Ensure DAI widget is valid during params"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: SOF: Intel: hda-dai: Ensure DAI widget is valid during params\n\nEach cpu DAI should associate with a widget. However, the topology might\nnot create the right number of DAI widgets for aggregated amps. And it\nwill cause NULL pointer deference.\nCheck that the DAI widget associated with the CPU DAI is valid to prevent\nNULL pointer deference due to missing DAI widgets in topologies with\naggregated amps."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58012",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-58012\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-58012](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58012)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: SOF: Intel: hda-dai: Ensure DAI widget is valid during params\n\nEach cpu DAI should associate with a widget. However, the topology might\nnot create the right number of DAI widgets for aggregated amps. And it\nwill cause NULL pointer deference.\nCheck that the DAI widget associated with the CPU DAI is valid to prevent\nNULL pointer deference due to missing DAI widgets in topologies with\naggregated amps.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-58012**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2024-58012](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58012)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: SOF: Intel: hda-dai: Ensure DAI widget is valid during params\n\nEach cpu DAI should associate with a widget. However, the topology might\nnot create the right number of DAI widgets for aggregated amps. And it\nwill cause NULL pointer deference.\nCheck that the DAI widget associated with the CPU DAI is valid to prevent\nNULL pointer deference due to missing DAI widgets in topologies with\naggregated amps."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-58015",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: ath12k: Fix for out-of bound access error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath12k: Fix for out-of bound access error\n\nSelfgen stats are placed in a buffer using print_array_to_buf_index() function.\nArray length parameter passed to the function is too big, resulting in possible\nout-of bound memory error.\nDecreasing buffer size by one fixes faulty upper bound of passed array.\n\nDiscovered in coverity scan, CID 1600742 and CID 1600758"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58015",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-58015\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-58015](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58015)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath12k: Fix for out-of bound access error\n\nSelfgen stats are placed in a buffer using print_array_to_buf_index() function.\nArray length parameter passed to the function is too big, resulting in possible\nout-of bound memory error.\nDecreasing buffer size by one fixes faulty upper bound of passed array.\n\nDiscovered in coverity scan, CID 1600742 and CID 1600758",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-58015**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2024-58015](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58015)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath12k: Fix for out-of bound access error\n\nSelfgen stats are placed in a buffer using print_array_to_buf_index() function.\nArray length parameter passed to the function is too big, resulting in possible\nout-of bound memory error.\nDecreasing buffer size by one fixes faulty upper bound of passed array.\n\nDiscovered in coverity scan, CID 1600742 and CID 1600758"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-58094",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: jfs: add check read-only before truncation in jfs_truncate_nolock()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njfs: add check read-only before truncation in jfs_truncate_nolock()\n\nAdded a check for \"read-only\" mode in the `jfs_truncate_nolock`\nfunction to avoid errors related to writing to a read-only\nfilesystem.\n\nCall stack:\n\nblock_write_begin() {\n  jfs_write_failed() {\n    jfs_truncate() {\n      jfs_truncate_nolock() {\n        txEnd() {\n          ...\n          log = JFS_SBI(tblk-\u003esb)-\u003elog;\n          // (log == NULL)\n\nIf the `isReadOnly(ip)` condition is triggered in\n`jfs_truncate_nolock`, the function execution will stop, and no\nfurther data modification will occur. Instead, the `xtTruncate`\nfunction will be called with the \"COMMIT_WMAP\" flag, preventing\nmodifications in \"read-only\" mode."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58094",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-58094\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-58094](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58094)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njfs: add check read-only before truncation in jfs_truncate_nolock()\n\nAdded a check for \"read-only\" mode in the `jfs_truncate_nolock`\nfunction to avoid errors related to writing to a read-only\nfilesystem.\n\nCall stack:\n\nblock_write_begin() {\n  jfs_write_failed() {\n    jfs_truncate() {\n      jfs_truncate_nolock() {\n        txEnd() {\n          ...\n          log = JFS_SBI(tblk-\u003esb)-\u003elog;\n          // (log == NULL)\n\nIf the `isReadOnly(ip)` condition is triggered in\n`jfs_truncate_nolock`, the function execution will stop, and no\nfurther data modification will occur. Instead, the `xtTruncate`\nfunction will be called with the \"COMMIT_WMAP\" flag, preventing\nmodifications in \"read-only\" mode.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-58094**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2024-58094](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58094)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njfs: add check read-only before truncation in jfs_truncate_nolock()\n\nAdded a check for \"read-only\" mode in the `jfs_truncate_nolock`\nfunction to avoid errors related to writing to a read-only\nfilesystem.\n\nCall stack:\n\nblock_write_begin() {\n  jfs_write_failed() {\n    jfs_truncate() {\n      jfs_truncate_nolock() {\n        txEnd() {\n          ...\n          log = JFS_SBI(tblk-\u003esb)-\u003elog;\n          // (log == NULL)\n\nIf the `isReadOnly(ip)` condition is triggered in\n`jfs_truncate_nolock`, the function execution will stop, and no\nfurther data modification will occur. Instead, the `xtTruncate`\nfunction will be called with the \"COMMIT_WMAP\" flag, preventing\nmodifications in \"read-only\" mode."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-58095",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: jfs: add check read-only before txBeginAnon() call"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njfs: add check read-only before txBeginAnon() call\n\nAdded a read-only check before calling `txBeginAnon` in `extAlloc`\nand `extRecord`. This prevents modification attempts on a read-only\nmounted filesystem, avoiding potential errors or crashes.\n\nCall trace:\n txBeginAnon+0xac/0x154\n extAlloc+0xe8/0xdec fs/jfs/jfs_extent.c:78\n jfs_get_block+0x340/0xb98 fs/jfs/inode.c:248\n __block_write_begin_int+0x580/0x166c fs/buffer.c:2128\n __block_write_begin fs/buffer.c:2177 [inline]\n block_write_begin+0x98/0x11c fs/buffer.c:2236\n jfs_write_begin+0x44/0x88 fs/jfs/inode.c:299"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58095",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-58095\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2024-58095](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58095)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njfs: add check read-only before txBeginAnon() call\n\nAdded a read-only check before calling `txBeginAnon` in `extAlloc`\nand `extRecord`. This prevents modification attempts on a read-only\nmounted filesystem, avoiding potential errors or crashes.\n\nCall trace:\n txBeginAnon+0xac/0x154\n extAlloc+0xe8/0xdec fs/jfs/jfs_extent.c:78\n jfs_get_block+0x340/0xb98 fs/jfs/inode.c:248\n __block_write_begin_int+0x580/0x166c fs/buffer.c:2128\n __block_write_begin fs/buffer.c:2177 [inline]\n block_write_begin+0x98/0x11c fs/buffer.c:2236\n jfs_write_begin+0x44/0x88 fs/jfs/inode.c:299",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-58095**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2024-58095](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58095)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njfs: add check read-only before txBeginAnon() call\n\nAdded a read-only check before calling `txBeginAnon` in `extAlloc`\nand `extRecord`. This prevents modification attempts on a read-only\nmounted filesystem, avoiding potential errors or crashes.\n\nCall trace:\n txBeginAnon+0xac/0x154\n extAlloc+0xe8/0xdec fs/jfs/jfs_extent.c:78\n jfs_get_block+0x340/0xb98 fs/jfs/inode.c:248\n __block_write_begin_int+0x580/0x166c fs/buffer.c:2128\n __block_write_begin fs/buffer.c:2177 [inline]\n block_write_begin+0x98/0x11c fs/buffer.c:2236\n jfs_write_begin+0x44/0x88 fs/jfs/inode.c:299"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
