            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-68188",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: tcp: use dst_dev_rcu() in tcp_fastopen_active_disable_ofo_check()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntcp: use dst_dev_rcu() in tcp_fastopen_active_disable_ofo_check()\n\nUse RCU to avoid a pair of atomic operations and a potential\nUAF on dst_dev()-\u003eflags."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68188",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-68188\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-68188](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68188)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntcp: use dst_dev_rcu() in tcp_fastopen_active_disable_ofo_check()\n\nUse RCU to avoid a pair of atomic operations and a potential\nUAF on dst_dev()-\u003eflags.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-68188**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2025-68188](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-68188)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntcp: use dst_dev_rcu() in tcp_fastopen_active_disable_ofo_check()\n\nUse RCU to avoid a pair of atomic operations and a potential\nUAF on dst_dev()-\u003eflags."
              },
              "properties": {
