            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-31777",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ALSA: ctxfi: Check the error for index mapping"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: ctxfi: Check the error for index mapping\n\nThe ctxfi driver blindly assumed a proper value returned from\ndaio_device_index(), but it's not always true.  Add a proper error\ncheck to deal with the error from the function."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31777",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-31777\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-31777](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31777)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: ctxfi: Check the error for index mapping\n\nThe ctxfi driver blindly assumed a proper value returned from\ndaio_device_index(), but it's not always true.  Add a proper error\ncheck to deal with the error from the function.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-31777**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-31777](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31777)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: ctxfi: Check the error for index mapping\n\nThe ctxfi driver blindly assumed a proper value returned from\ndaio_device_index(), but it's not always true.  Add a proper error\ncheck to deal with the error from the function."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
