            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-46171",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: riscv: kvm: fix vector context allocation leak"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nriscv: kvm: fix vector context allocation leak\n\nWhen the second kzalloc (host_context.vector.datap) fails in\nkvm_riscv_vcpu_alloc_vector_context, the first allocation\n(guest_context.vector.datap) is leaked. Free it before returning."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46171",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-46171\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-46171](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46171)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nriscv: kvm: fix vector context allocation leak\n\nWhen the second kzalloc (host_context.vector.datap) fails in\nkvm_riscv_vcpu_alloc_vector_context, the first allocation\n(guest_context.vector.datap) is leaked. Free it before returning.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-46171**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-46171](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-46171)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nriscv: kvm: fix vector context allocation leak\n\nWhen the second kzalloc (host_context.vector.datap) fails in\nkvm_riscv_vcpu_alloc_vector_context, the first allocation\n(guest_context.vector.datap) is leaked. Free it before returning."
              },
              "properties": {
