            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53104",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: mt76: Fix memory leak destroying device"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: Fix memory leak destroying device\n\nAll MT76 rx queues have an associated page_pool even if the queue is not\nassociated to a NAPI (e.g. WED RRO queues with WED enabled). Destroy the\npage_pool running mt76_dma_cleanup routine during module unload.\nMoreover returns pages to the page pool if WED is not enabled for WED RRO\nqueues."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53104",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53104\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-53104](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53104)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: Fix memory leak destroying device\n\nAll MT76 rx queues have an associated page_pool even if the queue is not\nassociated to a NAPI (e.g. WED RRO queues with WED enabled). Destroy the\npage_pool running mt76_dma_cleanup routine during module unload.\nMoreover returns pages to the page pool if WED is not enabled for WED RRO\nqueues.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53104**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-53104](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-53104)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: Fix memory leak destroying device\n\nAll MT76 rx queues have an associated page_pool even if the queue is not\nassociated to a NAPI (e.g. WED RRO queues with WED enabled). Destroy the\npage_pool running mt76_dma_cleanup routine during module unload.\nMoreover returns pages to the page pool if WED is not enabled for WED RRO\nqueues."
              },
              "properties": {
