            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-64227",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ACPI: driver: Check ACPI_COMPANION() against NULL during probe"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: driver: Check ACPI_COMPANION() against NULL during probe\n\nSince every platform driver can be forced to match a device that doesn't\nmatch its list of device IDs because of device_match_driver_override(),\nplatform drivers that rely on the existence of a device's ACPI companion\nobject should verify its presence.\n\nAccordingly, add requisite ACPI_COMPANION() or ACPI_HANDLE() checks\nagainst NULL to 13 platform drivers handling core ACPI devices.\n\nAlso change the value returned by the ACPI thermal zone driver when\nthe device's ACPI companion is not present to -ENODEV for consistency\nwith the other drivers."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64227",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-64227\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-64227](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64227)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: driver: Check ACPI_COMPANION() against NULL during probe\n\nSince every platform driver can be forced to match a device that doesn't\nmatch its list of device IDs because of device_match_driver_override(),\nplatform drivers that rely on the existence of a device's ACPI companion\nobject should verify its presence.\n\nAccordingly, add requisite ACPI_COMPANION() or ACPI_HANDLE() checks\nagainst NULL to 13 platform drivers handling core ACPI devices.\n\nAlso change the value returned by the ACPI thermal zone driver when\nthe device's ACPI companion is not present to -ENODEV for consistency\nwith the other drivers.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-64227**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-64227](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-64227)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: driver: Check ACPI_COMPANION() against NULL during probe\n\nSince every platform driver can be forced to match a device that doesn't\nmatch its list of device IDs because of device_match_driver_override(),\nplatform drivers that rely on the existence of a device's ACPI companion\nobject should verify its presence.\n\nAccordingly, add requisite ACPI_COMPANION() or ACPI_HANDLE() checks\nagainst NULL to 13 platform drivers handling core ACPI devices.\n\nAlso change the value returned by the ACPI thermal zone driver when\nthe device's ACPI companion is not present to -ENODEV for consistency\nwith the other drivers."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
