            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80643",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: EDAC/igen6: Fix call trace due to missing release()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nEDAC/igen6: Fix call trace due to missing release()\n\nWhen unloading the igen6_edac driver, there is a call trace:\n\n  Device '(null)' does not have a release() function, it is broken and must be fixed.\n  See Documentation/core-api/kobject.rst.\n  WARNING: drivers/base/core.c:2567 at device_release+0x84/0x90, CPU#5: rmmod/127209\n  ...\n  RIP: 0010:device_release+0x84/0x90\n  Call Trace:\n   \u003cTASK\u003e\n   kobject_put+0x8c/0x220\n   put_device+0x17/0x30\n   igen6_unregister_mcis+0xa2/0xe0 [igen6_edac]\n   igen6_remove+0x82/0xb0 [igen6_edac]\n   ...\n\nFix the call trace by providing empty release() functions for the\nmemory controller devices."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80643",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80643\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80643](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80643)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nEDAC/igen6: Fix call trace due to missing release()\n\nWhen unloading the igen6_edac driver, there is a call trace:\n\n  Device '(null)' does not have a release() function, it is broken and must be fixed.\n  See Documentation/core-api/kobject.rst.\n  WARNING: drivers/base/core.c:2567 at device_release+0x84/0x90, CPU#5: rmmod/127209\n  ...\n  RIP: 0010:device_release+0x84/0x90\n  Call Trace:\n   \u003cTASK\u003e\n   kobject_put+0x8c/0x220\n   put_device+0x17/0x30\n   igen6_unregister_mcis+0xa2/0xe0 [igen6_edac]\n   igen6_remove+0x82/0xb0 [igen6_edac]\n   ...\n\nFix the call trace by providing empty release() functions for the\nmemory controller devices.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80643**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80643](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80643)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nEDAC/igen6: Fix call trace due to missing release()\n\nWhen unloading the igen6_edac driver, there is a call trace:\n\n  Device '(null)' does not have a release() function, it is broken and must be fixed.\n  See Documentation/core-api/kobject.rst.\n  WARNING: drivers/base/core.c:2567 at device_release+0x84/0x90, CPU#5: rmmod/127209\n  ...\n  RIP: 0010:device_release+0x84/0x90\n  Call Trace:\n   \u003cTASK\u003e\n   kobject_put+0x8c/0x220\n   put_device+0x17/0x30\n   igen6_unregister_mcis+0xa2/0xe0 [igen6_edac]\n   igen6_remove+0x82/0xb0 [igen6_edac]\n   ...\n\nFix the call trace by providing empty release() functions for the\nmemory controller devices."
              },
