            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80679",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: s390/dasd: Fix potential NULL pointer dereference"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/dasd: Fix potential NULL pointer dereference\n\ndasd_release_space() checks the implementation of the is_ese()\ndiscipline function before calling it to determine if a given device is\nan ESE DASD.\n\nThe current usage of the logical AND operator will lead to a NULL\npointer dereference as the function is called even if the function\npointer is NULL.\n\nFix this by using the logical OR operator."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80679",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80679\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80679](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80679)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/dasd: Fix potential NULL pointer dereference\n\ndasd_release_space() checks the implementation of the is_ese()\ndiscipline function before calling it to determine if a given device is\nan ESE DASD.\n\nThe current usage of the logical AND operator will lead to a NULL\npointer dereference as the function is called even if the function\npointer is NULL.\n\nFix this by using the logical OR operator.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80679**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80679](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80679)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/dasd: Fix potential NULL pointer dereference\n\ndasd_release_space() checks the implementation of the is_ese()\ndiscipline function before calling it to determine if a given device is\nan ESE DASD.\n\nThe current usage of the logical AND operator will lead to a NULL\npointer dereference as the function is called even if the function\npointer is NULL.\n\nFix this by using the logical OR operator."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80680",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: i2c: amd-mp2: Unregister callback on adapter add failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni2c: amd-mp2: Unregister callback on adapter add failure\n\namd_mp2_register_cb() stores the platform I2C context in the MP2 PCI\ndriver's callback table before the adapter is registered. If\ni2c_add_adapter() fails, probe returns and devres frees the context,\nbut the PCI driver can still dereference the stale pointer from its IRQ\nand system-sleep callbacks.\n\nUnregister the callback before returning the adapter registration error."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80680",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80680\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80680](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80680)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni2c: amd-mp2: Unregister callback on adapter add failure\n\namd_mp2_register_cb() stores the platform I2C context in the MP2 PCI\ndriver's callback table before the adapter is registered. If\ni2c_add_adapter() fails, probe returns and devres frees the context,\nbut the PCI driver can still dereference the stale pointer from its IRQ\nand system-sleep callbacks.\n\nUnregister the callback before returning the adapter registration error.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80680**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80680](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80680)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni2c: amd-mp2: Unregister callback on adapter add failure\n\namd_mp2_register_cb() stores the platform I2C context in the MP2 PCI\ndriver's callback table before the adapter is registered. If\ni2c_add_adapter() fails, probe returns and devres frees the context,\nbut the PCI driver can still dereference the stale pointer from its IRQ\nand system-sleep callbacks.\n\nUnregister the callback before returning the adapter registration error."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80689",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: tracing/mmiotrace: Add NULL check for mmio_trace_array in logging functions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing/mmiotrace: Add NULL check for mmio_trace_array in logging functions\n\nmmio_trace_rw() and mmio_trace_mapping() retrieve mmio_trace_array into\ntr and pass it to __trace_mmiotrace_rw() and __trace_mmiotrace_map().\nIf these functions are invoked while mmio_trace_array is NULL (e.g. before\ninitialization or after disabled), accessing tr-\u003earray_buffer.buffer will\nresult in a NULL pointer dereference crash.\n\nFix this by adding an explicit NULL check for tr at the beginning of\n__trace_mmiotrace_rw() and __trace_mmiotrace_map()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80689",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80689\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-80689](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80689)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing/mmiotrace: Add NULL check for mmio_trace_array in logging functions\n\nmmio_trace_rw() and mmio_trace_mapping() retrieve mmio_trace_array into\ntr and pass it to __trace_mmiotrace_rw() and __trace_mmiotrace_map().\nIf these functions are invoked while mmio_trace_array is NULL (e.g. before\ninitialization or after disabled), accessing tr-\u003earray_buffer.buffer will\nresult in a NULL pointer dereference crash.\n\nFix this by adding an explicit NULL check for tr at the beginning of\n__trace_mmiotrace_rw() and __trace_mmiotrace_map().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80689**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-80689](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80689)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing/mmiotrace: Add NULL check for mmio_trace_array in logging functions\n\nmmio_trace_rw() and mmio_trace_mapping() retrieve mmio_trace_array into\ntr and pass it to __trace_mmiotrace_rw() and __trace_mmiotrace_map().\nIf these functions are invoked while mmio_trace_array is NULL (e.g. before\ninitialization or after disabled), accessing tr-\u003earray_buffer.buffer will\nresult in a NULL pointer dereference crash.\n\nFix this by adding an explicit NULL check for tr at the beginning of\n__trace_mmiotrace_rw() and __trace_mmiotrace_map()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
