            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89468",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: power: supply: lp8788-charger: fix use-after-free on remove"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: supply: lp8788-charger: fix use-after-free on remove\n\nlp8788_charger_remove() flushes charger_work before unregistering the\nIRQs. An IRQ thread can queue charger_work after flush_work() has\nreturned. The work can then run after devres frees pchg and dereference\nit in lp8788_charger_event().\n\nUnregister the IRQs first. free_irq() waits for any running threaded\nhandler, so no handler can queue more work afterwards. Then use\ncancel_work_sync() to cancel pending work or wait for running work to\nfinish.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89468",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89468\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89468](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89468)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: supply: lp8788-charger: fix use-after-free on remove\n\nlp8788_charger_remove() flushes charger_work before unregistering the\nIRQs. An IRQ thread can queue charger_work after flush_work() has\nreturned. The work can then run after devres frees pchg and dereference\nit in lp8788_charger_event().\n\nUnregister the IRQs first. free_irq() waits for any running threaded\nhandler, so no handler can queue more work afterwards. Then use\ncancel_work_sync() to cancel pending work or wait for running work to\nfinish.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89468**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89468](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89468)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: supply: lp8788-charger: fix use-after-free on remove\n\nlp8788_charger_remove() flushes charger_work before unregistering the\nIRQs. An IRQ thread can queue charger_work after flush_work() has\nreturned. The work can then run after devres frees pchg and dereference\nit in lp8788_charger_event().\n\nUnregister the IRQs first. free_irq() waits for any running threaded\nhandler, so no handler can queue more work afterwards. Then use\ncancel_work_sync() to cancel pending work or wait for running work to\nfinish.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
