            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-89824",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/panel-edp: fix i2c adapter leak on probe failure"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/panel-edp: fix i2c adapter leak on probe failure\n\nMake sure to drop the i2c adapter reference on probe failure (e.g.\nprobe deferral) and on driver unbind also if a devicetree redundantly\nuses the 'ddc-i2c-bus' property to point to the aux ddc bus."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89824",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-89824\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-89824](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89824)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/panel-edp: fix i2c adapter leak on probe failure\n\nMake sure to drop the i2c adapter reference on probe failure (e.g.\nprobe deferral) and on driver unbind also if a devicetree redundantly\nuses the 'ddc-i2c-bus' property to point to the aux ddc bus.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-89824**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-89824](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-89824)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/panel-edp: fix i2c adapter leak on probe failure\n\nMake sure to drop the i2c adapter reference on probe failure (e.g.\nprobe deferral) and on driver unbind also if a devicetree redundantly\nuses the 'ddc-i2c-bus' property to point to the aux ddc bus."
              },
