            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90027",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  u ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: disable cc_debounce_dwork on stop\n\ncc_debounce_dwork is queued from the set_cc() and start_toggling()\ncallbacks, which run from TCPM's kthread worker.  port_stop() returns\nbefore tcpm_unregister_port() destroys that worker.  Flushing the worker\nduring unregister may therefore run a callback which queues the delayed\nwork after port_stop() has returned.\n\nThe delayed work can then run after devres has freed pmic_typec_port.\n\nUse disable_delayed_work_sync() in port_stop() to cancel a pending\ninstance and prevent the TCPM callbacks from queueing another one.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90027",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90027\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90027](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90027)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: disable cc_debounce_dwork on stop\n\ncc_debounce_dwork is queued from the set_cc() and start_toggling()\ncallbacks, which run from TCPM's kthread worker.  port_stop() returns\nbefore tcpm_unregister_port() destroys that worker.  Flushing the worker\nduring unregister may therefore run a callback which queues the delayed\nwork after port_stop() has returned.\n\nThe delayed work can then run after devres has freed pmic_typec_port.\n\nUse disable_delayed_work_sync() in port_stop() to cancel a pending\ninstance and prevent the TCPM callbacks from queueing another one.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90027**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90027](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90027)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: disable cc_debounce_dwork on stop\n\ncc_debounce_dwork is queued from the set_cc() and start_toggling()\ncallbacks, which run from TCPM's kthread worker.  port_stop() returns\nbefore tcpm_unregister_port() destroys that worker.  Flushing the worker\nduring unregister may therefore run a callback which queues the delayed\nwork after port_stop() has returned.\n\nThe delayed work can then run after devres has freed pmic_typec_port.\n\nUse disable_delayed_work_sync() in port_stop() to cancel a pending\ninstance and prevent the TCPM callbacks from queueing another one.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
