            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90060",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ALSA: control: Don't add invalid kcontrols to LED layer"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: control: Don't add invalid kcontrols to LED layer\n\nThe kcontrol LED state layer tries to track the all associated\nkcontrol elements with naive assumptions that they are readable.\nBut one can create a write-only element that has no get callback (even\na user element can do it), and this may lead to a NULL dereference at\nthe call chain of snd_ctl_led_notify(), as found by syzkaller.\n\nFor avoiding the Oops, add a sanity check of the kcontrol's info and\nget callbacks, and just skip the invalid kcontrols before assigning\nthe kctl to the LED layer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90060",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90060\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90060](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90060)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: control: Don't add invalid kcontrols to LED layer\n\nThe kcontrol LED state layer tries to track the all associated\nkcontrol elements with naive assumptions that they are readable.\nBut one can create a write-only element that has no get callback (even\na user element can do it), and this may lead to a NULL dereference at\nthe call chain of snd_ctl_led_notify(), as found by syzkaller.\n\nFor avoiding the Oops, add a sanity check of the kcontrol's info and\nget callbacks, and just skip the invalid kcontrols before assigning\nthe kctl to the LED layer.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90060**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90060](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90060)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: control: Don't add invalid kcontrols to LED layer\n\nThe kcontrol LED state layer tries to track the all associated\nkcontrol elements with naive assumptions that they are readable.\nBut one can create a write-only element that has no get callback (even\na user element can do it), and this may lead to a NULL dereference at\nthe call chain of snd_ctl_led_notify(), as found by syzkaller.\n\nFor avoiding the Oops, add a sanity check of the kcontrol's info and\nget callbacks, and just skip the invalid kcontrols before assigning\nthe kctl to the LED layer."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
