            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-90180",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: block: mtip32xx: synchronize ioctls with device removal"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblock: mtip32xx: synchronize ioctls with device removal\n\nThe ioctl handlers only test REMOVE_PENDING before entering\nmtip_hw_ioctl(). Removal can set that bit immediately afterwards and free\ndd-\u003eport in mtip_hw_exit() while an ioctl still dereferences it. An already\nopen block device can reach the handlers while del_gendisk() is in\nprogress.\n\nSerialize both native and compat ioctls with removal. Set REMOVE_PENDING\nbefore taking the mutex so new callers fail after an in-flight ioctl has\ndrained, and hold the mutex until the port has been torn down."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90180",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-90180\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-90180](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90180)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblock: mtip32xx: synchronize ioctls with device removal\n\nThe ioctl handlers only test REMOVE_PENDING before entering\nmtip_hw_ioctl(). Removal can set that bit immediately afterwards and free\ndd-\u003eport in mtip_hw_exit() while an ioctl still dereferences it. An already\nopen block device can reach the handlers while del_gendisk() is in\nprogress.\n\nSerialize both native and compat ioctls with removal. Set REMOVE_PENDING\nbefore taking the mutex so new callers fail after an in-flight ioctl has\ndrained, and hold the mutex until the port has been torn down.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-90180**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-90180](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-90180)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblock: mtip32xx: synchronize ioctls with device removal\n\nThe ioctl handlers only test REMOVE_PENDING before entering\nmtip_hw_ioctl(). Removal can set that bit immediately afterwards and free\ndd-\u003eport in mtip_hw_exit() while an ioctl still dereferences it. An already\nopen block device can reach the handlers while del_gendisk() is in\nprogress.\n\nSerialize both native and compat ioctls with removal. Set REMOVE_PENDING\nbefore taking the mutex so new callers fail after an in-flight ioctl has\ndrained, and hold the mutex until the port has been torn down."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
