            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93062",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:  w ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: guard against division by zero in iwl_dbg_tlv_alloc_fragments\n\nMake sure we don't end-up with a num_frags = 0 situation.\nFor that, check that the required size is not 0 and put a checker on\nnum_frags as well."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93062",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-93062\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-93062](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93062)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: guard against division by zero in iwl_dbg_tlv_alloc_fragments\n\nMake sure we don't end-up with a num_frags = 0 situation.\nFor that, check that the required size is not 0 and put a checker on\nnum_frags as well.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-93062**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-93062](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-93062)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlwifi: guard against division by zero in iwl_dbg_tlv_alloc_fragments\n\nMake sure we don't end-up with a num_frags = 0 situation.\nFor that, check that the required size is not 0 and put a checker on\nnum_frags as well."
              },
              "properties": {
