            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97427",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amd/pm: bound pp_dpm_set_pp_table() memcpy"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/pm: bound pp_dpm_set_pp_table() memcpy\n\nThe powerplay path allocates hardcode_pp_table once with kmemdup(...,\nsoft_pp_table_size). memcpy(..., size) used the sysfs store count (up to\nPAGE_SIZE) with no upper bound, causing heap overflow. Reject\nwrites where size exceeds soft_pp_table_size."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97427",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97427\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97427](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97427)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/pm: bound pp_dpm_set_pp_table() memcpy\n\nThe powerplay path allocates hardcode_pp_table once with kmemdup(...,\nsoft_pp_table_size). memcpy(..., size) used the sysfs store count (up to\nPAGE_SIZE) with no upper bound, causing heap overflow. Reject\nwrites where size exceeds soft_pp_table_size.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97427**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97427](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97427)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/pm: bound pp_dpm_set_pp_table() memcpy\n\nThe powerplay path allocates hardcode_pp_table once with kmemdup(...,\nsoft_pp_table_size). memcpy(..., size) used the sysfs store count (up to\nPAGE_SIZE) with no upper bound, causing heap overflow. Reject\nwrites where size exceeds soft_pp_table_size."
              },
