            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97521",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: gfs2: fix quota init duplicate scan"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngfs2: fix quota init duplicate scan\n\ngfs2_quota_init() checks for duplicate quota_change IDs while holding\nqd_lock and the quota hash bucket bitlock. That path used\ngfs2_qd_search_bucket(), which takes a lockref reference via\nlockref_get_not_dead().\n\nOn PREEMPT_RT this may sleep, which is not allowed under the bucket\nbitlock, triggering \"sleeping function called from invalid context\".\n\nUse a no-ref bucket lookup in this path, then continue duplicate\nhandling without taking a lockref there.\n\nRefactor gfs2_qd_search_bucket() to build on top of the no-ref helper\nso lookup traversal stays in one place.\n\nThis patch fixes a bug reported by syzbot."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97521",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97521\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97521](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97521)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngfs2: fix quota init duplicate scan\n\ngfs2_quota_init() checks for duplicate quota_change IDs while holding\nqd_lock and the quota hash bucket bitlock. That path used\ngfs2_qd_search_bucket(), which takes a lockref reference via\nlockref_get_not_dead().\n\nOn PREEMPT_RT this may sleep, which is not allowed under the bucket\nbitlock, triggering \"sleeping function called from invalid context\".\n\nUse a no-ref bucket lookup in this path, then continue duplicate\nhandling without taking a lockref there.\n\nRefactor gfs2_qd_search_bucket() to build on top of the no-ref helper\nso lookup traversal stays in one place.\n\nThis patch fixes a bug reported by syzbot.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97521**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97521](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97521)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngfs2: fix quota init duplicate scan\n\ngfs2_quota_init() checks for duplicate quota_change IDs while holding\nqd_lock and the quota hash bucket bitlock. That path used\ngfs2_qd_search_bucket(), which takes a lockref reference via\nlockref_get_not_dead().\n\nOn PREEMPT_RT this may sleep, which is not allowed under the bucket\nbitlock, triggering \"sleeping function called from invalid context\".\n\nUse a no-ref bucket lookup in this path, then continue duplicate\nhandling without taking a lockref there.\n\nRefactor gfs2_qd_search_bucket() to build on top of the no-ref helper\nso lookup traversal stays in one place.\n\nThis patch fixes a bug reported by syzbot."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97531",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: scsi: qla2xxx: Skip vport under deletion in report ID acquisition"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Skip vport under deletion in report ID acquisition\n\nqla24xx_report_id_acquisition() format-1 handling walks ha-\u003evp_list under\nvport_slock, takes a vref_count on the matching vport and calls\nqla_update_host_map() to register its port id.\n\nA vport teardown via qla24xx_vport_delete() sets VPORT_DELETE, then\nqla24xx_disable_vp() removes the vport from the host_map btree and zeroes\nvha-\u003ed_id (RESET_AL_PA). The vport is only unlinked from vp_list later,\nin qla24xx_deallocate_vp_id(), which clears vp_map[idx] (RESET_VP_IDX)\nbut does not touch host_map. In the window in between, report ID\nacquisition can still find the vport on vp_list and call\nqla_update_host_map(); with d_id already zeroed it takes the\nbtree_insert32() path and re-inserts the dying vport into host_map.\nNothing cleans that entry afterwards, so once scsi_host_put() frees the\nvha a later host_map lookup dereferences freed memory.\n\nSkip a vport that has VPORT_DELETE set before taking the reference, so it\nis neither re-registered nor scheduled for DPC re-registration. This\nmirrors the existing guard in qla2x00_alert_all_vps()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97531",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-97531\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-97531](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97531)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Skip vport under deletion in report ID acquisition\n\nqla24xx_report_id_acquisition() format-1 handling walks ha-\u003evp_list under\nvport_slock, takes a vref_count on the matching vport and calls\nqla_update_host_map() to register its port id.\n\nA vport teardown via qla24xx_vport_delete() sets VPORT_DELETE, then\nqla24xx_disable_vp() removes the vport from the host_map btree and zeroes\nvha-\u003ed_id (RESET_AL_PA). The vport is only unlinked from vp_list later,\nin qla24xx_deallocate_vp_id(), which clears vp_map[idx] (RESET_VP_IDX)\nbut does not touch host_map. In the window in between, report ID\nacquisition can still find the vport on vp_list and call\nqla_update_host_map(); with d_id already zeroed it takes the\nbtree_insert32() path and re-inserts the dying vport into host_map.\nNothing cleans that entry afterwards, so once scsi_host_put() frees the\nvha a later host_map lookup dereferences freed memory.\n\nSkip a vport that has VPORT_DELETE set before taking the reference, so it\nis neither re-registered nor scheduled for DPC re-registration. This\nmirrors the existing guard in qla2x00_alert_all_vps().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-97531**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-97531](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97531)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Skip vport under deletion in report ID acquisition\n\nqla24xx_report_id_acquisition() format-1 handling walks ha-\u003evp_list under\nvport_slock, takes a vref_count on the matching vport and calls\nqla_update_host_map() to register its port id.\n\nA vport teardown via qla24xx_vport_delete() sets VPORT_DELETE, then\nqla24xx_disable_vp() removes the vport from the host_map btree and zeroes\nvha-\u003ed_id (RESET_AL_PA). The vport is only unlinked from vp_list later,\nin qla24xx_deallocate_vp_id(), which clears vp_map[idx] (RESET_VP_IDX)\nbut does not touch host_map. In the window in between, report ID\nacquisition can still find the vport on vp_list and call\nqla_update_host_map(); with d_id already zeroed it takes the\nbtree_insert32() path and re-inserts the dying vport into host_map.\nNothing cleans that entry afterwards, so once scsi_host_put() frees the\nvha a later host_map lookup dereferences freed memory.\n\nSkip a vport that has VPORT_DELETE set before taking the reference, so it\nis neither re-registered nor scheduled for DPC re-registration. This\nmirrors the existing guard in qla2x00_alert_all_vps()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
