            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98245",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: btrfs: take commit root semaphore when iterating in mark_block_group_to_copy()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: take commit root semaphore when iterating in mark_block_group_to_copy()\n\nmark_block_group_to_copy() iterates over the commit root with\nskip_locking=true. A concurrent transaction commit can swap and free\nthe commit root during iteration, causing use-after-free when\naccessing extent buffers.\n\nFix it by using path-\u003eneed_commit_sem to protect the commit root search."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98245",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98245\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98245](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98245)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: take commit root semaphore when iterating in mark_block_group_to_copy()\n\nmark_block_group_to_copy() iterates over the commit root with\nskip_locking=true. A concurrent transaction commit can swap and free\nthe commit root during iteration, causing use-after-free when\naccessing extent buffers.\n\nFix it by using path-\u003eneed_commit_sem to protect the commit root search.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98245**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98245](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98245)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: take commit root semaphore when iterating in mark_block_group_to_copy()\n\nmark_block_group_to_copy() iterates over the commit root with\nskip_locking=true. A concurrent transaction commit can swap and free\nthe commit root during iteration, causing use-after-free when\naccessing extent buffers.\n\nFix it by using path-\u003eneed_commit_sem to protect the commit root search."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
