            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98248",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: arm64: percpu: Fix LSE operations on {8,16}-bit types"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: percpu: Fix LSE operations on {8,16}-bit types\n\nThe assembly for __percpu_##name##_case_##sz() and\n__percpu_##name##_return_case_##sz() doesn't use the 'sfx' macro\nargument to form the LSE instruction. Without 'sfx', a W register\nargument will imply a 32-bit memory location, and consequently\n{8,16}-bit ops will erroneously read and write 32 bits of memory when\nthe LSE instruction is used.\n\nFix this by appending 'sfx' to 'op_lse' to LSE instruction. It is not\nnecessary (and not valid) to append 'sfx' to 'op_llsc', as 'op_llsc' is\na register-register operation which does not access memory (and does not\ntake a size suffix)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98248",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98248\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98248](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98248)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: percpu: Fix LSE operations on {8,16}-bit types\n\nThe assembly for __percpu_##name##_case_##sz() and\n__percpu_##name##_return_case_##sz() doesn't use the 'sfx' macro\nargument to form the LSE instruction. Without 'sfx', a W register\nargument will imply a 32-bit memory location, and consequently\n{8,16}-bit ops will erroneously read and write 32 bits of memory when\nthe LSE instruction is used.\n\nFix this by appending 'sfx' to 'op_lse' to LSE instruction. It is not\nnecessary (and not valid) to append 'sfx' to 'op_llsc', as 'op_llsc' is\na register-register operation which does not access memory (and does not\ntake a size suffix).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98248**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98248](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98248)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: percpu: Fix LSE operations on {8,16}-bit types\n\nThe assembly for __percpu_##name##_case_##sz() and\n__percpu_##name##_return_case_##sz() doesn't use the 'sfx' macro\nargument to form the LSE instruction. Without 'sfx', a W register\nargument will imply a 32-bit memory location, and consequently\n{8,16}-bit ops will erroneously read and write 32 bits of memory when\nthe LSE instruction is used.\n\nFix this by appending 'sfx' to 'op_lse' to LSE instruction. It is not\nnecessary (and not valid) to append 'sfx' to 'op_llsc', as 'op_llsc' is\na register-register operation which does not access memory (and does not\ntake a size suffix)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
