            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98355",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: RDMA/rtrs: guard against null kobj name"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/rtrs: guard against null kobj name\n\nIn the client, if `init_path()` errors, the callee tries to clean up\nwith `rtrs_clt_close_conns()`. However, this can lead to calling the\nevent tracing code with `clt_path-\u003ekobj-\u003ename` being `NULL` and thus\ncausing a null pointer dereference when trying to copy from it.\n\nThis just adds a guard to check that the name is not `NULL` before\ncopying from it. The server appears to have a similar pattern."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98355",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98355\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98355](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98355)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/rtrs: guard against null kobj name\n\nIn the client, if `init_path()` errors, the callee tries to clean up\nwith `rtrs_clt_close_conns()`. However, this can lead to calling the\nevent tracing code with `clt_path-\u003ekobj-\u003ename` being `NULL` and thus\ncausing a null pointer dereference when trying to copy from it.\n\nThis just adds a guard to check that the name is not `NULL` before\ncopying from it. The server appears to have a similar pattern.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98355**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98355](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98355)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/rtrs: guard against null kobj name\n\nIn the client, if `init_path()` errors, the callee tries to clean up\nwith `rtrs_clt_close_conns()`. However, this can lead to calling the\nevent tracing code with `clt_path-\u003ekobj-\u003ename` being `NULL` and thus\ncausing a null pointer dereference when trying to copy from it.\n\nThis just adds a guard to check that the name is not `NULL` before\ncopying from it. The server appears to have a similar pattern."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-98375",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: xen/netfront: drop RX packets with a short Ethernet header"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxen/netfront: drop RX packets with a short Ethernet header\n\nhandle_incoming_queue() pulls pull_to bytes into the head before\ncalling eth_type_trans().  pull_to is the length of the first RX slot,\ncapped at RX_COPY_THRESHOLD, and that length comes from the backend.\nNothing checks it against ETH_HLEN.\n\nIf the first slot is shorter than ETH_HLEN and more slots follow, the\nhead ends up shorter than an Ethernet header while skb-\u003elen is longer,\nand eth_type_trans() BUG()s in __skb_pull().  If the whole packet is\nshorter than ETH_HLEN, eth_type_trans() reads the header past the end\nof the data instead.\n\nPull at least ETH_HLEN, and drop the packet if that fails, which also\ndrops packets too short to hold an Ethernet header.  This also checks\nthe return value of the pull, which was ignored."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98375",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-98375\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-98375](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98375)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxen/netfront: drop RX packets with a short Ethernet header\n\nhandle_incoming_queue() pulls pull_to bytes into the head before\ncalling eth_type_trans().  pull_to is the length of the first RX slot,\ncapped at RX_COPY_THRESHOLD, and that length comes from the backend.\nNothing checks it against ETH_HLEN.\n\nIf the first slot is shorter than ETH_HLEN and more slots follow, the\nhead ends up shorter than an Ethernet header while skb-\u003elen is longer,\nand eth_type_trans() BUG()s in __skb_pull().  If the whole packet is\nshorter than ETH_HLEN, eth_type_trans() reads the header past the end\nof the data instead.\n\nPull at least ETH_HLEN, and drop the packet if that fails, which also\ndrops packets too short to hold an Ethernet header.  This also checks\nthe return value of the pull, which was ignored.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-98375**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|linux-libc-dev||[CVE-2026-98375](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-98375)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxen/netfront: drop RX packets with a short Ethernet header\n\nhandle_incoming_queue() pulls pull_to bytes into the head before\ncalling eth_type_trans().  pull_to is the length of the first RX slot,\ncapped at RX_COPY_THRESHOLD, and that length comes from the backend.\nNothing checks it against ETH_HLEN.\n\nIf the first slot is shorter than ETH_HLEN and more slots follow, the\nhead ends up shorter than an Ethernet header while skb-\u003elen is longer,\nand eth_type_trans() BUG()s in __skb_pull().  If the whole packet is\nshorter than ETH_HLEN, eth_type_trans() reads the header past the end\nof the data instead.\n\nPull at least ETH_HLEN, and drop the packet if that fails, which also\ndrops packets too short to hold an Ethernet header.  This also checks\nthe return value of the pull, which was ignored."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
