            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-111063",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "aiohttp: aiohttp: Information disclosure via unenforced Secure attribute on shared cookies"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "AIOHTTP is an asynchronous HTTP client/server framework for asyncio and Python. Prior to 3.14.4, the Secure attribute for a shared cookie is not enforced. An attacker can consequently cause a shared cookie marked Secure to be sent with an unencrypted request. This issue is fixed in version 3.14.4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-111063",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-111063\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: aiohttp\nFixed Version: 3.14.4\nLink: [CVE-2026-111063](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-111063)\nAIOHTTP is an asynchronous HTTP client/server framework for asyncio and Python. Prior to 3.14.4, the Secure attribute for a shared cookie is not enforced. An attacker can consequently cause a shared cookie marked Secure to be sent with an unencrypted request. This issue is fixed in version 3.14.4.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-111063**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|aiohttp|3.14.4|[CVE-2026-111063](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-111063)|\n\nAIOHTTP is an asynchronous HTTP client/server framework for asyncio and Python. Prior to 3.14.4, the Secure attribute for a shared cookie is not enforced. An attacker can consequently cause a shared cookie marked Secure to be sent with an unencrypted request. This issue is fixed in version 3.14.4."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
